stor" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add an investor</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Investors</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Add an investor</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Fill in the Legal name and the Type: Individual, or Corporation with the Person who signs for the corporation. Then the Email, the Phone and the Address (start typing and choose it).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Optional: the Amount committed, and the Yearly return offered (the investor offer&#39;s, 30% unless you change it; the investment agreement sets the one that applies).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Invite now is ticked: press <b class="gd-ui">Add and invite</b>. The record is added and the investor gets the invitation to choose a password for the investor portal. Untick it to add the record only, and invite later from the list.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-send-a-password-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Send a password link</h2><p class="gd-p">For anyone who forgot their password or let their invitation expire.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Under People who can sign in, search by name or email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On their row, press <b class="gd-ui">Send password link</b>. They get &quot;Reset your CarmaCars password&quot;, valid for 24 hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">View as (...)</b> on the same row opens their portal, read only.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/portals</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/440"><img src="/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-ee9b3e94.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="440"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.8%;top:6.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:68.2%;top:28.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:84.1%;top:28.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-view-as-see-what-someone-sees" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">View as: see what someone sees</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A red banner says &quot;Viewing as Name (email), read only.&quot; on every page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Click around their portal. Nothing can be changed: every save is refused.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Exit</b> to come back. A view also ends by itself after 30 minutes.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/620"><img src="/guides/img/admin-28-view-as-desktop-f858e38c.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="620"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:48.6%;top:4.5%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:94.4%;top:4.5%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Can&#39;t change anything in Admin? You may still be viewing as someone. Look for the red banner and press Exit.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-the-audit-log" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The audit log</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Logs</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Changes</b> tab, shows who changed what, and when.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Changes lists every change with the person, the action, the table and the record. Data access lists lookups of private data.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every View as is recorded (view_as_start), with the person viewed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Search by table, record id or value.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/audit</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/admin-29-audit-desktop-b7504100.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:22.6%;top:31.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:39%;top:46.4%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:89.6%;top:20.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-staff-and-roles" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff and roles</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Team</b> opens Staff and roles.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Invite staff here too: Role, Name, Email, Main function and Also covers, then <b class="gd-ui">Invite</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each row has <b class="gd-ui">Send password link</b>, <b class="gd-ui">View as (...)</b> and Limits (how much they may approve or refund).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">End access</b> to close their staff portal at once. <b class="gd-ui">Restore</b> undoes it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/settings/staff</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/780"><img src="/guides/img/admin-26-staff-desktop-72287d0b.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="780"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.8%;top:59%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:94.4%;top:86.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:83.3%;top:92.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-admin-access" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Admin access</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then Admin access. Who may hold the Admin role.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The list holds rent@carmacars.ca, and verify-admin@carmacars.ca, the automated test account the site&#39;s nightly checks sign in with.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Below it: everyone who holds the Admin role now. Each must be on the list; the database refuses the Admin role to any other address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Change the list only if the business&#39;s Admin address changes.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-staff-scorecards" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff scorecards</h2><p class="gd-p">See how each assistant is doing against the targets.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a staff member&#39;s row in Staff and roles, press <b class="gd-ui">Scorecard</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">By week shows each measure (for example quote sent within 5 minutes) and the result for each week.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A task meets its target when it is done by its due time. Daily checks count when done by 9:00 and 18:00.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/scorecard</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/350"><img src="/guides/img/va-sales-05-scorecard-desktop-956a5a9e.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="350"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:21.1%;top:42.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-sales-by-staff-member" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sales by staff member</h2><p class="gd-p">See each person&#39;s commissions, quotes, offers, rentals added, bookings confirmed and booked revenue.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a staff member&#39;s row in Staff and roles, press <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b>. Press <b class="gd-ui">By week</b> or <b class="gd-ui">By month</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The tiles show the current week or month. By week (or By month) lists each period: quotes created, offers sent, rentals added, bookings confirmed, conversion and booked revenue.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Follow-ups due lists their open deals with the next step. Deals lists each booking they created, added or sent an offer on, with what it counts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A deal credited to the wrong person, or marked sourced when it was not? Press <b class="gd-ui">Reassign</b> beside it, choose who, say whether they sourced the client, and write the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Commission rate</b> gives this person their own flat rate (empty: the Program settings). <b class="gd-ui">Reverse</b> beside a commission stops it, for example for a household rental found later.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Staff enter their own home address (at their first sign-in, before they sign their agreement, or in their profile). It is needed before they add a rental or earn a commission, and spots a household rental. <b class="gd-ui">Home address</b> here changes it if it is wrong.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">The whole team: <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Overview</b>, the Sales card at the bottom. Choose another month and press <b class="gd-ui">Show</b>.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Figure</th><th scope="col">How it is counted</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Credited to</td><td>Whoever created the quote or added the rental; for a website request, whoever sent its first offer. An Admin can reassign it.</td></tr><tr><td>Conversion</td><td>Of the deals credited in the period, the share confirmed so far.</td></tr><tr><td>Booked revenue</td><td>The rental charge before tax, after discounts, for bookings confirmed in the period. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-sales-staff-in-person-or-remote" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sales staff: in person or remote</h2><p class="gd-p">Each Sales person works in person (Toronto) or remote (anywhere, a contractor). Staff and roles lists them under Sales staff: in person or remote.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Work mode</b> on a person (or on their Sales page), choose In person or Remote and give the reason. A new Sales person starts in person.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The list shows the mode, the rate now, the rate the month would end at, and for remote this month&#39;s touches against 400, the peak hours scheduled this week (20 needed, Thursday to Sunday afternoons) and the replies on time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On a remote person&#39;s Sales page, Remote duties shows their checklist, touches, blocks and reply time. <b class="gd-ui">Void</b> beside a touch logged by mistake takes it off, with a reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">When you approve a Sales month, its mode, rates, touches and any drop are locked: a later change of mode or settings does not change it. Their My sales shows each month in one line.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Rule</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Rates</td><td>In person 10%, 15% from 50 rental days, 20% from 100. Remote 5 points lower on every tier: 5%, 10%, 15%</td></tr><tr><td>Credit</td><td>In person: walk-ins, handovers, partner visits and the rentals they source. Remote: only the rentals they source; a website request they answer with the first offer during their blocks is credited to them; a walk-in or a partner deal earns them nothing</td></tr><tr><td>Remote minimum</td><td>400 touches a month. Under it, when the month ends, the month&#39;s rate is one tier lower (5% becomes 2.5%). Settings &gt; Program settings, Staff commissions, changes the minimum, the drop and the floor</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-an-admin-has-every-staff-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An Admin has every staff page</h2><p class="gd-p">An Admin account is only an Admin: it already has every page of the staff portals, so no office or field role can be added to it, and the invite form and Staff and roles refuse it. To work as staff, use a separate account. An Admin can still be given a field job and opens it on the field portal.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-two-records-of-one-person" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Two records of one person</h2><p class="gd-p">When two renter records are clearly the same person (the same phone verified with a code, or the same name, date of birth and phone), the site merges them by itself within 15 minutes, into the record with more bookings. Bookings, licences, cards, payments, documents and messages move. The person can then sign in with either email or with their phone number and a code, and gets one short note: &quot;Your CarmaCars accounts are now one&quot;. A match on the name alone stays a task for you, and <b class="gd-ui">Merge into this record</b> under the renter still works as before.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the renter. The Merged records card lists each merge, automatic or by staff, with what moved and the emails that now sign in there.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Two different people after all? Press <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> and say why. Everything moved goes back and both records are as they were.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-new-staff-the-academy-then-the-agreement-then-the-portal" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">New staff: the academy, then the agreement, then the portal</h2><p class="gd-p">Every staff member (never an Admin) opens their portal in this order: their staff agreement first, then the academy, then everything else (release 48: the agreement moved before the academy; anyone who already passed the academy is only asked to sign). Until the agreement is signed they open only <b class="gd-ui">Welcome</b>, their profile, the guide and their documents to sign; after it, until the academy is passed, only the academy, the guide, their profile and Welcome.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The agreement is sent by itself to everyone without one, filled from their record and their hire&#39;s pay and start date: the Field Staff Agreement for field work, the contractor agreement for customer service, Fleet, Finance and Sales (in person or remote). One reminder goes 3 days after it was sent.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Team</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff and roles</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Staff agreements</b>: who has not signed, what the automatic send waits for (for example a field hire&#39;s licence number), and <b class="gd-ui">Waive</b> with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Welcome also asks for the name they go by (the preferred name, shown across the portals and on the staff list), and, once the agreement and the academy are done, shows the team&#39;s WhatsApp group (Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">WhatsApp team group link</b> and <b class="gd-ui">WhatsApp Sales group link</b>; empty until you set them: while either is empty, Hiring warns and To do keeps an urgent task. Reset the invite link in WhatsApp, keep Add other members for admins only and Approve new participants on, then paste it). Each group shows the person&#39;s member tag (&quot;Name - Position&quot;) with Copy and the steps; I joined needs <b class="gd-ui">I set my member tag</b>. The same link goes by email, once.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-accounts-locked-for-inactivity" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Accounts locked for inactivity</h2><p class="gd-p">A staff account with no sign-in or use for 10 days (Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">Staff inactive lock days</b>) is locked; the person is warned by email on day 7 and sees &quot;Account locked for inactivity&quot; when they sign in. You get an alert. On <b class="gd-ui">Team</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff and roles</b> the row says <b class="gd-ui">Locked for inactivity</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Unlock</b>. The staff list shows each person&#39;s last sign-in. Admin accounts are never locked.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-hours-and-the-townhall" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Hours and the townhall</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Team</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Timesheet</b>: the hours customer service, Fleet and Finance clocked (Clock in and out on their home page). Add hours someone forgot, or void a wrong entry, with the reason. A person not clocked in 15 minutes after their start time (customer service 9:00, Fleet 11:00, Toronto) is reminded.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Breaks and idle time (release 35).</b> Customer service, Fleet and Finance press <b class="gd-ui">Start break</b> and <b class="gd-ui">End break</b> next to the clock; breaks have no fixed length. On <b class="gd-ui">Timesheet</b>, each person&#39;s days show the hours clocked and worked, their breaks (how many, the total and the longest) and their idle time, with every break and idle stretch listed. <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> a break with the reason (in the audit log). Finance sees the breaks but never the idle time. A break open past 30 minutes reminds the person and you. Whether breaks are paid is <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; va_breaks_paid (on: salaried; off: breaks come off the hours on the payroll, where each line shows the period&#39;s breaks).</p><p class="gd-p">While someone is clocked in, not on a break and within their scheduled hours, the portal notes the fact of their activity (never keys, pages or screens), at most once a minute; their actions count too. With no activity for more than va_idle_alert_minutes (10), you get one alert, &quot;Name (role) inactive since 10:42, 12 min&quot;, and one more at va_idle_followup_minutes (30). A call they are on (their Quo user, set with <b class="gd-ui">Set Quo user</b> on Timesheet; the <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> button; a note in the caller pop-up) and the townhall (joined or present, to its end plus 10 minutes) pause it. <b class="gd-ui">KPIs</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Idle minutes</b> against kpi_idle_minutes_week.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Team</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Townhall</b>: the weekly staff call (Wednesdays at 6:30 pm Toronto). The deck builds itself every Sunday night from the week&#39;s data: the week, platform updates, fleet, staff, sales with the leaderboard, finances and claims (the last two for Admins only). Add a note to any slide; <b class="gd-ui">Build again</b> refreshes the numbers. With no call link in Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> opens the call in the site; staff add the call to their calendar from the page.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-the-townhall-day-attendance-and-the-team-slide-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The townhall day, attendance and the team slide (release 35)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The townhall is every Wednesday at 6:30 pm Toronto time. To change it, press <b class="gd-ui">Change the day or time</b> on the Townhall page. Beside it, a table shows the website&#39;s visitor sessions of the last 8 weeks for each day, as information. Field applicants&#39; live calls always take the hour before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every staff member is invited and reminded an hour before. <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> on the townhall page, or <b class="gd-ui">Check in</b> from 15 minutes before, counts them as there.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When the call ends, the people who missed it are recorded, the staff list shows &quot;Missed N townhalls&quot; for the last 8 weeks, and you get an alert with the names.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The deck&#39;s last slide is the team: a tile per person with their role&#39;s numbers for the week. Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a shout-out</b> on a tile to add yours.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-where-staff-live-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Where staff live (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Welcome asks every hire for their city and country. In the Toronto area Sales keep the mode they were hired in; elsewhere Sales is remote. The staff list shows the location.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-staff-onboarding-breaks-and-shifts-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff onboarding, breaks and shifts (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>New staff open their portal after four steps in order: the staff agreement, the academy, confirming the team&#39;s WhatsApp groups, then an Admin&#39;s or a Fleet team member&#39;s approval (or a rejection with a reason the person sees). Everyone already working waits for the same approval once.</li><li>Each person&#39;s row on the Staff onboarding card in Settings and on the Fleet approvals list says exactly what is missing, for example &quot;Waiting on: Academy (3 of 11 sections), Staff agreement signature&quot;. <b class="gd-ui">Mark WhatsApp joined</b> records only the WhatsApp groups, at any step: it never passes the academy or signs the agreement, and it counts when the person reaches that step. Once the agreement and the academy are done, <b class="gd-ui">Confirm WhatsApp and approve</b> marks the groups and approves in one press (Admins only, recorded in the audit log).</li><li>Schedules: customer service, Fleet and Finance have a schedule per role, and an Admin can give one person their own. Today&#39;s duty board shows who is working, late or absent.</li><li>Breaks: office staff log a break from their home page, and the time on break is kept on their timesheet. While someone is on a break, on a call or in the townhall, the idle alert is paused; otherwise a person with no activity for a while on a shift gets an alert, then the Admins do.</li><li>Quiet hours: staff alerts held by a person&#39;s quiet hours arrive as one summary when they end, and no text goes to a renter at night (an answer asked for then arrives in the morning).</li><li>Field staff set their availability (mornings, afternoons and evenings for each weekday) on Welcome and later on My shifts or Profile; Fleet and Admin see it on the shift board.</li><li>Standing weekly shifts are claimed by themselves up to two weeks ahead; the minimum shifts a week is a Program setting (2 in 7 days), and anyone under it gets a reminder and a To do.</li><li>Shifts are published by themselves every hour from the shift template in Program settings (Field jobs and handovers: one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day, up to 14 days ahead, only forward from the latest shift already published and never before the start date set there). A handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own, 90 minutes either side.</li><li>A published shift nobody has claimed 48 hours before it starts alerts Fleet and the Admins with the people to ask.</li><li>Payroll runs every two weeks: Finance prepares it, an Admin approves it and records the payments. KPIs per role are on Team, KPIs, each against a target in Program settings.</li><li>The townhall is every Wednesday at 6:30 pm Toronto time; two missed in a row lock the account until an Admin restores it. A townhall that did not happen (nobody attended, cancelled ahead, or marked by an Admin) counts nobody absent.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-work-chats-only" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Work chats only</h2><p class="gd-p">All staff work communication happens in the group work chats (the CarmaCars Team and Sales WhatsApp groups, and the chats in the portal), never in private messages. It is in every staff guide and in the academy (Work chats). Answer a private work message in the group.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-staff-rewards-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff rewards (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Team</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff rewards</b> lists every staff member: whether they get rental perks and why not, their tier, their progress, their free days and what they used.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Rental perks are for in-person staff in Canada. Remote and international staff get none. Use <b class="gd-ui">Perks</b> to switch one person on or off by hand, with the reason they read.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">From day one (the academy and the agreement done): 15% off their own rentals. Sales earn 1 free day per 100 rental days booked, Field 1 per 100 handovers. Silver at 50 rental days booked in a month is 20% off; Gold at 100 is 25% off and 1 bonus free day. The month&#39;s top seller gets a free weekend.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A perk rental is picked up within 48 hours of booking and never on dates a renter asked for, never on exotic or partner cars, and the staff member must be the driver. A free day ends after 6 months. A suspended account&#39;s perks are frozen.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Free days go on CarmaCars&#39; and shareholders&#39; cars first. On a co-host owner&#39;s car the owner is paid as at the full rate. Each perk used is posted as a staff benefit expense (account 5300).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add free days</b> gives a person free days by hand, with the reason. Every number is in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff rewards</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-data-to-check-on-each-record-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Data to check on each record (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every portal checks the person&#39;s own record and shows them a box with the fix: Settings &gt; Staff, Owners and Renters (renters with a booking in the last 90 days) list everyone with something open, in words. <b class="gd-ui">Send reminder</b> sends a staff member an alert; an owner or a renter sees the box again at their next page, even a warning they put off. A blocking item (the staff agreement waiting for the licence number or the home address, an expired licence of someone who drives) cannot be put off. In-person staff with a home address outside Ontario are asked to confirm it with the reason; what they wrote is kept.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-updated-agreements-to-accept-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Updated agreements to accept (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">When a document changes (the terms of use, the privacy policy, the rental agreement, the owner program agreement, the staff agreements), everyone it binds sees one box at their next sign-in: what changed in a few lines, the new text, and <b class="gd-ui">Accept and continue</b>. Accepting is recorded with the version, the time, the IP address and the device; nobody signs again. Declining keeps their portal closed and shows how to reach us. Admin settings, Terms, lists each version with how many accepted, declined or still wait, and who.</p><p class="gd-p">Release 48 published three: the rental agreement (the new return charges), the owner program agreement (owner use for someone else, the $150 Install Fee) and the staff agreements (confidentiality, non-solicitation for 12 months, data returned or deleted on exit, and a non-compete for contractors only: none for employees, as Ontario&#39;s Employment Standards Act requires).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-people-on-the-live-map" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">People on the live map</h2><p class="gd-p">The live map (Visitors, and Cars &gt; Fleet tracking) has a <b class="gd-ui">People</b> layer: staff on shift or on a job, and renters and owners at a pickup or return, each with a marker by role. Use the role chips to show or hide each group. Staff appear only after they accept the electronic monitoring policy, and never off duty; renters and owners only with their phone&#39;s permission and only two hours either side of a pickup or return. Only the latest position is kept, plus a job&#39;s points for 30 days. Admins and Fleet see everyone; customer service and Sales see renters at a pickup or return; Finance and field staff see no one.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-resignations-release-50" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Resignations (release 50)</h2><p class="gd-p">Staff resign themselves on their <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b> (<b class="gd-ui">Resign</b>, the last section; on <b class="gd-ui">Welcome</b> while still in onboarding). You get an email and an alert, Finance too, and an Offboarding To do opens in the Admin queue.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff and roles</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Resigning: last day</b> with the day notice was given, the reason and the <b class="gd-ui">Offboarding To do</b> link. After the last day it shows Resigned, with the dates.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The To do lists what to do: final pay up to the last day (Finance), the keys, cards and equipment to collect (not tracked in the system), their open field jobs and shifts to reassign, and the leads, chats, To dos and claims to hand back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Their field jobs and shifts after the last day go back to the queue at once; nobody can give them a shift or a job after it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Change last day</b> moves it earlier or later (from today); they are emailed the new day and the To do follows. <b class="gd-ui">Withdraw resignation</b> cancels it for them. <b class="gd-ui">End access now</b> ends it at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">After the last day their access ends by itself (the same as <b class="gd-ui">End access</b>), their open To dos and chats go back to the queues and their claims are released. <b class="gd-ui">Restore</b> gives access back if they return.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Someone who resigned by email or in person: <b class="gd-ui">Record a resignation</b> on their row, with the last day and the reason as they gave it. Today ends their access now.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">The connector&#39;s <span class="gd-url">list_staff</span> shows each person&#39;s resignation.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-managers-and-their-teams-release-51" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Managers and their teams (release 51)</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Team</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff and roles</b>. The <b class="gd-ui">Manager</b> column shows each person&#39;s manager, or the size of a manager&#39;s team.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Make manager</b> on the person who manages.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On each staff member, press <b class="gd-ui">Assign to a manager</b>, choose the manager and press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>. Both are told.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Not a manager</b> ends it: their team is unassigned and told.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">A manager opens <b class="gd-ui">My team</b> in their portal and in the app (Profile, <b class="gd-ui">My team</b>): each member&#39;s hours in the last 7 days, academy progress, pay owed, field jobs and when they were last on; one member&#39;s KPIs, jobs, hours and last 20 actions. It is read only, with no pay details, addresses or customer numbers. Nobody manages themself, and a team never loops back.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'insurance-replacements-rates-and-billing', 'chapter', 'partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand', 'Each insurance company pays an agreed rate a day for a replacement car, by car class. The rate sheet keeps those rates with their history; a rental billed to an insurer takes its rate from it, the insurer''s invoice follows it, and each insurer''s page shows what it was billed, paid and still owes.

## The rate sheet

Open **Money** > **Insurers** (the **Rates** tab).

1. One row for each insurer, one column for each car class (the list in Settings > Vehicle classes). Each cell shows the rate today and, under it, a rate already saved for a later date. On a phone each insurer is a card with its classes.
2. Press **Set** (or **Change**) in a cell. Type the Daily rate and, when the insurer has them, a weekly cap, a cap for 30 days, a delivery and pickup allowance, the kilometres a day and a taxes note (printed on its invoices). Choose From, say why it changed, and press **Save the rate**.
3. A change never overwrites the rate before it: it is a new rate from its date, and the earlier one stays in the history. **End** stops a rate from a date.
4. Add an insurer, or change its billing contact and email, in Settings > Insurers.

> Good to know: A car takes the rate of its pricing class; when the insurer has no rate for that class, the rate of the car''s other classes, in the order of the list. A 2024 Jetta (standard, also a sedan) replaced for an insurer that pays $65 a day for sedans is billed $65 a day.

## The rate on a rental

- Add a rental, Insurance replacement (or Insurer billed later): once the price is checked and the insurer chosen, the daily rate authorized is filled from its rate sheet for the car, with the caps and the taxes note under it.
- A different rate: type it, and Differs from the rate sheet asks for the reason. The rental is not added without it. Empty the field to take the sheet''s rate again.
- The review screen of a request or an offer does the same when you choose Bill to and the insurer: the rate follows the insurer chosen, and a rate typed that differs needs the reason.
- An insurer with no rate for the car: type the rate the adjuster authorized, as before.
- The booking''s Insurance replacement card (Overview and Money tabs) shows the insurer and the claim, the daily rate and where it comes from, Differs with the reason when it is not the sheet''s, the caps, the days covered, what the insurer pays and its invoices.

## Charges to the insurer

VLF (vehicle licence fee), LDW, T&LDW, PAP/PEC and Waiver Saver are charged to the insurer, a rate a day each, only on a rental billed to an insurer. They have no set price: type the rate the insurer authorized on each booking.

1. Add a rental, Insurer billed later (or the Insurance replacement quick start): under the insurer''s details, **Charges to the insurer** has a box for each, the rate a day before HST. Under each box the amount for the days shows; the check of the price adds each line with its HST. Leave a box empty for none.
2. A request or an offer: on the review screen, once Bill to is an insurer, the same boxes are under the insurer''s details. Save, Send offer or the updated offer keeps them; Bill to back to Renter removes them in the same save.
3. A confirmed booking: the Insurance replacement card lists each charge with its rate a day, the days and the amount. **Change the charges** (or **Add a charge**), type the rates, and press **Save the charges**. Each change is in the booking''s history and the changes to the fees.
4. Each line is the rate times the rental days, plus HST: when the dates change, the amount follows. The insurer pays them whether it pays everything or the rental only.

> Good to know: They never show for a rental the renter pays, and the database refuses them there. They print on both agreements: on Blind Spot''s, VLF in box 43, LDW in 45, T&LDW in 46, PAP/PEC in 47 (each with its rate a day and amount) and Waiver Saver in its box beside Accepted; a box with no charge says N/A.

## Insurance replacements: one list

**Money** > **Insurers** > **Replacements** lists every rental an insurer pays for: the claim, the insurer and adjuster, the renter, the car, the dates and days, where it stands (Upcoming, On rent, Returned, Invoiced, Negotiating, Approved, Paid, Written off), the invoice and how many versions were sent, what was billed, approved and paid, and the aging. Search by claim, booking, renter, insurer, adjuster or plate; the tiles open what is still to invoice and what is over 30 or 60 days. Finance and customer service have the same page in the staff portal.

## Add one in a minute

1. Press **Add an insurance replacement**. Only the renter''s name, the insurer, the claim number and the dates are needed; the phone and the email are optional.
2. To fill it from an email, paste the adjuster''s email or the claim notice in **Paste text** and press **Read it**. Check what was found, then press **Use these**.
3. The car: a car of the fleet, or **Not in the fleet (type it)** with its year, make, model and plate. A car typed in never shows in the fleet, on the calendars or to an owner.
4. **Off the calendar and owner notices** is always on for a car typed in, and a choice for a fleet car. It can be switched later on the rental (**Take off the calendar**, **Put on the calendar**).
5. Press **Add the rental**. The form saves as a draft while you type: an unfinished one waits in Unfinished rentals, and a discarded one comes back with **Restore it**.

## Invoices, estimates and versions

- On the rental''s page every field of the invoice can be changed: each line with its days and rate, the fees (**Add the winter tire fee**), the HST, the notes, the dates, who it is billed to and the email it goes to. **Start from the booking''s figures** fills the lines from the booking again (after an extension or a new end of rental).
- **Send as an estimate** sends a version that bills nothing. **Send the invoice** sends the version the insurer owes from then on. Send again as often as needed: each send is a version, kept as sent, with its PDF and what changed from the one before. **Record as sent (no email)** keeps a version sent another way.
- **Extend** moves the return when the insurer authorizes more days; the renter''s card is never charged, and the invoice''s next version takes the new figures.
- Changes saved after an invoice was sent wait as the next version: the insurer still owes the last version sent until the new one is sent.

## Getting paid

- **Record a payment**: the amount, how (cheque, e-Transfer, direct deposit), the reference and the day. Part payments are fine.
- **Approved amount**: what the adjuster approved. **Negotiating** records what the adjuster disputes.
- **Write off the rest** writes off what is left unpaid, with the reason.
- Finance and the Admins get a reminder 30 days after an invoice is sent, then every week while it is unpaid.

> Tip: The connector (Claude) does all of it with the same checks: `list_insurer_rentals`, `get_insurer_rental`, `insurer_rental_create`, `insurer_rental_update`, `insurer_rental_extend`, `insurer_invoice_edit`, `insurer_invoice_send` and `insurer_money`, each change previewed, then confirmed. The key''s person must be an Admin, Finance or customer service, and the key needs the Act as the Admin scope.

## Billing history

**Money** > **Insurers**, then the insurer''s name.

1. The tiles: bookings, days used and authorized, billed, paid, outstanding, the average daily rate and the days the insurer takes to pay (from sent to paid).
2. Rates by class (Set, Change and End work here too), then the History of the rates: each rate with its dates, its status, why it changed and who saved it.
3. Billing by class: for each class the bookings, days authorized and used, billed, paid, outstanding, the average rate and the days to pay.
4. Bookings: each booking with its class, claim, dates, days, rate (Sheet and the reason when it differs), what was billed, paid and outstanding, and its invoices (each opens its PDF).
5. Choose Picked up from and to and press **Show** for a period. **Download CSV** saves the bookings of the period for a spreadsheet.

## Emails as Blind Spot Car Rental

Insurance emails go from **Blind Spot Car Rental <blindspotcarrental@carmacars.ca>** and replies come back to that address: the insurer invoice, **Email the adjuster**, and Email the renter when you choose Blind Spot Car Rental as the sender on a booking an insurer pays. Every other email still goes from CarmaCars.

> Good to know: The address sends today. To receive the replies, the mailbox (or an alias of rent@carmacars.ca in Google Workspace) must exist.

### VLF (vehicle licensing fee)
A default VLF a day can be set in **Settings** (Insurer-billed rentals: VLF a day; $0 means none). When a rental is first billed to an insurer, that VLF is put on it as one of its charges to the insurer; change the rate or remove it there, like the others. Before the renter pays again, remove the charges to the insurer.

### Adjusters
Each insurer has its adjusters, and an invoice goes to the booking''s adjuster (else the insurer''s billing email, which is now optional).

1. On a booking, in **Insurance claim and adjuster**, press **Edit**. Choose the insurer, or **Not listed: add it** and type its name.
2. Choose a saved **Adjuster** of that insurer, or **Add the adjuster** and type the name, phone and email. A new adjuster is saved with the insurer for the next booking.
3. On **Add a rental**, **Saved adjuster** fills the adjuster''s fields; a new one typed is saved the same way (matched by email, else by name).
4. On **Insurers**, open an insurer: Adjusters lists them (**Add an adjuster**, **Change**).

### What was billed
**Insurers** shows **Billed by insurer and class**: bookings, days, the average daily rate, the rental, the charges (VLF, LDW and the others), HST and the insurer''s total. Open an insurer for **Charged by class**, **Billing by car** and **Billing by adjuster**, and each booking with its car, adjuster and charges.


## Winter tire fee on a rental

Open the booking. The **Winter tire fee** card sets this rental''s rate a day (0 removes the tires) and, if needed, a cap for the rental, with the reason.

1. It works on a rental the renter pays and on an insurer-billed rental (the tires are then one of the charges on the insurer''s invoice).
2. The change is kept in the booking''s history with who made it and why, and the total is worked out again. The renter of a rental they pay gets an email.', 'Insurance replacements: rates and billing', 'The rate sheet by insurer and car class, the rate on a rental, the invoices and the billing history.',
