5. Choose Picked up from and to and press **Show** for a period. **Download CSV** saves the bookings of the period for a spreadsheet.

## Emails as Blind Spot Car Rental

Insurance emails go from **Blind Spot Car Rental <blindspotcarrental@carmacars.ca>** and replies come back to that address: the insurer invoice, **Email the adjuster**, and Email the renter when you choose Blind Spot Car Rental as the sender on a booking an insurer pays. Every other email still goes from CarmaCars.

> Good to know: The address sends today. To receive the replies, the mailbox (or an alias of rent@carmacars.ca in Google Workspace) must exist.

### VLF (vehicle licensing fee)
A default VLF a day can be set in **Settings** (Insurer-billed rentals: VLF a day; $0 means none). When a rental is first billed to an insurer, that VLF is put on it as one of its charges to the insurer; change the rate or remove it there, like the others. Before the renter pays again, remove the charges to the insurer.

### Adjusters
Each insurer has its adjusters, and an invoice goes to the booking''s adjuster (else the insurer''s billing email, which is now optional).

1. On a booking, in **Insurance claim and adjuster**, press **Edit**. Choose the insurer, or **Not listed: add it** and type its name.
2. Choose a saved **Adjuster** of that insurer, or **Add the adjuster** and type the name, phone and email. A new adjuster is saved with the insurer for the next booking.
3. On **Add a rental**, **Saved adjuster** fills the adjuster''s fields; a new one typed is saved the same way (matched by email, else by name).
4. On **Insurers**, open an insurer: Adjusters lists them (**Add an adjuster**, **Change**).

### What was billed
**Insurers** shows **Billed by insurer and class**: bookings, days, the average daily rate, the rental, the charges (VLF, LDW and the others), HST and the insurer''s total. Open an insurer for **Charged by class**, **Billing by car** and **Billing by adjuster**, and each booking with its car, adjuster and charges.


## Winter tire fee on a rental

Open the booking. The **Winter tire fee** card sets this rental''s rate a day (0 removes the tires) and, if needed, a cap for the rental, with the reason.

1. It works on a rental the renter pays and on an insurer-billed rental (the tires are then one of the charges on the insurer''s invoice).
2. The change is kept in the booking''s history with who made it and why, and the total is worked out again. The renter of a rental they pay gets an email.

## When an insurer''s mail server refuses our email (release 51)

Some insurers'' mailboxes accept only senders on their list. Their server then sends back a bounce email. The site reads it, marks that version **bounced** under **Versions sent** with the reason, and writes it in the claim history.

1. If the insurer has a general claims email (Settings, Insurers), the same invoice or estimate goes again there at once, one time.
2. Admin gets one urgent To do, "Insurer email bounced", with the reason, the adjuster, the insurer''s claims contact and an allowlist request ready to copy. Send it from the Blind Spot email, or call the adjuster.
3. Each version shows how each email went: queued, sent, delivered (no bounce in 24 hours), bounced or failed.

> Good to know: A refusal like this is the insurer''s setting, not ours: the email passed every check on our side. It stops once they add our sender address to their list.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Each insurance company pays an agreed rate a day for a replacement car, by car class. The rate sheet keeps those rates with their history; a rental billed to an insurer takes its rate from it, the insurer&#39;s invoice follows it, and each insurer&#39;s page shows what it was billed, paid and still owes.</p><section class="gd-task" id="insurance-replacements-rates-and-billing-the-rate-sheet" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The rate sheet</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Insurers</b> (the <b class="gd-ui">Rates</b> tab).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">One row for each insurer, one column for each car class (the list in Settings &gt; Vehicle classes). Each cell shows the rate today and, under it, a rate already saved for a later date. On a phone each insurer is a card with its classes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Set</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Change</b>) in a cell. Type the Daily rate and, when the insurer has them, a weekly cap, a cap for 30 days, a delivery and pickup allowance, the kilometres a day and a taxes note (printed on its invoices). Choose From, say why it changed, and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the rate</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A change never overwrites the rate before it: it is a new rate from its date, and the earlier one stays in the history. <b class="gd-ui">End</b> stops a rate from a date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add an insurer, or change its billing contact and email, in Settings &gt; Insurers.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A car takes the rate of its pricing class; when the insurer has no rate for that class, the rate of the car&#39;s other classes, in the order of the list. A 2024 Jetta (standard, also a sedan) replaced for an insurer that pays $65 a day for sedans is billed $65 a day.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="insurance-replacements-rates-and-billing-the-rate-on-a-rental" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The rate on a rental</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Add a rental, Insurance replacement (or Insurer billed later): once the price is checked and the insurer chosen, the daily rate authorized is filled from its rate sheet for the car, with the caps and the taxes note under it.</li><li>A different rate: type it, and Differs from the rate sheet asks for the reason. The rental is not added without it. Empty the field to take the sheet&#39;s rate again.</li><li>The review screen of a request or an offer does the same when you choose Bill to and the insurer: the rate follows the insurer chosen, and a rate typed that differs needs the reason.</li><li>An insurer with no rate for the car: type the rate the adjuster authorized, as before.</li><li>The booking&#39;s Insurance replacement card (Overview and Money tabs) shows the insurer and the claim, the daily rate and where it comes from, Differs with the reason when it is not the sheet&#39;s, the caps, the days covered, what the insurer pays and its invoices.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="insurance-replacements-rates-and-billing-charges-to-the-insurer" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Charges to the insurer</h2><p class="gd-p">VLF (vehicle licence fee), LDW, T&amp;LDW, PAP/PEC and Waiver Saver are charged to the insurer, a rate a day each, only on a rental billed to an insurer. They have no set price: type the rate the insurer authorized on each booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Add a rental, Insurer billed later (or the Insurance replacement quick start): under the insurer&#39;s details, <b class="gd-ui">Charges to the insurer</b> has a box for each, the rate a day before HST. Under each box the amount for the days shows; the check of the price adds each line with its HST. Leave a box empty for none.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A request or an offer: on the review screen, once Bill to is an insurer, the same boxes are under the insurer&#39;s details. Save, Send offer or the updated offer keeps them; Bill to back to Renter removes them in the same save.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A confirmed booking: the Insurance replacement card lists each charge with its rate a day, the days and the amount. <b class="gd-ui">Change the charges</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Add a charge</b>), type the rates, and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the charges</b>. Each change is in the booking&#39;s history and the changes to the fees.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Each line is the rate times the rental days, plus HST: when the dates change, the amount follows. The insurer pays them whether it pays everything or the rental only.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>They never show for a rental the renter pays, and the database refuses them there. They print on both agreements: on Blind Spot&#39;s, VLF in box 43, LDW in 45, T&amp;LDW in 46, PAP/PEC in 47 (each with its rate a day and amount) and Waiver Saver in its box beside Accepted; a box with no charge says N/A.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="insurance-replacements-rates-and-billing-insurance-replacements-one-list" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Insurance replacements: one list</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Insurers</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Replacements</b> lists every rental an insurer pays for: the claim, the insurer and adjuster, the renter, the car, the dates and days, where it stands (Upcoming, On rent, Returned, Invoiced, Negotiating, Approved, Paid, Written off), the invoice and how many versions were sent, what was billed, approved and paid, and the aging. Search by claim, booking, renter, insurer, adjuster or plate; the tiles open what is still to invoice and what is over 30 or 60 days. Finance and customer service have the same page in the staff portal.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="insurance-replacements-rates-and-billing-add-one-in-a-minute" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add one in a minute</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add an insurance replacement</b>. Only the renter&#39;s name, the insurer, the claim number and the dates are needed; the phone and the email are optional.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">To fill it from an email, paste the adjuster&#39;s email or the claim notice in <b class="gd-ui">Paste text</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Read it</b>. Check what was found, then press <b class="gd-ui">Use these</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The car: a car of the fleet, or <b class="gd-ui">Not in the fleet (type it)</b> with its year, make, model and plate. A car typed in never shows in the fleet, on the calendars or to an owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Off the calendar and owner notices</b> is always on for a car typed in, and a choice for a fleet car. It can be switched later on the rental (<b class="gd-ui">Take off the calendar</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Put on the calendar</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add the rental</b>. The form saves as a draft while you type: an unfinished one waits in Unfinished rentals, and a discarded one comes back with <b class="gd-ui">Restore it</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="insurance-replacements-rates-and-billing-invoices-estimates-and-versions" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Invoices, estimates and versions</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>On the rental&#39;s page every field of the invoice can be changed: each line with its days and rate, the fees (<b class="gd-ui">Add the winter tire fee</b>), the HST, the notes, the dates, who it is billed to and the email it goes to. <b class="gd-ui">Start from the booking&#39;s figures</b> fills the lines from the booking again (after an extension or a new end of rental).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Send as an estimate</b> sends a version that bills nothing. <b class="gd-ui">Send the invoice</b> sends the version the insurer owes from then on. Send again as often as needed: each send is a version, kept as sent, with its PDF and what changed from the one before. <b class="gd-ui">Record as sent (no email)</b> keeps a version sent another way.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Extend</b> moves the return when the insurer authorizes more days; the renter&#39;s card is never charged, and the invoice&#39;s next version takes the new figures.</li><li>Changes saved after an invoice was sent wait as the next version: the insurer still owes the last version sent until the new one is sent.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="insurance-replacements-rates-and-billing-getting-paid" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Getting paid</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Record a payment</b>: the amount, how (cheque, e-Transfer, direct deposit), the reference and the day. Part payments are fine.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Approved amount</b>: what the adjuster approved. <b class="gd-ui">Negotiating</b> records what the adjuster disputes.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Write off the rest</b> writes off what is left unpaid, with the reason.</li><li>Finance and the Admins get a reminder 30 days after an invoice is sent, then every week while it is unpaid.</li></ul><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The connector (Claude) does all of it with the same checks: <span class="gd-url">list_insurer_rentals</span>, <span class="gd-url">get_insurer_rental</span>, <span class="gd-url">insurer_rental_create</span>, <span class="gd-url">insurer_rental_update</span>, <span class="gd-url">insurer_rental_extend</span>, <span class="gd-url">insurer_invoice_edit</span>, <span class="gd-url">insurer_invoice_send</span> and <span class="gd-url">insurer_money</span>, each change previewed, then confirmed. The key&#39;s person must be an Admin, Finance or customer service, and the key needs the Act as the Admin scope.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="insurance-replacements-rates-and-billing-billing-history" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Billing history</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Insurers</b>, then the insurer&#39;s name.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The tiles: bookings, days used and authorized, billed, paid, outstanding, the average daily rate and the days the insurer takes to pay (from sent to paid).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Rates by class (Set, Change and End work here too), then the History of the rates: each rate with its dates, its status, why it changed and who saved it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Billing by class: for each class the bookings, days authorized and used, billed, paid, outstanding, the average rate and the days to pay.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Bookings: each booking with its class, claim, dates, days, rate (Sheet and the reason when it differs), what was billed, paid and outstanding, and its invoices (each opens its PDF).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Choose Picked up from and to and press <b class="gd-ui">Show</b> for a period. <b class="gd-ui">Download CSV</b> saves the bookings of the period for a spreadsheet.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="insurance-replacements-rates-and-billing-emails-as-blind-spot-car-rental" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Emails as Blind Spot Car Rental</h2><p class="gd-p">Insurance emails go from <b class="gd-ui">Blind Spot Car Rental &lt;blindspotcarrental@carmacars.ca&gt;</b> and replies come back to that address: the insurer invoice, <b class="gd-ui">Email the adjuster</b>, and Email the renter when you choose Blind Spot Car Rental as the sender on a booking an insurer pays. Every other email still goes from CarmaCars.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The address sends today. To receive the replies, the mailbox (or an alias of rent@carmacars.ca in Google Workspace) must exist.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">VLF (vehicle licensing fee)</h3><p class="gd-p">A default VLF a day can be set in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> (Insurer-billed rentals: VLF a day; $0 means none). When a rental is first billed to an insurer, that VLF is put on it as one of its charges to the insurer; change the rate or remove it there, like the others. Before the renter pays again, remove the charges to the insurer.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Adjusters</h3><p class="gd-p">Each insurer has its adjusters, and an invoice goes to the booking&#39;s adjuster (else the insurer&#39;s billing email, which is now optional).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a booking, in <b class="gd-ui">Insurance claim and adjuster</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b>. Choose the insurer, or <b class="gd-ui">Not listed: add it</b> and type its name.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose a saved <b class="gd-ui">Adjuster</b> of that insurer, or <b class="gd-ui">Add the adjuster</b> and type the name, phone and email. A new adjuster is saved with the insurer for the next booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On <b class="gd-ui">Add a rental</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Saved adjuster</b> fills the adjuster&#39;s fields; a new one typed is saved the same way (matched by email, else by name).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On <b class="gd-ui">Insurers</b>, open an insurer: Adjusters lists them (<b class="gd-ui">Add an adjuster</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Change</b>).</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">What was billed</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Insurers</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Billed by insurer and class</b>: bookings, days, the average daily rate, the rental, the charges (VLF, LDW and the others), HST and the insurer&#39;s total. Open an insurer for <b class="gd-ui">Charged by class</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Billing by car</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Billing by adjuster</b>, and each booking with its car, adjuster and charges.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="insurance-replacements-rates-and-billing-winter-tire-fee-on-a-rental" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Winter tire fee on a rental</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the booking. The <b class="gd-ui">Winter tire fee</b> card sets this rental&#39;s rate a day (0 removes the tires) and, if needed, a cap for the rental, with the reason.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">It works on a rental the renter pays and on an insurer-billed rental (the tires are then one of the charges on the insurer&#39;s invoice).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The change is kept in the booking&#39;s history with who made it and why, and the total is worked out again. The renter of a rental they pay gets an email.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="insurance-replacements-rates-and-billing-when-an-insurer-s-mail-server-refuses-our-email-release-51" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">When an insurer&#39;s mail server refuses our email (release 51)</h2><p class="gd-p">Some insurers&#39; mailboxes accept only senders on their list. Their server then sends back a bounce email. The site reads it, marks that version <b class="gd-ui">bounced</b> under <b class="gd-ui">Versions sent</b> with the reason, and writes it in the claim history.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">If the insurer has a general claims email (Settings, Insurers), the same invoice or estimate goes again there at once, one time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Admin gets one urgent To do, &quot;Insurer email bounced&quot;, with the reason, the adjuster, the insurer&#39;s claims contact and an allowlist request ready to copy. Send it from the Blind Spot email, or call the adjuster.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each version shows how each email went: queued, sent, delivered (no bounce in 24 hours), bounced or failed.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A refusal like this is the insurer&#39;s setting, not ours: the email passed every check on our side. It stops once they add our sender address to their list.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line', 'chapter', 'live-visitors-and-live-chat', 'Every call and text on the CarmaCars number (Quo) is kept and matched to the person: staff, a renter and their booking, an owner or a lead. Staff answer texts from the same inbox as live chat. It is on by default; Program settings switch each part.

## The inbox

1. Open **Today** > **Visitors**, the **Chat** tab, and press **Texts and calls**. Each number shows who it is (Renter, Owner, Lead, Staff or Unknown caller), unread texts and missed calls.
2. Choose a number. Calls and texts are in order; a call shows its length, and Quo''s summary or a one-line AI summary when there is one.
3. Write a text and press **Send text**: it goes from the CarmaCars number through Quo. **Suggest a reply** puts an AI draft in the box; nothing is ever sent until you press Send text.
4. Beside the conversation: the renter with their bookings, the owner or the lead. A caller who gave the same phone in live chat or a discount game shows their visit on the site.
5. **Stop texts** stops every text to the number, booking texts included. A person who texts STOP is stopped the same way; START allows texts again.

## Unknown callers

Press **Unknown callers**. For a number nobody on file has, type the name if you know it and press **Create lead**, or find the renter and press **Link to** the name. The calls and texts so far follow the link. **Match automatically again** undoes a link made by hand.

## Missed calls

A missed call raises the task "Missed call from ..." for the person on duty in customer service (whoever has Live chat or Texts and calls open), otherwise the customer service queue, and the Admins when nobody holds that function. In the quiet hours (11 pm to 7 am) the task is due at 7 am. One open task per number.

> Tip: Quo itself texts back missed callers (its own auto-reply). The platform can do it instead (Program settings, "Missed call: text the caller back"), once per number in 12 hours: turn off Quo''s own auto-reply first, or callers get two texts.

## Calls and texts on records

A renter''s page and a booking''s Messages & history section show the texts, calls, missed calls, voicemails and summaries in the Activity log (chips **Texts** and **Calls**); an owner''s page has "Calls and texts". Calls are recorded: each call has its transcript and a one-line summary in the Activity log, and calls placed from the site''s Call button are recorded too (below).

## The Activity log (release 35)

A renter''s page and a booking''s **Messages & history** section have one **Activity** log: everything about the renter, newest first, grouped by day. It holds the emails and account messages both ways and the emails the platform sent, the texts, the live chat, the calls with their summaries and next steps, the notes, the booking''s events, the payments and refunds, the documents, identity checks and signatures, and the visits to the site with what they did there and the signals.

1. **All** shows everything. Press a chip (Emails, Texts, Live chat, Calls, Notes, Booking, Payments, Documents and ID, Website) to see one type; press **All** to go back.
2. Type in **Search the activity** and press **Search** to find a word in the log; **Clear** takes it away.
3. 50 lines show at a time: **Older** shows the next 50, **Newest** goes back to the top.
4. **Email**, **Call** and **Text** are at the top of the log. An email from the renter has **Reply**, a text or call from them **Text** or **Call**, a chat line **Open the chat**.
5. **Add a note** is above the log; the note shows in it at once.

> Good to know: Payments show to Admins, customer service, Sales and Finance, as the booking''s Money section. The log never shows an email address or a phone number.

## Quo contacts

Everyone on the site with a phone number is a contact in Quo under the same name, with their email and company: staff, renters and their drivers, owners, partners, investors, referral partners, job applicants, named visitors, leads, chauffeur clients, live chats, game players and forms left unfinished.

- A new person is added within about five minutes; a changed name, phone or email is updated the same way. Change people on the site, not in Quo: the site''s version is sent again.
- One contact per number. When two records share a number, the strongest names the contact: staff, then a renter, a driver, an owner, a partner. A number without any name is not sent.
- A contact someone already made in Quo for the number is updated rather than made twice, and its other numbers and emails are kept.
- If Quo is down or slow, bookings and everything else go on; the contacts follow when it answers again.
- **Settings**, **Quo contacts**: how many are in Quo, waiting and in error, the last run and the last error, and **Sync everyone again**. Program settings, "Phone and texts (Quo)", turn it off.

## Booking texts

Since October 22, 2026 these are text alerts: each person chooses Email, Text or Both (the chapter Text alerts, below, and **Settings**, **Text alerts**).

## The settings

Program settings, "Phone and texts (Quo)": the line on or off, calls and texts kept, the missed-call text and its task, who calls back, AI suggestions and summaries with their daily neurons, the visit of a caller, and how long calls and texts of people who are not customers are kept (12 months).


## Call and Text buttons

Every Call and Text button in Admin and the staff portal (a booking, a renter, the Now view, the map''s cards, Visitors, the field jobs) goes through Quo, from the CarmaCars number.

1. Press **Text**: a small window opens with the person and the number. Write the text (sign it CarmaCars) and press **Send**. It goes out from the CarmaCars number at once and is kept in the person''s conversation under **Today** > **Visitors** > **Chat** > **Texts and calls**; press **Open the conversation** to see it there. A number that asked for no texts is refused with the reason.
2. Press **Call**: on a phone the Quo app opens with the number in its dialer; press call there. On a computer the Quo web app opens in a new tab and the number is copied: open the dialer (Alt+C, or Ctrl+C on a Mac) and paste it. If Quo''s desktop app is your computer''s calling app, tick **On this computer, call with the Quo desktop app** once: Call then opens it straight away. Every call is noted on the conversation as Call started from the site, and Quo adds the call itself when it ends.
3. Fleet, finance and field staff can call and text the people of their work (renters, owners, leads and staff); customer service and Sales any number.
4. To use the phone''s own phone and messages apps instead, turn off **Call and Text buttons go through Quo** in **Settings** > **Program**. With Phone and texts off, the buttons use the phone''s own apps too.

## The CarmaCars app links

**Settings** > **Program**, card The CarmaCars app (App Store and Google Play). Paste the App Store link (https://apps.apple.com/...) and the Google Play link (https://play.google.com/...) once the apps are live and press Save. From then on, iPhones and Android phones browsing the site see **Download the CarmaCars app** in the footer and in the alerts invitation, with the link of their own store. Empty, nothing shows.

## Who is calling: the caller pop-up (release 34)

When someone calls the CarmaCars number, a panel opens at the bottom right of every Admin page (across the bottom on a phone) while the phone rings, and stays while the call goes on and for 3 minutes after it ends. Customer service get the same panel in their portal. The number is matched to the renter on file (their mobile or their account holder''s), the same way Texts and calls matches it.

1. A renter: their name, the booking on rent (or the next one coming) with the car, the balance they owe now (rental payments due and unpaid charges after a rental, **overdue** when a payment is late), the deposit (held, waived, released, or not taken yet), what they are waiting on (a booking request or offer, a change, a question to them, an open To do) and the last three notes.
2. Write what the call was about in **Note about this call** and press **Add note**: it is kept on the renter with the time, your name and the booking.
3. **Open the renter''s page** opens the full record. The booking opens from its line.
4. An unknown number shows **Unknown caller**: press **Create lead** to keep it as a phone lead, then open the conversation in Texts and calls to name it.
5. Press the cross to close a call; it stays closed in this browser. The panel checks for calls every 10 seconds while you use the portal (once a minute when the page is left alone).

## Calls through the site open the pop-up too (release 48)

1. A call you place from the site (the Call button, the phone in your browser) opens the pop-up at once with the Call helper, for you only. It says **Your call: on now**, then **Call ended**.
2. A call to the CarmaCars number that rings the browsers opens the pop-up for everyone it rings (customer service and Sales, as set in Program settings), and for every Admin. When someone answers, it says **On the phone now** and the history names who took it.
3. The pop-up opens within about a second of the ring: it no longer waits for the 10 second check. Every office role gets it: customer service, Fleet, Sales and Finance.
4. Every call through the site is recorded (both sides), turned into text and summarised. On the renter''s page, choose **Calls** in the Activity log: each call shows the date, in or out, who took it, how long, **Play**, **Show the transcript** and the summary. The booking''s history shows the same.
5. Quo calls show Quo''s recording, transcript and summary there too. When Quo sends no summary, the site writes a one line summary from the transcript.
6. Calls of the last 60 days that were missing a recording, transcript or summary are looked up once at Twilio and at Quo, a few every five minutes.

## Minimize the pop-up, and the Call helper (release 43)

1. The line at the top right of a call minimizes it to a small chip at the bottom of the page: the caller''s name and the call''s timer. A click anywhere outside the panel, or Esc, minimizes it too; nothing is closed by accident. Press the chip to open the call again. The cross still closes a call in this browser, and a new call always opens by itself.
2. Inside each call, the **Call helper** is for new hires: **Say** (the greeting, with the staff member''s first name and the caller''s name and booking when known), a button for each situation with 3 to 6 short steps and links to the right page of their portal, and **Search the quick answers**. **Hide** puts it away in that browser.
3. You write all of it in **Settings** > **Call helper** (see Settings). **Edit** on the helper takes you there.

## Renter notes (release 34)

Every renter page has **Add a note**, and its Activity log lists the notes (chip **Notes**): what staff noted about the renter, newest first, with the date and time, who wrote it and their role, the booking and the words during a call when it was written from the pop-up. Admins and office staff add notes; nobody can change one. To take one away, press **Remove** and give the reason: it is no longer shown, and the note, the removal and the reason stay in the audit log. The same notes show on the caller pop-up, on a renter''s conversation in Texts and calls, and on the staff portal''s renter.

## The Call button through Twilio (release 35)
Since release 44 calls are made and taken in the browser (below); ringing the staff member''s own cell first is a Program setting, off by default. The release 35 way: **Call** on a staff page rings the staff member''s own cell, then connects the customer with the CarmaCars number as caller ID, and logs the call with its length and outcome on the renter, lead or booking. It needs the GitHub secrets TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID, TWILIO_API_KEY and TWILIO_API_SECRET (and the CarmaCars number as a verified caller ID in Twilio); until then **Call** opens Quo and says why. A staff member with no mobile on their profile is asked for it the first time they press **Call** (a Canadian or US mobile, saved without a texted code), then the call starts (release 40).

## Calls in the browser (release 44)

Staff, Admins included, make and take calls in the browser of the staff and Admin portals, with the CarmaCars number as caller ID. Staff abroad never use their own international number.

1. **Call** anywhere opens the call screen (a card at the bottom left on a computer, the whole screen on a phone): the name and number, then the timer, **Mute**, **Keypad**, **Speaker** (microphone and speaker choice), **Hold** and the red **End call**, which is always on the screen and also cancels a call that is still starting. Switching apps on a phone keeps the call on; closing the page ends a call that is still starting. The round green phone button at the bottom left opens **Keypad** (any number) and **Contacts** (the people called last, or a search of renters and leads; Sales see only their own leads, masked). The browser asks once for the microphone. The call is kept on the person''s history with its length and its recording, as before.
2. A call to the business number rings the browsers of the staff who have a staff page open, by role (customer service and Sales by default), each with **Answer** and **Decline**. Sales sees the caller''s name or the number hidden.
3. Nobody online or nobody answered: the caller hears the message of Program settings and it is a missed call with its task and its text back, like every missed call. With a forward number set, the call goes there instead. Never to a staff member''s own number.
4. **Settings** > **Program**, the phone settings: **Calls in the browser** (on), Whose browser rings (cs, sales; add admin, fleet or finance), **Ring for (seconds)** (25), **Calls in the browser: nobody answered, forward to** (empty), **Calls in the browser: nobody answered, the message**, and Ring my own mobile first (the release 35 way, off).

> Good to know: Setting up Twilio once: save the GitHub repository secrets TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID (AC...), TWILIO_API_KEY (an API key SID, SK...), TWILIO_API_SECRET (that key''s secret) and TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN (the account''s Auth Token, which checks every request from Twilio), and TWILIO_CALLER_ID (the business number, for example +12895550123) when it differs from the CarmaCars number of Site settings. The business number must be a Twilio number or a verified caller ID in Twilio. The site makes the TwiML App "CarmaCars browser calls" itself, and points a Twilio business number with no Voice URL at the site. For incoming calls to ring browsers, calls to the business number must reach that Twilio number (buy it in Twilio, or forward to it). Until all is set, **Call** says what is missing.

Sales sees customer numbers hidden. Viewing as a Sales rep, **Reveal** shows a number; every reveal is in the audit log.

## Unanswered

**Leads** > **Unanswered** (customer service has it too): every customer text with no reply and every missed call not called back, oldest first. **Reply** or **Call back** opens the conversation; **Mark answered** when it was answered another way. A customer waiting more than 15 minutes (Program settings, **Unanswered SLA minutes**) alerts customer service and the Admins once. WhatsApp is not in the list: the morning digest reminds you to check it.

## Call recording and transcripts (release 35)

Calls placed from the site''s Call button are recorded from the moment the customer answers. No caller notice plays.

1. The recording is copied to CarmaCars'' private storage and deleted at Twilio once our copy is safe (Program settings, on by default).
2. It is turned into text with the free daily AI allowance; when the allowance is used, the call waits for the next day.
3. The transcript, its summary and Play recording show on the renter''s, the lead''s, the booking''s and the conversation''s history, for Admins, customer service and Sales.
4. The transcript feeds the renter''s and the lead''s intent at once (hot, warm or cold, with what they said they want).
5. Recording and deleting at Twilio are two switches in Program settings, under the phone settings.

## Calls first, texts after (release 37)

Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.

1. Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.
2. **Call before you text.** On a lead, a renter or a booking, **Call** is the first button and **Text** the second.
3. A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.
4. On your To do and on **Unanswered**, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.', 'Texts and calls (the Quo phone line)', 'Texts and calls in the chat inbox, unknown callers, missed calls, booking texts, call summaries and the settings.',
  'Every call and text on the CarmaCars number (Quo) is kept and matched to the person: staff, a renter and their booking, an owner or a lead. Staff answer texts from the same inbox as live chat. It is on by default; Program settings switch each part.

## The inbox

1. Open **Today** > **Visitors**, the **Chat** tab, and press **Texts and calls**. Each number shows who it is (Renter, Owner, Lead, Staff or Unknown caller), unread texts and missed calls.
2. Choose a number. Calls and texts are in order; a call shows its length, and Quo''s summary or a one-line AI summary when there is one.
3. Write a text and press **Send text**: it goes from the CarmaCars number through Quo. **Suggest a reply** puts an AI draft in the box; nothing is ever sent until you press Send text.
4. Beside the conversation: the renter with their bookings, the owner or the lead. A caller who gave the same phone in live chat or a discount game shows their visit on the site.
5. **Stop texts** stops every text to the number, booking texts included. A person who texts STOP is stopped the same way; START allows texts again.

## Unknown callers

Press **Unknown callers**. For a number nobody on file has, type the name if you know it and press **Create lead**, or find the renter and press **Link to** the name. The calls and texts so far follow the link. **Match automatically again** undoes a link made by hand.

## Missed calls

A missed call raises the task "Missed call from ..." for the person on duty in customer service (whoever has Live chat or Texts and calls open), otherwise the customer service queue, and the Admins when nobody holds that function. In the quiet hours (11 pm to 7 am) the task is due at 7 am. One open task per number.

> Tip: Quo itself texts back missed callers (its own auto-reply). The platform can do it instead (Program settings, "Missed call: text the caller back"), once per number in 12 hours: turn off Quo''s own auto-reply first, or callers get two texts.

## Calls and texts on records

A renter''s page and a booking''s Messages & history section show the texts, calls, missed calls, voicemails and summaries in the Activity log (chips **Texts** and **Calls**); an owner''s page has "Calls and texts". Calls are recorded: each call has its transcript and a one-line summary in the Activity log, and calls placed from the site''s Call button are recorded too (below).

## The Activity log (release 35)

A renter''s page and a booking''s **Messages & history** section have one **Activity** log: everything about the renter, newest first, grouped by day. It holds the emails and account messages both ways and the emails the platform sent, the texts, the live chat, the calls with their summaries and next steps, the notes, the booking''s events, the payments and refunds, the documents, identity checks and signatures, and the visits to the site with what they did there and the signals.

1. **All** shows everything. Press a chip (Emails, Texts, Live chat, Calls, Notes, Booking, Payments, Documents and ID, Website) to see one type; press **All** to go back.
2. Type in **Search the activity** and press **Search** to find a word in the log; **Clear** takes it away.
3. 50 lines show at a time: **Older** shows the next 50, **Newest** goes back to the top.
4. **Email**, **Call** and **Text** are at the top of the log. An email from the renter has **Reply**, a text or call from them **Text** or **Call**, a chat line **Open the chat**.
5. **Add a note** is above the log; the note shows in it at once.

> Good to know: Payments show to Admins, customer service, Sales and Finance, as the booking''s Money section. The log never shows an email address or a phone number.

## Quo contacts

Everyone on the site with a phone number is a contact in Quo under the same name, with their email and company: staff, renters and their drivers, owners, partners, investors, referral partners, job applicants, named visitors, leads, chauffeur clients, live chats, game players and forms left unfinished.

- A new person is added within about five minutes; a changed name, phone or email is updated the same way. Change people on the site, not in Quo: the site''s version is sent again.
- One contact per number. When two records share a number, the strongest names the contact: staff, then a renter, a driver, an owner, a partner. A number without any name is not sent.
- A contact someone already made in Quo for the number is updated rather than made twice, and its other numbers and emails are kept.
- If Quo is down or slow, bookings and everything else go on; the contacts follow when it answers again.
- **Settings**, **Quo contacts**: how many are in Quo, waiting and in error, the last run and the last error, and **Sync everyone again**. Program settings, "Phone and texts (Quo)", turn it off.

## Booking texts

Since October 22, 2026 these are text alerts: each person chooses Email, Text or Both (the chapter Text alerts, below, and **Settings**, **Text alerts**).

## The settings

Program settings, "Phone and texts (Quo)": the line on or off, calls and texts kept, the missed-call text and its task, who calls back, AI suggestions and summaries with their daily neurons, the visit of a caller, and how long calls and texts of people who are not customers are kept (12 months).


## Call and Text buttons

Every Call and Text button in Admin and the staff portal (a booking, a renter, the Now view, the map''s cards, Visitors, the field jobs) goes through Quo, from the CarmaCars number.

1. Press **Text**: a small window opens with the person and the number. Write the text (sign it CarmaCars) and press **Send**. It goes out from the CarmaCars number at once and is kept in the person''s conversation under **Today** > **Visitors** > **Chat** > **Texts and calls**; press **Open the conversation** to see it there. A number that asked for no texts is refused with the reason.
2. Press **Call**: on a phone the Quo app opens with the number in its dialer; press call there. On a computer the Quo web app opens in a new tab and the number is copied: open the dialer (Alt+C, or Ctrl+C on a Mac) and paste it. If Quo''s desktop app is your computer''s calling app, tick **On this computer, call with the Quo desktop app** once: Call then opens it straight away. Every call is noted on the conversation as Call started from the site, and Quo adds the call itself when it ends.
3. Fleet, finance and field staff can call and text the people of their work (renters, owners, leads and staff); customer service and Sales any number.
4. To use the phone''s own phone and messages apps instead, turn off **Call and Text buttons go through Quo** in **Settings** > **Program**. With Phone and texts off, the buttons use the phone''s own apps too.

