## AI and automation on quizzes (release 51)

Every question says: **Answer yourself. Using AI tools, browser agents or computer-use software on this test is not allowed and breaks your agreement; CarmaCars may take legal action.** The quiz page blocks paste and copy and notices browser automation, clicks not made by a person, a pointer that jumps, leaving the page more than twice and answers picked faster than reading allows. Any of them voids the try (it counts as a failed try) and the Admins get the alert "Academy attempt voided (AI or automation)".

1. Open **Team** > **Academy** and the person: **Voided or flagged attempts** lists each one with what the quiz page saw.
2. Talk to the person before you reset a section.
3. **Program settings**: academy_integrity_void (on: void; off: grade and only flag), academy_focus_loss_max (2) and academy_answer_floor_seconds (2).

> Good to know: No web page can fully stop an AI agent that controls the browser. These checks make it detectable. The staff agreements say the same (section 2.3 of the Field Staff Agreement, 2.4 of the contractor agreement).',
