4. You never check an e-Transfer you reported yourself.


## 407 ETR statements

1. Read the statement PDF or its CSV download (the PDF and the CSV of one statement are the same trips: read one of them).
2. Each trip is read from its column: the date and the entry time, the plate (from its own column, or the Licence Plate line above its trips), the entry and the exit, and the toll with its camera and trip toll charges. The line''s amount is what the renter owes for the trip; Of which fees is the camera and trip toll charges. A distance is never read as money.
3. The monthly account fee and a late payment charge are not trips: they are listed under the read as left out.
4. A credit or a reversal is left out and said. A line whose charges do not add up to its total is marked for you to check.
5. Each trip goes to whoever had the car at that minute. Within the boundary margin of Program settings (30 minutes) of a rental''s start or end, a person confirms who had it; nothing is charged by itself there.

## Log an expense from the receipt

**More finance** > **Maintenance and expenses** > **Expenses**, on a phone or a computer.

1. Press **Take a photo** (or **Upload photos**). Add more photos of the same receipt if it is long.
2. The amount before tax, the HST, the date, the shop, the category and the car are read from the photo. Check each one; anything not read clearly is said above the fields.
3. Who pays: the car''s owner (it goes on their next statement as a cost, with the receipt in their documents, and they get an email) or CarmaCars (a company expense on the car). Tick **I paid with my own money** to be paid back.
4. Press **Save**. The expense is listed under Logged from receipts, with its photos.

## Winter tire fee on a rental

Open the booking. The **Winter tire fee** card sets this rental''s rate a day (0 removes the tires) and, if needed, a cap for the rental, with the reason.

1. It works on a rental the renter pays and on an insurer-billed rental (the tires are then one of the charges on the insurer''s invoice).
2. The change is kept in the booking''s history with who made it and why, and the total is worked out again. The renter of a rental they pay gets an email.

## Insurance replacements

**Money** > **Insurance replacements** (customer service: the button on Bookings) lists every rental an insurer pays for, with its claim, car, dates, invoice versions, what was billed, approved and paid, and the aging.

1. **Add an insurance replacement**: the renter''s name, the insurer and claim, and the dates are enough. **Paste text** reads an adjuster''s email for you to check (**Use these**). A car not in the fleet is typed in (year, make, model, plate) and stays off the calendar and owner notices.
2. On the rental, change any field of the invoice, then **Send as an estimate** or **Send the invoice**, as often as needed: each send is a version with its PDF and what changed. **Extend** moves the return when the insurer authorizes more days.
3. **Record a payment** (cheque, e-Transfer, direct deposit; part payments too), **Approved amount**, **Negotiating** and **Write off the rest** with the reason. Customer service adds and edits rentals; Finance sends invoices and records the money.



## When an insurer''s mail server refuses our email (release 51)

Some insurers'' mailboxes accept only senders on their list. Their server then sends back a bounce email. The site reads it, marks that version **bounced** under **Versions sent** with the reason, and writes it in the claim history.

1. If the insurer has a general claims email (Settings, Insurers), the same invoice or estimate goes again there at once, one time.
2. Admin gets one urgent To do, "Insurer email bounced", with the reason, the adjuster, the insurer''s claims contact and an allowlist request ready to copy. Send it from the Blind Spot email, or call the adjuster.
3. Each version shows how each email went: queued, sent, delivered (no bounce in 24 hours), bounced or failed.

> Good to know: A refusal like this is the insurer''s setting, not ours: the email passed every check on our side. It stops once they add our sender address to their list.',
  '<p class="gd-p">You keep the money right: payments, deposits and refunds, toll notices, processor payouts and Turo trips. There is no commission for Finance, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.</p><p class="gd-p">Your rail: Queue, Today, Money, Tolls and tickets, Turo trips, Find a renter, Calendar and Scorecard. <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> opens with a row of tabs on top, as in Admin: <b class="gd-ui">To handle</b> (payments, deposits, refunds), <b class="gd-ui">By day</b> (with Today, 7 days, 30 days and 90 days), <b class="gd-ui">All payments</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Refunds</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Deposits</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Reconciliation</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Unlinked Stripe</b> (the Stripe payments of the last 60 days that no booking knows, checked every night, with a best guess of the booking: an Admin links one from the booking&#39;s Money tab; put one aside with the reason when it is not a booking&#39;s payment). <b class="gd-ui">Owner money</b> lists every owner invoice and owner statement. The old Payments by day and Reconciliation addresses open their tabs.</p><section class="gd-task" id="finance-your-queue" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your queue</h2><p class="gd-p">Finance tasks include failed owner debits, toll notices with no match, statements to review and refunds to issue.</p><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/940"><img src="/guides/img/va-finance-01-queue-desktop-2f37513d.jpg" alt="The lanes show what Finance handles: payments to fix, refunds waiting, tolls and tickets, deposits to settle and owner statements. Money today counts them below." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="940"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.3%;top:24.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div><figcaption>The lanes show what Finance handles: payments to fix, refunds waiting, tolls and tickets, deposits to settle and owner statements. Money today counts them below.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-payments-by-day" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Payments by day</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">By day</b> tab, is your day in one screen: every payment and refund, by method, with the cash drawer and the refunds to decide.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose From and To (today by default) and tick the methods you want (card, e-Transfer, cash, cheque, platform payout, insurer and others; none ticked shows all), then press <b class="gd-ui">Show</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Totals by method: received, refunded and net. Each day: the same by method, the cash expected in the drawer (cash received less cash given back) and the cash counted.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">At the end of the day count the drawer and press <b class="gd-ui">Record the count</b>. The difference shows &quot;balanced&quot;, or &quot;over&quot; or &quot;short&quot; with the amount.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Refunds waiting: every refund asked for anywhere (a cancellation, a booking, Finance), with the policy maths (paid, the tier, the percentage back, what is kept). Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> with the reason in the same row; above your limit it says an Admin approves. Approved: <b class="gd-ui">Issue the refund</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Export CSV</b> gives the same rows for the bank or the bookkeeper: refunds as negative amounts, holds marked as not money in.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-payments-deposits-refunds" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Payments, deposits, refunds</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">To handle</b> tab.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Failed payments: each with the purpose, amount and the bank&#39;s reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Deposits to take before pickup, and deposits due back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Refunds in progress. Press <b class="gd-ui">Request the refund</b> and choose What it refunds (the rental charge, delivery or pickup, kilometres, add-ons or other charges); above your limit it waits for an Admin. Then <b class="gd-ui">Issue the refund</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Owner invoices that failed, and owner statements to prepare.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/money</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/865"><img src="/guides/img/va-finance-02-money-desktop-486a8fbc.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="865"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:10.6%;top:60.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.4%;top:21.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:73.2%;top:33.8%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:11%;top:45.9%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-a-payment-received-another-way" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A payment received another way</h2><p class="gd-p">An owner or renter paid by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Owner invoice: on <b class="gd-ui">Payments, deposits, refunds</b>, find it under Owner invoices owing and press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Renter: beside the failed payment, press <b class="gd-ui">Paid another way</b>. Or open the booking&#39;s Money tab: in Rental charges press Collect (the amount) rental, or in Security deposit Collect (the amount) deposit, choose <b class="gd-ui">Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)</b> and how it was paid, then record it. Each panel collects its own part only.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Choose Paid by, the Date received and the Reference (the cheque number for a cheque). Leave Amount empty for the full balance; type less for a partial payment.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add the proof if you have it (a screenshot or a photo of the cheque), then press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The invoice is marked paid or partly paid, the automatic debit stops for that amount and the owner gets a receipt. Above your single limit the payment needs an Admin. Recorded something wrong? Ask an Admin to void it; you cannot void a payment.</p><p class="gd-p">Each month&#39;s payments recorded by hand are listed under Reconciliation, with the totals by method, to check against the bank.</p><p class="gd-p">A pay link for the rental, the fees or the balance asks for what is owed and never more (release 48): the booking&#39;s total less every payment of it, refunds counted back. After a change to the total, the link is for the difference. A booking paid in full gets no balance link: anything on top is a later charge, with its reason. A new link replaces any open one for the booking&#39;s money, and a link still open when a payment lands is cancelled by itself (the booking history says so), so the renter is never charged twice.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-cards-holds-and-deposits-given-back" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cards, holds and deposits given back</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking&#39;s Money tab.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">After the return, <b class="gd-ui">Charge the renter</b>: the Reason from the list (Other with its note), the Amount, and the line that says where the money comes from (the deposit hold while it is valid, else the card on file, else a pay link) before you press <b class="gd-ui">Charge $...</b>. Before the return, Rental charges, <b class="gd-ui">A later charge</b>, with the same reason list on the renter&#39;s receipt. A deposit that cannot be held: Security deposit, <b class="gd-ui">Charge the card on file as the deposit</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A deposit hold, in the Security deposit panel: <b class="gd-ui">Keep part (damage/fees)</b> with the amount and the reason from the list (the rest is released), or <b class="gd-ui">Release</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Hold expired</b>: nothing can be kept from it; press <b class="gd-ui">Charge the card on file instead</b> (the amount and the reason are filled in). While the car is out, inside the toll window or while something is open, both wait for the settlement; an Admin may do it with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A deposit taken in cash or by e-Transfer is given back the same way: the task Give the deposit back the way it came; then press <b class="gd-ui">Returned</b> with the reference or receipt number.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-settle-a-deposit" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Settle a deposit</h2><p class="gd-p">The deposit is never given back by itself. Finance or an Admin settles it after the return: on the booking&#39;s Money tab, under Deposit, press <b class="gd-ui">Settle the deposit</b>. Issue the Check-out statement first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The form shows the deposit, what is still available, the charges owed from the statement and what is taken from the deposit for them. What the deposit does not cover is charged to the card on file; with no card (or a card declined), the renter gets a pay link by email and text, and Finance has a task until it is paid.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Tolls and tickets can take up to 7 days to come in. Inside that window the whole rest of the deposit is filled in as the hold-back, until the window ends. To give it back sooner, tick Release now anyway: a toll that comes in later is charged to the card on file.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Something still open keeps the whole deposit: an incident, a claim, new damage at the return not priced, damage found later not billed, a toll or ticket on the car during the rental not matched or not charged, a card dispute, or charges not on a statement yet. The form lists them. Only an Admin can release part of it, with the reason; it is recorded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Damage: an Admin keeps the whole deposit (<b class="gd-ui">Keep the whole deposit (damage)</b>) or bills a damage charge up to the $2,500 deductible. Ask an Admin, with the photos.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Settle</b>. The money moves at Stripe at once: the charges are collected and what is not owed is refunded or the hold released. A step Stripe refuses is tried again by itself, and Finance gets a task if it keeps failing.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A card hold lapses after about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise. While the car is out, or returned and not settled, the hold is collected in full a day and a half before it lapses: that keeps the money, and the settlement refunds what is not owed. A hold that lapses anyway is charged to the saved card, and Finance is told at once.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-read-a-toll-notice" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Read a toll notice</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Tolls and tickets</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Read a notice</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the file: a PDF, a photo or a CSV, under 15 MB. Leave the reading profile to find it from the text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Read it</b>. Then check each line beside the notice and fix what was read wrong.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Checked against the notice</b> on each line (<b class="gd-ui">Leave out</b> to skip one), then <b class="gd-ui">Save as checked</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Confirm and import</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/tolls/read</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/580"><img src="/guides/img/va-finance-04-tolls-read-desktop-aa04a6b2.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="580"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.5%;top:44.1%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:4.1%;top:64.8%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:4.1%;top:89.7%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>In the work queue, <b class="gd-ui">Match again</b> retries the match after a fix, and <b class="gd-ui">Dispute</b> marks a notice you think is wrong. Renters matched with high confidence are charged at import, with the notice and our fee.</div></aside><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/tolls</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/540"><img src="/guides/img/va-finance-03-tolls-desktop-37b6f99c.jpg" alt="The work queue: Unmatched, Needs review, Matched not charged and Disputed, with each notice&#39;s plate, date, amount and match." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="540"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:23.6%;top:12.2%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div><figcaption>The work queue: Unmatched, Needs review, Matched not charged and Disputed, with each notice&#39;s plate, date, amount and match.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-reconciliation-and-turo-trips" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Reconciliation and Turo trips</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Reconciliation</b> tab: press <b class="gd-ui">Record a processor payout</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Match</b> it to the payments it contains. Anything still unmatched at the closing check goes to an Admin.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Turo trips</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Add a trip</b> for one trip, or paste CSV rows and press <b class="gd-ui">Import</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/turo</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/540"><img src="/guides/img/va-finance-06-turo-desktop-b59cc7f9.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="540"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:95.1%;top:14.8%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-deposits-to-release" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Deposits to release</h2><p class="gd-p">A deposit is never released by itself. Each morning the system puts one task in your queue for every deposit due back: &quot;Release the deposit for&quot; the booking, with the amount and the day it is due (7 business days after the check-out, or after the return when no check-out was recorded). On the day, and every day after, you and the Admins also get a notice in the portal. Nothing is emailed.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the task: it opens the booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Settle the deposit: apply what is owed, hold back what an open item needs, release the rest.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The task closes by itself once nothing is left to give back.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Card payments outside the site and the card reader</h3><p class="gd-p">On a booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab: <b class="gd-ui">Record card payment</b> records a card taken in the Stripe Dashboard or on a reader (the last 4 digits always; a Stripe payment id, pi_..., checks it, and a deposit hold needs it). <b class="gd-ui">Charge on reader</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Hold deposit on reader</b> send the amount to the S700; the renter taps the card and the screen updates by itself. On a credit card coverage rental the whole rental is paid on the same card: another card is refused with the reason, and only an Admin can allow another one.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-deposit-holds-and-partner-invoices-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Deposit holds and partner invoices (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">Deposits stay as holds with Stripe and are never captured by itself. A job re-authorizes a hold by itself about 24 hours before it expires; when it cannot, you get the alert <b class="gd-ui">Deposit hold not re-authorized</b>. A <b class="gd-ui">The deposit hold expires soon</b> To do opens the booking: <b class="gd-ui">Re-authorize the hold</b> places a new hold on the saved card and releases the old one; or <b class="gd-ui">Keep part (damage/fees)</b> for only what is owed. A deposit not taken yet: in the Security deposit panel, <b class="gd-ui">Hold on the card on file</b>. Under <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Partner invoices</b> you write invoices to body shops, tow trucks and storage yards for their kickback, send them, record the cheques and e-Transfers that come in, and export the CSV for the bookkeeper.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-kickbacks-and-repairs" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Kickbacks and repairs</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Kickbacks and repairs</b>: the kickbacks received on partner invoices (before HST) and the repair costs paid by CarmaCars for a period, by owner and by car, with the CSV. An invoice with no car counts nowhere until you choose it: open the invoice under <b class="gd-ui">Partner invoices</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Choose the car</b>. Add a repair cost with <b class="gd-ui">Add a repair cost</b>; Fleet adds them on the car&#39;s page too.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">A debit deposit&#39;s card fee</h3><p class="gd-p">A deposit charged (not held) on a debit or prepaid card carries the non-refundable <b class="gd-ui">Card processing fee for a debit deposit</b>, shown on its line in the history and on the receipt. The deposit refund returns the deposit only.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-partners-the-timesheet-and-ended-trips" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Partners, the timesheet and ended trips</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">More finance</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Partners</b>: the rental partners (their pages, cars, rates, invoices) and the referral partners (kickbacks, payments), with every action an Admin has there.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Timesheet</b>: the hours customer service, Fleet and Finance clocked. Add forgotten hours or void a wrong entry, with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Close ended trips</b>: mark trips that ended and were never closed, and choose the deposit decision. An Admin presses Release; nothing is released by itself.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-deposit-review-double-check-tolls-and-tickets-then-bill-or-r" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Deposit review: double-check, tolls and tickets, then bill or release</h2><p class="gd-p">Once Fleet signed every item of a returned booking you get a To do to double-check the deposit review. The deposit stays held until you signed every item too; only an Admin can release it earlier, with the reason.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Deposit reviews</b> and open the booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Double-check</b> on each item: read Fleet&#39;s finding and the photos, then <b class="gd-ui">OK</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Issue</b> with the amount to bill. Someone else double-checks an item you signed for Fleet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Highway tolls</b>: open the toll operator&#39;s site from the review, search the plate for the rental dates, then double-check the item.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Tickets</b>: open each place in the list (its official lookup link), search the plate, and press <b class="gd-ui">None found</b> or <b class="gd-ui">A ticket</b>. A ticket is logged in <b class="gd-ui">Tolls and tickets</b> with the place and the plate and matched to the booking there. The Tickets item waits until every place is checked.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Then open <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> on the booking: bill what is owed with the charge after the return, or release the deposit.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">The sweep, Monday, Wednesday and Friday</h3><p class="gd-p">On each sweep day a To do <b class="gd-ui">Deposit check sweep</b> lists every plate returned since the last sweep and every booking still inside the toll and ticket window. <b class="gd-ui">Deposit reviews</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">This sweep</b> shows them by plate with every link, so you check them in one go. The days are in Program settings.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Countdowns</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Countdowns</b> (and the top of <b class="gd-ui">To handle</b>, and each booking) shows the time left before each deposit hold expires (with when the automatic re-authorization runs, 24 hours before), before each deposit is due back to the renter, and before the next payment of a weekly, biweekly or monthly plan. Red is within 24 hours or late, amber within 48. Sort by any column. You get an alert at 48 and 24 hours, and the counts are in your morning digest.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Do sales too</h3><p class="gd-p">Under <b class="gd-ui">My numbers</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Do sales too</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">I want to do sales too</b>: the Sales path is added to your academy (your Finance work is never held by it), and the Sales pages open once you pass it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-the-fuel-line-on-the-deposit-review-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The fuel line on the deposit review (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">The fuel item shows <b class="gd-ui">Suggested</b> with its working: the tank x the fuel missing x the pump price x 1.25, plus the $20 refuelling fee. It is a line on the return charges, never charged by itself: sign the item, then bill it with the rest from the booking&#39;s Money. A pump receipt still wins: enter it when the car was filled up.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-statements-and-payroll-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Statements and payroll (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Statements cover the 8th to the 7th, paid on the 10th; amounts not yet collected from the renter are listed apart and paid on the statement after they come in.</li><li>Payroll every two weeks: prepare the run with any bonus or deduction and its reason, then send it for approval. An Admin approves and records the payments.</li><li>Field spending (release 50): each expense says whose money paid. You get an alert for each one. <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> with the reason (the person sees it). Own money is then owed to the person: <b class="gd-ui">Reimbursements owed</b> on Payroll and Field spending lists it per person; press <b class="gd-ui">Mark paid back</b> once it is paid with their pay.</li><li>Email: Settings, Usage shows the real daily capacity of our sending services together; nothing to count by hand.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-calls-first-texts-after-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls first, texts after (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call before you text.</b> On a lead, a renter or a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> is the first button and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> the second.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On your To do and on <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b>, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-a-late-return-is-a-choice-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A late return is a choice (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p">A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Late return</b> with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge as an extension</b>: every started day late at the booking&#39;s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge extra days</b>: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge the late return fee</b>: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge a custom amount</b>: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Waive it</b>: no charge, with the reason.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the late return charge</b>. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.</p><p class="gd-p">Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do &quot;Late return: choose the charge&quot;. Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do &quot;Late return: approve the charge&quot; and press <b class="gd-ui">Approve as asked</b>, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-payments-by-e-transfer-or-cash-deposits-and-tips" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Payments by e-Transfer or cash, deposits and tips</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Record a payment</b>: a payment of the whole total pays every line of the booking (the rental, short notice, the young driver fee, the Protection Plan), whichever part you record it for. When nothing is open, a booking waiting for payment is confirmed by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The deposit by e-Transfer or cash is doubled</b>: twice the car&#39;s deposit by default (Program settings). The Security deposit card shows both amounts (&quot;Credit card hold $300.00; e-Transfer or cash $600.00 (2x)&quot;), and the renter sees them on the offer and the pay page before paying.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Collect the deposit</b> &gt; Cash or e-Transfer: leave the amount empty to take what is owed. Less is recorded as a part (the card says <b class="gd-ui">under, still owed $X</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Collect the $X still owed</b> takes the rest); more is held and given back with the deposit (<b class="gd-ui">over, to return $X</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Change the deposit</b> on Edit booking (an Admin, with the reason), even while the booking waits for payment: the Money tab, the deposit link and Collect $X deposit follow at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Voided a deposit by mistake?</b> After the void the deposit is <b class="gd-ui">Not collected</b> again everywhere (the header too): record it again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Tips</b>: the renter can add one when paying, on the receipt and from the after-trip email. A tip in cash or by e-Transfer: <b class="gd-ui">Tips</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Record a tip</b>. Half goes to the booking&#39;s salesperson and half to the staff member at the handover; with no staff salesperson (a direct booking) CarmaCars keeps that half; one person who did both gets it all. An Admin can give one tip another split (<b class="gd-ui">All to ...</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Back to the usual split</b>). A tip is never part of the rental or the owner&#39;s share.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">A greyed-out button says under it what to do first.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-evidence-for-every-fee-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Evidence for every fee (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A fee waiting for its evidence stays off the statement; the rest goes as usual. Issuing a statement with only such a fee says what is missing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A To do in the Finance queue asks for a toll or ticket notice, a receipt or an invoice. Attach it on the Money tab (<b class="gd-ui">Attach evidence</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When the evidence of a held fee arrives after the Check-out statement, you get <b class="gd-ui">Evidence attached: bill the fee that was waiting</b>: bill it from the Money tab.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Only an Admin charges a fee without its evidence, with the reason.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-finance-dashboard-and-the-bank-release-49" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Finance dashboard and the bank (release 49)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Finance</b> is the money of the business on one page, read only: each figure opens the page where it is worked.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Cash position</b>: the bank balance from the latest RBC import, Stripe&#39;s balance (available and pending) and its payouts on the way, and <b class="gd-ui">Free cash</b>: all of that less the deposits held as cash, the owner payouts due, the refunds owed and the HST owed. An account whose balance is more than a week old is marked: import this week&#39;s download.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Money in</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Money out</b> for the month (Earlier month, Later month): rentals and charges taken, owner fees, insurers, tips (for the staff, never revenue); owner payouts due and paid on the 10th, commissions, expenses with HST and refunds.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Held for others</b>: deposits held as cash (owed back unless applied), deposit holds on cards (not money in the bank), what is kept back for claims and tolls, and refunds owed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">HST</b> for the quarter: collected (renters, owners, insurers) less paid (expenses, payouts to registered owners) is what is owed. An Insurance Fee never carries HST: a line that does is listed in red to correct.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Renter balances overdue</b> (past the statement&#39;s 7 days) and <b class="gd-ui">Insurer invoices unpaid</b> by age (0 to 30, 31 to 60, 61 to 90, over 90 days).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Twelve months</b>: money in, money out and net by month, beside the monthly statement&#39;s net where one is built.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Bank lines</b> is the reconciliation:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">In RBC online banking open the account, <b class="gd-ui">Download transactions</b>, CSV or OFX (OFX also has the balance), and drop the file on <b class="gd-ui">Import from RBC online banking</b>. The file stays on your computer; only its lines are saved, with the last four digits of the account. Importing the same days again adds nothing. With a CSV, type the balance shown in online banking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A line that fits exactly one record matches by itself: money in to a Stripe payout, an e-Transfer, bank transfer or cheque recorded on a booking or owner invoice, or an insurer invoice; money out to an owner payout, a commission or referral partner payout, an expense or a refund sent by transfer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">No match</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Match</b> shows the records that fit (amount, and a date within a few days), nearest first: pick one. Nothing fits: record the payment, payout or expense first, then match. <b class="gd-ui">Set aside</b> a bank fee or a transfer between CarmaCars accounts, saying what it is. <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> takes a reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A line with no match after two days is a To do for Finance and in the Finance morning email; matching it closes the To do. Every step is in the audit log.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-check-e-transfer-release-49" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check e-Transfer (release 49)</h2><p class="gd-p">Sales reports an e-Transfer a renter sent, with the screenshot; nothing is recorded until you check the bank. You get an alert and a To do, <b class="gd-ui">Check e-Transfer</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the To do: the booking opens on its <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab. The card shows the amount, what it covers, the sender, who reported it and <b class="gd-ui">Open the screenshot</b>, and says what <b class="gd-ui">Confirm received</b> will record (for both, the deposit part is the deposit still owed by e-Transfer and the rest is the rental and fees).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">In the bank: type the <b class="gd-ui">Bank reference (optional)</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Confirm received</b>. It is recorded as Record a payment does (method e-Transfer; your single limit applies) and a booking waiting for payment with nothing open is confirmed. The screenshot becomes the payment&#39;s proof.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Not there: <b class="gd-ui">Not received</b>, say why, <b class="gd-ui">Send back to the rep</b>. Nothing is recorded; the rep is told.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">You never check an e-Transfer you reported yourself.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-407-etr-statements" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">407 ETR statements</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Read the statement PDF or its CSV download (the PDF and the CSV of one statement are the same trips: read one of them).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each trip is read from its column: the date and the entry time, the plate (from its own column, or the Licence Plate line above its trips), the entry and the exit, and the toll with its camera and trip toll charges. The line&#39;s amount is what the renter owes for the trip; Of which fees is the camera and trip toll charges. A distance is never read as money.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The monthly account fee and a late payment charge are not trips: they are listed under the read as left out.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A credit or a reversal is left out and said. A line whose charges do not add up to its total is marked for you to check.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Each trip goes to whoever had the car at that minute. Within the boundary margin of Program settings (30 minutes) of a rental&#39;s start or end, a person confirms who had it; nothing is charged by itself there.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-log-an-expense-from-the-receipt" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Log an expense from the receipt</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">More finance</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Maintenance and expenses</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Expenses</b>, on a phone or a computer.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take a photo</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Upload photos</b>). Add more photos of the same receipt if it is long.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The amount before tax, the HST, the date, the shop, the category and the car are read from the photo. Check each one; anything not read clearly is said above the fields.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Who pays: the car&#39;s owner (it goes on their next statement as a cost, with the receipt in their documents, and they get an email) or CarmaCars (a company expense on the car). Tick <b class="gd-ui">I paid with my own money</b> to be paid back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>. The expense is listed under Logged from receipts, with its photos.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-winter-tire-fee-on-a-rental" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Winter tire fee on a rental</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the booking. The <b class="gd-ui">Winter tire fee</b> card sets this rental&#39;s rate a day (0 removes the tires) and, if needed, a cap for the rental, with the reason.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">It works on a rental the renter pays and on an insurer-billed rental (the tires are then one of the charges on the insurer&#39;s invoice).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The change is kept in the booking&#39;s history with who made it and why, and the total is worked out again. The renter of a rental they pay gets an email.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-insurance-replacements" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Insurance replacements</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Insurance replacements</b> (customer service: the button on Bookings) lists every rental an insurer pays for, with its claim, car, dates, invoice versions, what was billed, approved and paid, and the aging.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add an insurance replacement</b>: the renter&#39;s name, the insurer and claim, and the dates are enough. <b class="gd-ui">Paste text</b> reads an adjuster&#39;s email for you to check (<b class="gd-ui">Use these</b>). A car not in the fleet is typed in (year, make, model, plate) and stays off the calendar and owner notices.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On the rental, change any field of the invoice, then <b class="gd-ui">Send as an estimate</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Send the invoice</b>, as often as needed: each send is a version with its PDF and what changed. <b class="gd-ui">Extend</b> moves the return when the insurer authorizes more days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Record a payment</b> (cheque, e-Transfer, direct deposit; part payments too), <b class="gd-ui">Approved amount</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Negotiating</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Write off the rest</b> with the reason. Customer service adds and edits rentals; Finance sends invoices and records the money.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="finance-when-an-insurer-s-mail-server-refuses-our-email-release-51" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">When an insurer&#39;s mail server refuses our email (release 51)</h2><p class="gd-p">Some insurers&#39; mailboxes accept only senders on their list. Their server then sends back a bounce email. The site reads it, marks that version <b class="gd-ui">bounced</b> under <b class="gd-ui">Versions sent</b> with the reason, and writes it in the claim history.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">If the insurer has a general claims email (Settings, Insurers), the same invoice or estimate goes again there at once, one time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Admin gets one urgent To do, &quot;Insurer email bounced&quot;, with the reason, the adjuster, the insurer&#39;s claims contact and an allowlist request ready to copy. Send it from the Blind Spot email, or call the adjuster.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each version shows how each email went: queued, sent, delivered (no bounce in 24 hours), bounced or failed.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A refusal like this is the insurer&#39;s setting, not ours: the email passed every check on our side. It stops once they add our sender address to their list.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'fleet', 'chapter', 'finance', 'You keep the cars moving: field jobs, daily checks, photo reviews after returns, and the listings with their duplicate check and plate covering. There is no commission for Fleet, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Field jobs, Field hours, Daily checks, Photo reviews, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Find a renter and Scorecard.

## Schedule field jobs

Every confirmed booking gets its handover (or delivery) and return (or pickup) jobs by itself, at the booking''s times and place, and put on a shift: the shift covering its time, or that day''s (see Shifts and who gets a job). The people on the shift share its jobs, least busy first. You check and change them.

1. Jobs, next three days: each with its place, its shift, its field staff and whether they acknowledged it. "Made from the booking" marks the ones made by themselves; when the booking moves, they move too, unless you changed them.
2. Change a job with **To a shift** (another shift), **Assign** or **Reassign** (a field person on a shift that day when the day has shifts, or an Admin), **Move** (time and place) or **Cancel**.
3. Handovers and returns without a job (when the automatic jobs are off, or one was cancelled) are listed first: press **Schedule**, the place filled in from the booking.
4. An Admin turns the automatic jobs or the assignment off in Settings > Program.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-02-field-jobs-desktop-8e721230.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 565; address: carmacars.ca/va/fleet; pins: 1 17.9 51.3")


### Shifts in your Google Calendar

At the bottom of **Field jobs** (and on your **Profile**), **Add shifts, townhalls and interviews to Google Calendar** gives you a private link with every field shift, 14 days back to 60 days ahead: who claimed it or Open, the tasks and a link to it, and the weekly townhall. Press **Make my calendar link**, then **Add to Google Calendar** and **Add** in Google. Google refreshes it every few hours on its own. **Regenerate link** stops the old link; **Turn off** stops it.

## Shifts and who gets a job

Field staff take their shifts from the schedule published by itself: every hour, up to 14 days ahead, from the shift template in Program settings (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day), only forward from the latest shift already published. A handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own (90 minutes either side). A job is given by itself only to a field person who passed the academy and holds a shift that day, and work lands only on days with shifts.

1. On **Field jobs**, **Shifts, next seven days** shows each day and how many people are on a shift, and each shift its jobs (**Jobs on it**). A shift with jobs and nobody on it is marked; within 24 hours of its start you get an alert and a To do, once.
2. Need more? Press **Publish shifts**: the first day''s start and end, how many people, and for how many days the same hours repeat. A shift you cancel is not published again. Field staff take them on their phones.
3. **Add a person** puts someone on a shift and **Remove** takes them off. A person who has not passed the academy cannot take shifts or be given a job.
4. A shift nobody claimed keeps its jobs: field staff see them when they look for shifts to claim, and the one who claims it gets them. A shift given up or swapped takes its jobs along; a cancelled shift sends them to another shift.
5. Work due on a day with no shifts moves to the day before when it is known in advance, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day. The job shows its planned day and keeps the booking''s real time; the renter''s times never change. A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning: cover it, or move the booking time.
6. **Unassign** takes a job off its person and its shift; tick **Tell them** only if they should know. The Admins can be given a job too (no shift needed).

## Missing check-ins and check-outs

1. **Missing check-in and check-out** on Field jobs lists every past rental without its photos and readings (odometer, fuel, damage photos), closed bookings included.
2. Press **Give to field staff** and choose the person: they add the photos and readings from their Today page.

## Fleet map

At the top of **Field jobs**: every car on the map with its renter, booking, due-back time and state, the alerts, and the trips by booking, the same as the Admin''s. Every staff member sees the cars'' positions: customer service, Sales and Finance open the same map from **Find a car** (**Car map**), read only, and field staff under **Map**. Every car page and booking page shows **Where the car is**: moving or parked, when it last reported and **Open on the map**, or **No tracker yet**. Only Admins and fleet staff press **Seen** on an alert. Each owner sees where their own cars are, never the renter or the booking.

1. Press a car for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery and the trip under way.
2. An alert (speeding, left Ontario or the zone, still driving after the return time, low or unplugged tracker, not reporting) also comes to your bell and as an urgent phone alert. Call the renter, then press **Seen**.
3. A car still driving after its return time: call, send the late notice and offer a paid extension, as for any late return.

## Field hours

Field staff clock in and out on their phones. You see who is clocked in and every shift of the two-week pay period, and you fix what they cannot.

1. Open **Field hours**. **Clocked in now** lists who is on, since when. **Earlier period** and **Later period** move between pay periods.
2. Someone forgot to clock out: press **Clock out for them**, set the time they finished and write the reason.
3. Someone forgot to clock in, or a time is wrong: **Add hours** enters a shift, **Change** fixes one and **Remove** takes one out. Each needs a reason; the change is kept in a log with what it was before.
4. Once an Admin approves the pay run of a period, its shifts are locked: ask the Admin. You see hours only, not rates or pay.

### Where they clocked in
The hours list shows where each person clocked in and out: a map link and the distance from the lot. A clock in or out over 500 m away, or with the location refused, is shown in bold with the reason the person wrote. Their location is asked only at those two moments, never in between.

## Daily checks

Twice a day: the opening check by 9:00 and the closing check by 18:00.

1. Open **Daily checks** and choose **Opening check** or **Closing check**.
2. Each line shows what was found. Tick OK, or Problem with a note.
3. Press **Save the opening check** (or **Save the closing check**). You can save it again.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-03-daily-checks-desktop-be06d6c0.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 820; address: carmacars.ca/va/checks; pins: 1 6.5 15.4, 2 44.7 42.0, 3 64.2 94.0")

## Check a car out or in

Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in from the booking.

1. On a confirmed booking press **Check in (pickup)**; on a booking on rent, **Check out (return)**. Today lists the ones due, each with its button.
2. The checklist field staff use opens: readings (km and fuel or charge), the photo set with the plate and the gauges, damage close-ups and both signatures.
3. Afterwards press **Photo report**: times, Late by, kilometres, fuel, photos and the return charges. Fleet waives a charge with **Waive** and a reason.

## Photo reviews after a return

After each return, the field photo set waits under **Photo reviews**. Compare it with the pickup set. Press **Review done**, or **Ask for a re-shoot** if a photo is missing or unclear.

## Similar cars

A possible duplicate never keeps a car off the site: it shows on the car''s checklist until you decide. Only Same car takes it off.

1. Each flag shows the car, what it looks like (same VIN, plate, photo or specs) and the other car.
2. Compare the permit, the plate and the photos.
3. Press **Not a duplicate** with a note when they are different cars, or **Same car** when they are.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-06-similar-cars-desktop-562b0382.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 460; address: carmacars.ca/va/similar-cars; pins: 1 23.6 30.4, 3 94.8 30.4")

## Rates and kilometres

From a listing, press **The car and its rates**, or open the car from Field jobs and its **Rates & fees** tab.

1. Type the rates an Admin set. Only the daily rate is needed; the others follow from it when empty. The weekend rate is a price per day for each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday.
2. Keep **Use the defaults** for the kilometres, or choose **Custom for this car**.
3. Check What renters pay under the fields, then press **Save the rates**. Rates, kilometres and deposit save together.
4. **Price limits**, below: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts, read only. Offers, promo codes and lead-time pricing stay between them; an Admin or the owner changes them, and only an Admin allows one booking outside them.

## Listings and covering plates

1. Open **Listings**. A draft waiting shows Needs review. Open it.
2. The copy is written by itself (change a line only if you must: it is then kept). Check the photos: on each public photo, cover the plate or mark it not visible.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-05-listings-desktop-d2672e0a.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 340; address: carmacars.ca/va/listings; pins: 1 54.5 49.1")

3. The listing''s Steps to go live says what is next: 1 Photos, 2 Cover plates, 3 Review, 4 Live on the site, each with its button. The plates are checked by themselves: a plate found is blurred (Covered automatically), a photo with none is marked No plate visible, and a photo the check is not sure of stays Plate not checked. **Undo** on a photo takes an automatic decision back. To cover one yourself, press **Cover the plate**: the editor opens under the photo; **Suggest the plate** asks for the box. A photo filed under the wrong shot: **Remove** under it on the Photos card, then take the right one.
4. Drag over a plate to draw a box; drag a box to move it, its corner to resize it.
5. Only a plate that is there is blurred, tight to the plate with a soft edge, so no character can be read (nothing is drawn on it; a car with no front plate gets no box there), then **Save the covered photo**.
6. No plate in the shot? **No plate visible on this photo**.

![](/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-phone-95d5afd2.jpg "phone; size: 390 776; pins: 3 52.6 78.9, 4 50.0 43.8, 5 61.5 62.1, 6 43.1 92.3")

> Watch out: The plate check never holds a car back: a photo whose plate is not checked stays private, and goes public by itself once it is covered or marked. The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately.

## Missing angles and short videos

On a listing, below First photo (Sales: in the Marketplace kit of the car).

1. A required angle with no photo? Fleet and Sales press **Make** and the angle (for example **Make Rear**): the image model makes the view from the car''s photos, within its free daily use. Check it is the same car, then **Approve** or **Reject**.
2. Press **Make a short video** for a 9:16 video of the car''s approved photos with the price and the call to action. Keep the tab in front until it says Saved, then **Download** it or schedule it on your Marketing page (Scheduled posts).

> Watch out: An AI view shows on the site after the real photos, labelled AI view. It is never the cover and never damage or condition evidence. A real photo always replaces it.

## Publish now

Customer service and fleet publish a car themselves; nothing has to be finished first.

1. Open the car from Listings or Field jobs. Its listing says why it is not on the site yet; press **Publish now**. With no rates yet it uses the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults).
2. What is still open (paperwork, details, photos, No VIN yet for a car added by its plate, a possible duplicate) shows as warnings after Publish now and on the car. None of them stops publishing.
3. New cars with their rates usually go on the site by themselves (Publish new cars automatically, on by default). A car taken off the site by staff waits for Publish now.

> Tip: A car not on the fleet insurance policy yet can be requested, offered and paid for, but never handed over until the insurer confirms it. Requests and offers for such a car show a warning.

## Calendar sync with Turo and other platforms

**Cars** > **Calendar sync**: a car listed on Turo or Getaround must never be booked twice.

1. Turo has no calendar link: Turo''s trip emails come in by themselves, find their car by themselves (Turo car number, plate, VIN, year, make, model, trim, colour, what earlier emails taught) and block it with the turnaround. Nothing to set up per car.
2. An email the reader cannot place waits as "Which car is this?": press **Which car is this?** and press the right car (best guesses first). It is remembered for that car''s next emails. If the dates or trip number are missing: **Add as a Turo trip** (choose the car, check the dates) or **Dismiss**. A trip whose email did not come: **Add a Turo trip** on the car.
3. Each Turo trip shows the guest''s name and phone when Turo''s email includes them. Contact a Turo guest only about their trip, never with promotions.
4. Turo cannot read our calendar: under "Block on Turo", block each CarmaCars booking on the car''s Turo calendar, then press **Done on Turo**. Dates that changed or a booking cancelled here show the dates to free on Turo.
5. Getaround, Google Calendar or another platform with a calendar (iCal) link: open **Add a calendar link**, choose the platform, paste it and press **Add the link**. Copy the car''s CarmaCars link for that platform with **Copy** and paste it into the platform''s calendar import.
6. A double booking raises an urgent task for you and an email: move, swap or cancel one trip. A link that stops working raises a task after 3 failed reads: copy it from the platform again.

### Add the photos and readings
A pickup or return recorded with the details later gives Fleet the task **Add the photos and readings for CC-...**. Open the booking and press **Add the check-in (or check-out) photos and readings**: the usual checklist opens without the ready check or the renter''s signature. Take the photos, the odometer, fuel, keys (and cleanliness at a return), sign and save. The task closes by itself; it cannot be closed by hand before.

## Bookings now

**Rentals** > **Bookings** opens on Now for fleet and customer service: the cars out with their renter and due-back countdown, coming back today and tomorrow (overdue first, in red), going out in the next 72 hours with what is ready, the money due in 7 days and the free cars. It refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. A booking listed as **Out (pickup not recorded)** left without a check-in: press **Mark picked up**, then add the photos, km and fuel from the task. A car overdue or due back today has **Returned** (here, on Today and at the top of the booking): give the return time (now, or earlier; lateness follows it) and the km and fuel if known. The overdue messages stop and the task for the photos is yours. The search above it finds any booking.

### The renter says the car is back

An urgent To do "The renter says the car is back" means the renter pressed **I''ve returned the car** on an overdue booking. Their overdue notices are paused. Open the booking, check the car (place, tracker, the renter''s photos), then press **Confirm** (correct the odometer, fuel or time first if needed; the trip is completed) or **Deny** with the reason (the renter is told and the notices start again).

**Start a listing** takes the VIN from the car: **Scan the barcode** in the door frame or under the windshield, or **Photo of the VIN**.

**Add photos** on a listing takes any number of photos at once, in any order: each is sorted to its shot. A photo that fits no shot goes in with **Extra outside photos** or **Extra inside and detail photos**; drag the extras into their order in the review and press **Save the order**. 10 photos and one outside photo complete the listing. Outside photos are framed big on the studio floor with a shadow under the tyres; a watermark or caption at a photo''s edge is cut off by itself. **Cover the plate** opens with the plate box suggested: check it and save. A car small in the frame, or no model name behind it: press **Frame the outside photos again** (then check the plates again). A bad cut-out (a mirror missing, background left): press **Edit the cut-out**, erase or restore with the brush, move or size the car on the studio, then **Save as a new version**. The version before is kept; if the car did not move, the plate check carries over. Every photo gets a light touch-up by itself; tick **Use original colours** under a photo to make it again without it. Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom: a real photographed dealership room when one is stored (the car about 70% of the width, its wheels on the floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection; no logo on a real wall), else the dark drawn showroom (the logo on the wall, the model''s name behind the car on the cover). A cut-out that is not clean enough is never placed in a room: the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual), noted on the photo. A car still on the black studio: press **Apply showroom to this car**; **Listings** > **Apply showroom to every car** does every car. Under a photo, **Redo** makes it again and **Back to the original** puts back the version before. **Marketing photos** on a listing makes copies in other scenes for Marketplace and social posts (choose a scene or **Mix: a different scene on each photo**, then **Make the marketing set**); the website''s photos stay as they are. **First photo** on a listing chooses what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit: **Plain car**, **With a model** (the image model''s car-show photo, a fully clothed adult model beside the car) or **Flyer** (the price a day from the live rates, the call to action and the logo on the cover). Switch any time; until the chosen one is made the plain cover shows.
## One screen, many photos (release 28)

**Import photos from a Google Drive link** on a listing adds the photos of a public Drive folder to the car, sorted and processed like Add photos. **Listings** > **Import photos from Drive** reads a whole folder of folders (one per make, then per car), proposes the car for each folder, and imports once you confirm the table. The page follows the import and ends with what was imported, skipped and failed, and why. The same Drive file is never added twice. Customer service can import into a car whose listing is already started; Fleet and Admin can start one.

Check-in and check-out are one screen on the booking page: the time, km, fuel, many photos at once (tag angles if you like) and a note. The renter''s own photos join the same report; each photo shows who took it. On a car''s page, record **Pickup from owner** and **Return to owner** with photos: the owner sees them.

## Repair costs on a car

On a car''s page, **Kickbacks and repairs** lists its repair costs and the kickbacks partners paid on it. **Add a repair cost**: the date, the shop or another vendor, what was done, the amount and tax, who paid (CarmaCars, the owner or the insurer), the claim and a photo or PDF of the receipt.

## When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)
On the booking page, **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking''s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: **Ask to record a past trip** with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.

## Incident cards (release 34)
**Cars**, then **Incident cards**, prints the card for the visor or the glovebox: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, our support and roadside numbers, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. On a car''s page, **Incident card** prints that car; on the list, **Print all cars** prints every car, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks. Laminate it and put one in each car. The insurance policy on the card is set by an Admin; until it is, the card tells the renter to ask for the slip. No price is ever printed on it.

## Government forms (release 35)
The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner''s car are on the owner''s page and the car''s page, under **Government forms**. Open a form, press **Change a value**, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and **Save**: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under **Versions** with their downloads. **Back to the records** undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. **Make again** keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. **Owners**, then **Government forms**, opens the forms'' mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under **Earlier mappings**. Only the boxes are filled: the form''s own text and layout never change.

## Odometer and fuel at every check-in and check-out

Every check-in and check-out on one screen asks for two photos besides the others:

1. **Photo of the dashboard**: the odometer and the fuel gauge, from the camera roll or the camera. The site reads it and asks, for example, "Odometer 45,210 km, fuel 3/4: correct?". Press **Yes, correct**, or **No, I will type it** and type the odometer and pick the fuel in eighths.
2. **Selfie in front of the car**: taken now with the camera, never from the camera roll. A selfie without a fresh capture time is noted on the report for you to check; it never stops the check-in.

At the return the site compares with the pickup: km driven, km over the included allowance and the fuel difference. The extra km (the booking''s rate per km) are added to the booking by themselves. The fuel is prepared as a suggested line: the car''s tank x the fuel missing x the local pump price of its grade x 1.25, plus the $20 refuelling fee (an electric car: battery kWh x the charge missing x $0.40, plus the fee). You and Finance confirm it on the deposit review; no card is charged by it. The photo report shows both dashboard photos side by side with the readings and these charges.

## Change the car of a confirmed booking

A car with a problem before pickup? On the booking, press **Change the car**, choose a car free for the dates and say why. The price comes from the new car''s rate sheet; more to pay is left open for the renter, less becomes a refund for approval. The jobs move to the new car and the renter gets one email.

## An accident reported by a renter

A renter can report an accident from the accident card on their booking. It opens the incident with its first-response steps and your To do, and sends you an urgent alert (on duty) and to Admins: what happened, where, the photos and videos, the other party, the police report number, whether anyone is hurt and whether the car can be driven. Call the renter at once; a car that cannot be driven is already out of service with its calendar blocked.
## Payments and calls (release 35)
Fleet takes payments on a booking''s **Money** tab: text or email a pay link, charge the saved card when the renter agreed, hold the deposit, or record cash or an e-Transfer received (within your single limit; Finance gets a To do to check it). Refunds, captures and voids stay with Finance and the Admins.

Calls and texts about pickups, returns, deliveries and cars on rent come to Fleet first: the caller pop-up shows them, and **More fleet** > **Calls and texts** is your inbox. A car late back has **Returning now** on its late panel: press it when the renter says they are on the way, and they get no more overdue reminders for that return time.

The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner''s car are on the owner''s page and the car''s page, under **Government forms**. Open a form, press **Change a value**, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and **Save**: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under **Versions** with their downloads. **Back to the records** undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. **Make again** keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. **Owners**, then **Government forms**, opens the forms'' mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under **Earlier mappings**. Only the boxes are filled: the form''s own text and layout never change. The owner signs each form on screen: the page shows **Owner''s signature** beside the form (who, when, the version) and **Download the print-ready form** has no signature on it. A value changed after signing shows **Changed since signed** and the owner is asked to sign again.

## Close ended trips

A back-dated close sends the renter no email or text. Fleet gets a To do when a trip is still open 2 hours after its return time, and the morning digest lists how many are open.

**Field jobs** > **Close ended trips**: tick the trips that ended and were never closed, mark them returned on time or late (with the time), choose the deposit decision (deduct the balance owed, deduct the late fee, or release in full) and press **Close**. An expired card hold is settled by expiry at once. An Admin presses Release for the rest. On a booking, an expired hold after the return has **Mark settled (released by expiry)**.

## The primary photo (release 43)

The first photo of a car is always its front exterior. When a car shows the flag **Primary photo is not exterior** on the Vehicles list, its best outside photo is not on the site yet: add or approve one. **Redo photos with Gemini** on the car page makes every photo of the car again from its original with Gemini (the background replaced by the showroom, inside photos cleaned up and sharp, a plate blurred only where the car has one, tight to the plate) and generates the angles the car has no photo of, marked **AI generated**. A photo the check refuses three times stays off the site, flagged. Fleet also has the **Photo standard** card on Listings: each car''s photos at the standard, AI angles, flagged photos and last run, with **Redo this car now** and **Redo every car**. The whole fleet is brought to the standard by itself every 5 minutes, newest listed cars first.

## Field applicant calls (release 35)

Field applicants who pass the AI interview book a 10-minute interview date in the hour before the weekly townhall. **Field applicant calls** on your home page lists the six slots and who took each one.

## Value and fuel on the car page (release 35)

**Cars** > the car > **Overview** > **Value and fuel**:

- **Canadian Black Book value** (with the date checked) or an **Estimated value (when no Black Book)**: renters on credit card coverage are checked against it. With neither, they go to staff review.
- **Tank (litres)** and **Fuel grade** (regular, premium or diesel; empty uses the class), or **Battery (kWh)** for an electric car. Empty uses the default in Program settings.

Press **Save**. Customer service sees the card; only Fleet and an Admin change it.

## Shifts, delivery and fuel (release 35)

- The shift board shows each field person''s availability, the standing weekly shifts, who is under the minimum, and for each slot the people to ask. A shift nobody claimed 48 hours ahead alerts you.
- You can approve new staff at the fourth onboarding step, or reject with a reason.
- Delivery is priced by distance from 1940 Eglinton Ave E; the fuel line at the return is a suggestion from the tank and the pump price for you to check on the deposit review.
- An Admin can delete a car that has only test bookings; a car with a real booking stays.

## Calls first, texts after (release 37)

Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.

1. Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.
2. **Call before you text.** On a lead, a renter or a booking, **Call** is the first button and **Text** the second.
3. A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.
4. On your To do and on **Unanswered**, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.

## A lead you handle on a call (release 37)

When you answer or place a call with a lead, add a note on it, or create it from a call, the lead is yours for a limited time (15 minutes, as a Sales claim; an Admin can change it in **Settings** > **Sales**). Every call you handle adds the time again.

- Sales see **Being handled by** your first name and your function with the time, on the lead and in every list. They cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome meanwhile, and **Next lead** skips it.
- Another customer service or Fleet person can still work it; their call or note takes the hold over.
- When it ends, the lead goes back to the salesperson who had a claim on it or who brought it, else to the open list. An Admin can **Release hold** earlier.
- A booking made from the lead is credited as always: customer service and Fleet get no sales commission for it.
- Nobody who has not finished onboarding holds a lead.

## Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)

**Start the check-in (pickup)** and **Start the check-out (return)** on the booking, and **Check in** or **Check out** on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:

1. Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.
2. What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car''s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.
3. Photos are one tap each: **Take this photo** always shows the next angle.
4. What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.
5. The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example "Next: Odometer") and takes you to it. When everything is in, press **Hand over the keys** or **Complete the return**.

Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.

**Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)** is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.

## A late return is a choice (release 42)

A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows **Late return** with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:

1. **Charge as an extension**: every started day late at the booking''s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.
2. **Charge extra days**: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.
3. **Charge the late return fee**: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).
4. **Charge a custom amount**: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.
5. **Waive it**: no charge, with the reason.

Press **Save the late return charge**. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.

Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do "Late return: choose the charge". Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.

> Good to know: A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do "Late return: approve the charge" and press **Approve as asked**, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.

## Every view generated from the car''s photos (release 47)

Every car now shows nine views generated by Gemini (in the order of the sample photos: front three-quarter first, then side, rear three-quarter, front, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats, trunk), made from the car''s own photos, the sample view of the angle and the stock photo of the model, then cut out on the dealership background. A car with no listing photo of that side uses its check-in and check-out photos as references (never shown on the site). A view the check refuses three times is flagged (release 50: only views that passed are on the site). The real photos stay on the car''s record. On **Photo standard**, **Generated set** shows each car''s views made out of nine; **Redo this car now** makes them again.

## Picked up, deposit pending (release 48)
When the renter cannot place the deposit hold at the pickup (the card is declined, the bank wants a call) and the car must go, you can let it go with the deposit owed. On the job, under the deposit line, open **Let the car go with the deposit owed**, say why, and go on with the check-in. On a booking, **Record the pickup now** has the box **Deposit not taken yet: let the car go owing it, because**, and the check-in panel has **Deposit not taken: let the car go owing it**. The booking then shows **Deposit pending $X** everywhere. Each morning the renter''s saved card is tried once; if that fails, the renter gets the deposit link by text (or email). After 48 hours an Admin gets a To do. You do nothing more: once the deposit is taken the chip changes by itself.

## Studio renders (release 48)

- Every car''s first photos are studio views made from its own photos, the front three-quarter first. Its real outside photos come after them, cut out on the same background.
- Renders go live by themselves. You get "Studio photos live" in your next digest: check the colour, wheels and trim, and that the side profile faces left.
- Something is off: open the car, **Studio photos**, then **Make again** or **Take off the site**.
- To render every published car now: **Listings**, **Photo standard**, **Render every published car**.
## Evidence for every fee (release 48)

Every fee is charged only with its evidence. On a booking''s Money tab, **Evidence for every fee** lists each fee with what it needs, what was found by itself and what is missing.

1. A fee that Needs evidence has a To do in the Fleet queue (titled "Field:" when the field staff capture it) saying exactly what to take: the guided cleanliness photos and description, a damage close-up, photos of where the car was left, a receipt.
2. Press **Attach evidence** on the line, choose what it is and add the photo or PDF (or a note). It is checked again at once; the To do closes by itself.
3. The return checklist does not complete a return that is not clean without 3 guided photos and a description. The smoking or cleaning fee it drafts waits for your review of the return, then Finance.
4. **Add a return charge**: non-return, improper return, theft recovery, a flat tire or a roadside call-out (cost plus $50; not for a mechanical fault that is not the renter''s). Add each actual cost with its receipt.

## Tracker events and pound flags (release 48)

On the **Fleet map**, below the map and the alerts. It shows once an Admin has turned Tracker events on.

**Tracker events** lists each event with its evidence: when, the car and booking, the speed and the map point, the charge and the clause, and who was told. One event per car, kind and 30 minutes. The renter and the car''s owner are told by themselves; you do not need to message them about the event itself.

- A speeding record over 180, 220 or 300 km/h carries one charge, at the highest limit reached in the event. An Admin or Finance presses **Charge**; you do not.
- Harsh driving and a speed over the alert level are a heads-up only.
- A Tracker unplugged or tampered with, or a car outside Ontario: call the renter.

**A car that leaves Ontario or Canada**: you get an alert, an email and a text at once. Call the renter. For Canada there is an urgent To do: leaving Canada needs written approval, so with no approval and no answer, tell an Admin.

**Pound flags**: a car parked at a known pound.

1. You get an urgent To do and alert. Open **Pound flags**: the lot''s phone and hours are on the row.
2. Call the lot to confirm the car is there and what releases it. Call the renter. Keep every receipt.
3. Press **Record the path** and choose: the non-return charge with the costs, the theft recovery charge with the costs (add the police report number), **Recovered, nothing to charge**, or **Not a pound**. Write what happened in a sentence.

> Tip: Not sure which charge applies? Non-return is for a car not back after the final late notice. Theft recovery is for a car stolen, or recovered by the police or a repossession. Ask an Admin when it is neither.

**Pound lots** are listed below, read only. Tell an Admin when a lot''s phone or hours are wrong, or a pound is missing.

## One look: studio renders only (release 50)

Once a car has a studio view that passed, the site shows its studio views: each car is cut out and put on the same dealership background with the CarmaCars sign, one image exactly the same for every view of every car. The views are the sample photos'' angles in the same order (front three-quarter, side, rear three-quarter, front, rear, dashboard, seats, wheel); a view the car has no photo of is made by Gemini from its other photos. Its real outside photos follow, cut out the same way. Where the home page, a hero or a sample card showed a sample car, a real car takes its place only as a cutout, never its full photo. A car with none yet shows its photos as before. Its own photos stay on the car''s record. **Photo standard** > **Studio grid** shows every car''s views side by side with **Live**, **Gate refused** or **Flagged** and why.

## Sign first, then cars

An owner''s cars move only once the owner has signed their agreement and each car''s Schedule A entry. On the owner''s page, Agreements before cars lists what is missing and who it waits on; Send reminder emails the owner with the in-app notice and the push. A fleet supplier can add cars from a list of VINs too, with each car''s tier and plate.

A confirmed booking whose pickup was never recorded shows as "Pickup not recorded, car presumed out": record the handover (or the return, or a no-show) from the booking. Until then the car takes no new offer.

## Check-in visits (release 50)

A renter on a long rental (28 days or more, a long-term weekly rental, or a rideshare driver) is asked to bring the car in about once a month. It is a suggestion, never a requirement and never a fee.

1. Open **Checks** > **Check-in visits**. **Booked** comes first, then **Due**, **Overdue** (soft: a friendly call is fine) and **Done**. You get an email and a notice when a renter picks a time, and the morning of a visit.
2. Press **Do the visit**: take the five photos (front, rear, left side, right side, odometer), type the odometer, say whether there is new damage (where and what), the tire tread in mm, whether the fluids look right and any warning light, and notes.
3. Press **Save the visit**. The reading and the tread go into the car''s maintenance, which shows the next service due. Anything to look after (a service due, tread under 3 mm, fluids, a warning light) becomes a Fleet To do; damage is logged on the Damage tab with an Admin To do.
4. **Book a time for the renter** picks an office slot for them; **Skip this month** needs the reason; **Start a visit now** is for a renter who drops by.

On the booking page, **Check-in visits** shows the next one and turns them on for any rental, off for this one, or back to the rule.


## Log an expense from the receipt

**Maintenance** > **Expenses**, on a phone or a computer.

1. Press **Take a photo** (or **Upload photos**). Add more photos of the same receipt if it is long.
2. The amount before tax, the HST, the date, the shop, the category and the car are read from the photo. Check each one; anything not read clearly is said above the fields.
3. Who pays: the car''s owner (it goes on their next statement as a cost, with the receipt in their documents, and they get an email) or CarmaCars (a company expense on the car). Tick **I paid with my own money** to be paid back.
4. Press **Save**. The expense is listed under Logged from receipts, with its photos.

## Ownership documents in bulk

**More fleet** > **Listings** > **Ownership documents**

1. Press **Choose the files** and pick every permit photo or PDF at once.
2. Each file is read for its VIN and plate and filed on the car with that VIN. A file whose plate matches a car but whose VIN does not waits below with that car chosen: check it and press **File it on this car**. The owner sees it in their portal under Documents and gets an email.
3. A file that matched no car waits under Waiting for a car: open the file, choose the car and press **File it on this car**, or set it aside with the reason. Fleet has a To do while any file waits.

## Add old photos
**Add old photos** (a tab beside **Check-in visits**: Fleet under **Checks**, customer service under its **Check-in visits** link) puts photos of an earlier check-in or check-out on its booking: every booking picked up or returned in the last 60 days (`old_photos_days`), searchable by plate, car, renter or number. Choose **Check-in** or **Check-out** and pick many photos at once; they upload in the background and resume after a bad signal. **A pile of photos** groups a pile by the time each was taken (`old_photos_group_minutes`), reads the plate where it can, and suggests the check-in or check-out within `old_photos_match_hours` of it; one tap confirms a group. The photos show on the booking''s photo report as "added later by" the person, with the time they were taken. No email or text goes to the renter or the owner, and the booking does not change.
', 'Fleet', 'Field jobs, daily checks, photo reviews, similar cars and listings.',
  'You keep the cars moving: field jobs, daily checks, photo reviews after returns, and the listings with their duplicate check and plate covering. There is no commission for Fleet, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Field jobs, Field hours, Daily checks, Photo reviews, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Find a renter and Scorecard.

## Schedule field jobs

Every confirmed booking gets its handover (or delivery) and return (or pickup) jobs by itself, at the booking''s times and place, and put on a shift: the shift covering its time, or that day''s (see Shifts and who gets a job). The people on the shift share its jobs, least busy first. You check and change them.

1. Jobs, next three days: each with its place, its shift, its field staff and whether they acknowledged it. "Made from the booking" marks the ones made by themselves; when the booking moves, they move too, unless you changed them.
2. Change a job with **To a shift** (another shift), **Assign** or **Reassign** (a field person on a shift that day when the day has shifts, or an Admin), **Move** (time and place) or **Cancel**.
3. Handovers and returns without a job (when the automatic jobs are off, or one was cancelled) are listed first: press **Schedule**, the place filled in from the booking.
4. An Admin turns the automatic jobs or the assignment off in Settings > Program.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-02-field-jobs-desktop-8e721230.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 565; address: carmacars.ca/va/fleet; pins: 1 17.9 51.3")


### Shifts in your Google Calendar

At the bottom of **Field jobs** (and on your **Profile**), **Add shifts, townhalls and interviews to Google Calendar** gives you a private link with every field shift, 14 days back to 60 days ahead: who claimed it or Open, the tasks and a link to it, and the weekly townhall. Press **Make my calendar link**, then **Add to Google Calendar** and **Add** in Google. Google refreshes it every few hours on its own. **Regenerate link** stops the old link; **Turn off** stops it.

## Shifts and who gets a job

Field staff take their shifts from the schedule published by itself: every hour, up to 14 days ahead, from the shift template in Program settings (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day), only forward from the latest shift already published. A handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own (90 minutes either side). A job is given by itself only to a field person who passed the academy and holds a shift that day, and work lands only on days with shifts.

1. On **Field jobs**, **Shifts, next seven days** shows each day and how many people are on a shift, and each shift its jobs (**Jobs on it**). A shift with jobs and nobody on it is marked; within 24 hours of its start you get an alert and a To do, once.
2. Need more? Press **Publish shifts**: the first day''s start and end, how many people, and for how many days the same hours repeat. A shift you cancel is not published again. Field staff take them on their phones.
3. **Add a person** puts someone on a shift and **Remove** takes them off. A person who has not passed the academy cannot take shifts or be given a job.
4. A shift nobody claimed keeps its jobs: field staff see them when they look for shifts to claim, and the one who claims it gets them. A shift given up or swapped takes its jobs along; a cancelled shift sends them to another shift.
5. Work due on a day with no shifts moves to the day before when it is known in advance, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day. The job shows its planned day and keeps the booking''s real time; the renter''s times never change. A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning: cover it, or move the booking time.
6. **Unassign** takes a job off its person and its shift; tick **Tell them** only if they should know. The Admins can be given a job too (no shift needed).

## Missing check-ins and check-outs

1. **Missing check-in and check-out** on Field jobs lists every past rental without its photos and readings (odometer, fuel, damage photos), closed bookings included.
2. Press **Give to field staff** and choose the person: they add the photos and readings from their Today page.

## Fleet map

At the top of **Field jobs**: every car on the map with its renter, booking, due-back time and state, the alerts, and the trips by booking, the same as the Admin''s. Every staff member sees the cars'' positions: customer service, Sales and Finance open the same map from **Find a car** (**Car map**), read only, and field staff under **Map**. Every car page and booking page shows **Where the car is**: moving or parked, when it last reported and **Open on the map**, or **No tracker yet**. Only Admins and fleet staff press **Seen** on an alert. Each owner sees where their own cars are, never the renter or the booking.

1. Press a car for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery and the trip under way.
2. An alert (speeding, left Ontario or the zone, still driving after the return time, low or unplugged tracker, not reporting) also comes to your bell and as an urgent phone alert. Call the renter, then press **Seen**.
3. A car still driving after its return time: call, send the late notice and offer a paid extension, as for any late return.

## Field hours

Field staff clock in and out on their phones. You see who is clocked in and every shift of the two-week pay period, and you fix what they cannot.

1. Open **Field hours**. **Clocked in now** lists who is on, since when. **Earlier period** and **Later period** move between pay periods.
2. Someone forgot to clock out: press **Clock out for them**, set the time they finished and write the reason.
3. Someone forgot to clock in, or a time is wrong: **Add hours** enters a shift, **Change** fixes one and **Remove** takes one out. Each needs a reason; the change is kept in a log with what it was before.
4. Once an Admin approves the pay run of a period, its shifts are locked: ask the Admin. You see hours only, not rates or pay.

### Where they clocked in
The hours list shows where each person clocked in and out: a map link and the distance from the lot. A clock in or out over 500 m away, or with the location refused, is shown in bold with the reason the person wrote. Their location is asked only at those two moments, never in between.

## Daily checks

Twice a day: the opening check by 9:00 and the closing check by 18:00.

1. Open **Daily checks** and choose **Opening check** or **Closing check**.
2. Each line shows what was found. Tick OK, or Problem with a note.
3. Press **Save the opening check** (or **Save the closing check**). You can save it again.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-03-daily-checks-desktop-be06d6c0.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 820; address: carmacars.ca/va/checks; pins: 1 6.5 15.4, 2 44.7 42.0, 3 64.2 94.0")

## Check a car out or in

Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in from the booking.

1. On a confirmed booking press **Check in (pickup)**; on a booking on rent, **Check out (return)**. Today lists the ones due, each with its button.
2. The checklist field staff use opens: readings (km and fuel or charge), the photo set with the plate and the gauges, damage close-ups and both signatures.
3. Afterwards press **Photo report**: times, Late by, kilometres, fuel, photos and the return charges. Fleet waives a charge with **Waive** and a reason.

## Photo reviews after a return

After each return, the field photo set waits under **Photo reviews**. Compare it with the pickup set. Press **Review done**, or **Ask for a re-shoot** if a photo is missing or unclear.

## Similar cars

A possible duplicate never keeps a car off the site: it shows on the car''s checklist until you decide. Only Same car takes it off.

1. Each flag shows the car, what it looks like (same VIN, plate, photo or specs) and the other car.
2. Compare the permit, the plate and the photos.
3. Press **Not a duplicate** with a note when they are different cars, or **Same car** when they are.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-06-similar-cars-desktop-562b0382.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 460; address: carmacars.ca/va/similar-cars; pins: 1 23.6 30.4, 3 94.8 30.4")

## Rates and kilometres

From a listing, press **The car and its rates**, or open the car from Field jobs and its **Rates & fees** tab.

1. Type the rates an Admin set. Only the daily rate is needed; the others follow from it when empty. The weekend rate is a price per day for each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday.
2. Keep **Use the defaults** for the kilometres, or choose **Custom for this car**.
3. Check What renters pay under the fields, then press **Save the rates**. Rates, kilometres and deposit save together.
4. **Price limits**, below: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts, read only. Offers, promo codes and lead-time pricing stay between them; an Admin or the owner changes them, and only an Admin allows one booking outside them.

## Listings and covering plates

1. Open **Listings**. A draft waiting shows Needs review. Open it.
2. The copy is written by itself (change a line only if you must: it is then kept). Check the photos: on each public photo, cover the plate or mark it not visible.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-05-listings-desktop-d2672e0a.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 340; address: carmacars.ca/va/listings; pins: 1 54.5 49.1")

3. The listing''s Steps to go live says what is next: 1 Photos, 2 Cover plates, 3 Review, 4 Live on the site, each with its button. The plates are checked by themselves: a plate found is blurred (Covered automatically), a photo with none is marked No plate visible, and a photo the check is not sure of stays Plate not checked. **Undo** on a photo takes an automatic decision back. To cover one yourself, press **Cover the plate**: the editor opens under the photo; **Suggest the plate** asks for the box. A photo filed under the wrong shot: **Remove** under it on the Photos card, then take the right one.
4. Drag over a plate to draw a box; drag a box to move it, its corner to resize it.
5. Only a plate that is there is blurred, tight to the plate with a soft edge, so no character can be read (nothing is drawn on it; a car with no front plate gets no box there), then **Save the covered photo**.
6. No plate in the shot? **No plate visible on this photo**.

![](/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-phone-95d5afd2.jpg "phone; size: 390 776; pins: 3 52.6 78.9, 4 50.0 43.8, 5 61.5 62.1, 6 43.1 92.3")

> Watch out: The plate check never holds a car back: a photo whose plate is not checked stays private, and goes public by itself once it is covered or marked. The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately.

## Missing angles and short videos

On a listing, below First photo (Sales: in the Marketplace kit of the car).

1. A required angle with no photo? Fleet and Sales press **Make** and the angle (for example **Make Rear**): the image model makes the view from the car''s photos, within its free daily use. Check it is the same car, then **Approve** or **Reject**.
2. Press **Make a short video** for a 9:16 video of the car''s approved photos with the price and the call to action. Keep the tab in front until it says Saved, then **Download** it or schedule it on your Marketing page (Scheduled posts).

> Watch out: An AI view shows on the site after the real photos, labelled AI view. It is never the cover and never damage or condition evidence. A real photo always replaces it.

## Publish now

Customer service and fleet publish a car themselves; nothing has to be finished first.

1. Open the car from Listings or Field jobs. Its listing says why it is not on the site yet; press **Publish now**. With no rates yet it uses the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults).
2. What is still open (paperwork, details, photos, No VIN yet for a car added by its plate, a possible duplicate) shows as warnings after Publish now and on the car. None of them stops publishing.
3. New cars with their rates usually go on the site by themselves (Publish new cars automatically, on by default). A car taken off the site by staff waits for Publish now.

> Tip: A car not on the fleet insurance policy yet can be requested, offered and paid for, but never handed over until the insurer confirms it. Requests and offers for such a car show a warning.

## Calendar sync with Turo and other platforms

**Cars** > **Calendar sync**: a car listed on Turo or Getaround must never be booked twice.

1. Turo has no calendar link: Turo''s trip emails come in by themselves, find their car by themselves (Turo car number, plate, VIN, year, make, model, trim, colour, what earlier emails taught) and block it with the turnaround. Nothing to set up per car.
2. An email the reader cannot place waits as "Which car is this?": press **Which car is this?** and press the right car (best guesses first). It is remembered for that car''s next emails. If the dates or trip number are missing: **Add as a Turo trip** (choose the car, check the dates) or **Dismiss**. A trip whose email did not come: **Add a Turo trip** on the car.
3. Each Turo trip shows the guest''s name and phone when Turo''s email includes them. Contact a Turo guest only about their trip, never with promotions.
4. Turo cannot read our calendar: under "Block on Turo", block each CarmaCars booking on the car''s Turo calendar, then press **Done on Turo**. Dates that changed or a booking cancelled here show the dates to free on Turo.
5. Getaround, Google Calendar or another platform with a calendar (iCal) link: open **Add a calendar link**, choose the platform, paste it and press **Add the link**. Copy the car''s CarmaCars link for that platform with **Copy** and paste it into the platform''s calendar import.
6. A double booking raises an urgent task for you and an email: move, swap or cancel one trip. A link that stops working raises a task after 3 failed reads: copy it from the platform again.

### Add the photos and readings
A pickup or return recorded with the details later gives Fleet the task **Add the photos and readings for CC-...**. Open the booking and press **Add the check-in (or check-out) photos and readings**: the usual checklist opens without the ready check or the renter''s signature. Take the photos, the odometer, fuel, keys (and cleanliness at a return), sign and save. The task closes by itself; it cannot be closed by hand before.

## Bookings now

**Rentals** > **Bookings** opens on Now for fleet and customer service: the cars out with their renter and due-back countdown, coming back today and tomorrow (overdue first, in red), going out in the next 72 hours with what is ready, the money due in 7 days and the free cars. It refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. A booking listed as **Out (pickup not recorded)** left without a check-in: press **Mark picked up**, then add the photos, km and fuel from the task. A car overdue or due back today has **Returned** (here, on Today and at the top of the booking): give the return time (now, or earlier; lateness follows it) and the km and fuel if known. The overdue messages stop and the task for the photos is yours. The search above it finds any booking.

### The renter says the car is back

An urgent To do "The renter says the car is back" means the renter pressed **I''ve returned the car** on an overdue booking. Their overdue notices are paused. Open the booking, check the car (place, tracker, the renter''s photos), then press **Confirm** (correct the odometer, fuel or time first if needed; the trip is completed) or **Deny** with the reason (the renter is told and the notices start again).

**Start a listing** takes the VIN from the car: **Scan the barcode** in the door frame or under the windshield, or **Photo of the VIN**.

**Add photos** on a listing takes any number of photos at once, in any order: each is sorted to its shot. A photo that fits no shot goes in with **Extra outside photos** or **Extra inside and detail photos**; drag the extras into their order in the review and press **Save the order**. 10 photos and one outside photo complete the listing. Outside photos are framed big on the studio floor with a shadow under the tyres; a watermark or caption at a photo''s edge is cut off by itself. **Cover the plate** opens with the plate box suggested: check it and save. A car small in the frame, or no model name behind it: press **Frame the outside photos again** (then check the plates again). A bad cut-out (a mirror missing, background left): press **Edit the cut-out**, erase or restore with the brush, move or size the car on the studio, then **Save as a new version**. The version before is kept; if the car did not move, the plate check carries over. Every photo gets a light touch-up by itself; tick **Use original colours** under a photo to make it again without it. Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom: a real photographed dealership room when one is stored (the car about 70% of the width, its wheels on the floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection; no logo on a real wall), else the dark drawn showroom (the logo on the wall, the model''s name behind the car on the cover). A cut-out that is not clean enough is never placed in a room: the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual), noted on the photo. A car still on the black studio: press **Apply showroom to this car**; **Listings** > **Apply showroom to every car** does every car. Under a photo, **Redo** makes it again and **Back to the original** puts back the version before. **Marketing photos** on a listing makes copies in other scenes for Marketplace and social posts (choose a scene or **Mix: a different scene on each photo**, then **Make the marketing set**); the website''s photos stay as they are. **First photo** on a listing chooses what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit: **Plain car**, **With a model** (the image model''s car-show photo, a fully clothed adult model beside the car) or **Flyer** (the price a day from the live rates, the call to action and the logo on the cover). Switch any time; until the chosen one is made the plain cover shows.
## One screen, many photos (release 28)

**Import photos from a Google Drive link** on a listing adds the photos of a public Drive folder to the car, sorted and processed like Add photos. **Listings** > **Import photos from Drive** reads a whole folder of folders (one per make, then per car), proposes the car for each folder, and imports once you confirm the table. The page follows the import and ends with what was imported, skipped and failed, and why. The same Drive file is never added twice. Customer service can import into a car whose listing is already started; Fleet and Admin can start one.

Check-in and check-out are one screen on the booking page: the time, km, fuel, many photos at once (tag angles if you like) and a note. The renter''s own photos join the same report; each photo shows who took it. On a car''s page, record **Pickup from owner** and **Return to owner** with photos: the owner sees them.

## Repair costs on a car

On a car''s page, **Kickbacks and repairs** lists its repair costs and the kickbacks partners paid on it. **Add a repair cost**: the date, the shop or another vendor, what was done, the amount and tax, who paid (CarmaCars, the owner or the insurer), the claim and a photo or PDF of the receipt.

## When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)
On the booking page, **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking''s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: **Ask to record a past trip** with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.

## Incident cards (release 34)
**Cars**, then **Incident cards**, prints the card for the visor or the glovebox: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, our support and roadside numbers, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. On a car''s page, **Incident card** prints that car; on the list, **Print all cars** prints every car, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks. Laminate it and put one in each car. The insurance policy on the card is set by an Admin; until it is, the card tells the renter to ask for the slip. No price is ever printed on it.

## Government forms (release 35)
The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner''s car are on the owner''s page and the car''s page, under **Government forms**. Open a form, press **Change a value**, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and **Save**: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under **Versions** with their downloads. **Back to the records** undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. **Make again** keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. **Owners**, then **Government forms**, opens the forms'' mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under **Earlier mappings**. Only the boxes are filled: the form''s own text and layout never change.

## Odometer and fuel at every check-in and check-out

Every check-in and check-out on one screen asks for two photos besides the others:

1. **Photo of the dashboard**: the odometer and the fuel gauge, from the camera roll or the camera. The site reads it and asks, for example, "Odometer 45,210 km, fuel 3/4: correct?". Press **Yes, correct**, or **No, I will type it** and type the odometer and pick the fuel in eighths.
2. **Selfie in front of the car**: taken now with the camera, never from the camera roll. A selfie without a fresh capture time is noted on the report for you to check; it never stops the check-in.

At the return the site compares with the pickup: km driven, km over the included allowance and the fuel difference. The extra km (the booking''s rate per km) are added to the booking by themselves. The fuel is prepared as a suggested line: the car''s tank x the fuel missing x the local pump price of its grade x 1.25, plus the $20 refuelling fee (an electric car: battery kWh x the charge missing x $0.40, plus the fee). You and Finance confirm it on the deposit review; no card is charged by it. The photo report shows both dashboard photos side by side with the readings and these charges.

## Change the car of a confirmed booking

A car with a problem before pickup? On the booking, press **Change the car**, choose a car free for the dates and say why. The price comes from the new car''s rate sheet; more to pay is left open for the renter, less becomes a refund for approval. The jobs move to the new car and the renter gets one email.

## An accident reported by a renter

A renter can report an accident from the accident card on their booking. It opens the incident with its first-response steps and your To do, and sends you an urgent alert (on duty) and to Admins: what happened, where, the photos and videos, the other party, the police report number, whether anyone is hurt and whether the car can be driven. Call the renter at once; a car that cannot be driven is already out of service with its calendar blocked.
## Payments and calls (release 35)
Fleet takes payments on a booking''s **Money** tab: text or email a pay link, charge the saved card when the renter agreed, hold the deposit, or record cash or an e-Transfer received (within your single limit; Finance gets a To do to check it). Refunds, captures and voids stay with Finance and the Admins.

Calls and texts about pickups, returns, deliveries and cars on rent come to Fleet first: the caller pop-up shows them, and **More fleet** > **Calls and texts** is your inbox. A car late back has **Returning now** on its late panel: press it when the renter says they are on the way, and they get no more overdue reminders for that return time.

The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner''s car are on the owner''s page and the car''s page, under **Government forms**. Open a form, press **Change a value**, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and **Save**: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under **Versions** with their downloads. **Back to the records** undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. **Make again** keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. **Owners**, then **Government forms**, opens the forms'' mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under **Earlier mappings**. Only the boxes are filled: the form''s own text and layout never change. The owner signs each form on screen: the page shows **Owner''s signature** beside the form (who, when, the version) and **Download the print-ready form** has no signature on it. A value changed after signing shows **Changed since signed** and the owner is asked to sign again.

## Close ended trips

A back-dated close sends the renter no email or text. Fleet gets a To do when a trip is still open 2 hours after its return time, and the morning digest lists how many are open.

**Field jobs** > **Close ended trips**: tick the trips that ended and were never closed, mark them returned on time or late (with the time), choose the deposit decision (deduct the balance owed, deduct the late fee, or release in full) and press **Close**. An expired card hold is settled by expiry at once. An Admin presses Release for the rest. On a booking, an expired hold after the return has **Mark settled (released by expiry)**.

## The primary photo (release 43)

The first photo of a car is always its front exterior. When a car shows the flag **Primary photo is not exterior** on the Vehicles list, its best outside photo is not on the site yet: add or approve one. **Redo photos with Gemini** on the car page makes every photo of the car again from its original with Gemini (the background replaced by the showroom, inside photos cleaned up and sharp, a plate blurred only where the car has one, tight to the plate) and generates the angles the car has no photo of, marked **AI generated**. A photo the check refuses three times stays off the site, flagged. Fleet also has the **Photo standard** card on Listings: each car''s photos at the standard, AI angles, flagged photos and last run, with **Redo this car now** and **Redo every car**. The whole fleet is brought to the standard by itself every 5 minutes, newest listed cars first.

## Field applicant calls (release 35)

Field applicants who pass the AI interview book a 10-minute interview date in the hour before the weekly townhall. **Field applicant calls** on your home page lists the six slots and who took each one.

## Value and fuel on the car page (release 35)

**Cars** > the car > **Overview** > **Value and fuel**:

- **Canadian Black Book value** (with the date checked) or an **Estimated value (when no Black Book)**: renters on credit card coverage are checked against it. With neither, they go to staff review.
- **Tank (litres)** and **Fuel grade** (regular, premium or diesel; empty uses the class), or **Battery (kWh)** for an electric car. Empty uses the default in Program settings.

Press **Save**. Customer service sees the card; only Fleet and an Admin change it.

## Shifts, delivery and fuel (release 35)

- The shift board shows each field person''s availability, the standing weekly shifts, who is under the minimum, and for each slot the people to ask. A shift nobody claimed 48 hours ahead alerts you.
- You can approve new staff at the fourth onboarding step, or reject with a reason.
- Delivery is priced by distance from 1940 Eglinton Ave E; the fuel line at the return is a suggestion from the tank and the pump price for you to check on the deposit review.
- An Admin can delete a car that has only test bookings; a car with a real booking stays.

## Calls first, texts after (release 37)

Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.

1. Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.
2. **Call before you text.** On a lead, a renter or a booking, **Call** is the first button and **Text** the second.
3. A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.
4. On your To do and on **Unanswered**, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.

## A lead you handle on a call (release 37)

When you answer or place a call with a lead, add a note on it, or create it from a call, the lead is yours for a limited time (15 minutes, as a Sales claim; an Admin can change it in **Settings** > **Sales**). Every call you handle adds the time again.

- Sales see **Being handled by** your first name and your function with the time, on the lead and in every list. They cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome meanwhile, and **Next lead** skips it.
- Another customer service or Fleet person can still work it; their call or note takes the hold over.
- When it ends, the lead goes back to the salesperson who had a claim on it or who brought it, else to the open list. An Admin can **Release hold** earlier.
- A booking made from the lead is credited as always: customer service and Fleet get no sales commission for it.
- Nobody who has not finished onboarding holds a lead.

## Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)

**Start the check-in (pickup)** and **Start the check-out (return)** on the booking, and **Check in** or **Check out** on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:

1. Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.
2. What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car''s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.
3. Photos are one tap each: **Take this photo** always shows the next angle.
4. What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.
5. The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example "Next: Odometer") and takes you to it. When everything is in, press **Hand over the keys** or **Complete the return**.

Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.

**Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)** is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.

## A late return is a choice (release 42)

A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows **Late return** with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:

1. **Charge as an extension**: every started day late at the booking''s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.
2. **Charge extra days**: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.
3. **Charge the late return fee**: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).
4. **Charge a custom amount**: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.
5. **Waive it**: no charge, with the reason.

Press **Save the late return charge**. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.

Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do "Late return: choose the charge". Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.

> Good to know: A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do "Late return: approve the charge" and press **Approve as asked**, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.

## Every view generated from the car''s photos (release 47)

Every car now shows nine views generated by Gemini (in the order of the sample photos: front three-quarter first, then side, rear three-quarter, front, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats, trunk), made from the car''s own photos, the sample view of the angle and the stock photo of the model, then cut out on the dealership background. A car with no listing photo of that side uses its check-in and check-out photos as references (never shown on the site). A view the check refuses three times is flagged (release 50: only views that passed are on the site). The real photos stay on the car''s record. On **Photo standard**, **Generated set** shows each car''s views made out of nine; **Redo this car now** makes them again.

## Picked up, deposit pending (release 48)
When the renter cannot place the deposit hold at the pickup (the card is declined, the bank wants a call) and the car must go, you can let it go with the deposit owed. On the job, under the deposit line, open **Let the car go with the deposit owed**, say why, and go on with the check-in. On a booking, **Record the pickup now** has the box **Deposit not taken yet: let the car go owing it, because**, and the check-in panel has **Deposit not taken: let the car go owing it**. The booking then shows **Deposit pending $X** everywhere. Each morning the renter''s saved card is tried once; if that fails, the renter gets the deposit link by text (or email). After 48 hours an Admin gets a To do. You do nothing more: once the deposit is taken the chip changes by itself.

## Studio renders (release 48)

- Every car''s first photos are studio views made from its own photos, the front three-quarter first. Its real outside photos come after them, cut out on the same background.
- Renders go live by themselves. You get "Studio photos live" in your next digest: check the colour, wheels and trim, and that the side profile faces left.
- Something is off: open the car, **Studio photos**, then **Make again** or **Take off the site**.
- To render every published car now: **Listings**, **Photo standard**, **Render every published car**.
## Evidence for every fee (release 48)

Every fee is charged only with its evidence. On a booking''s Money tab, **Evidence for every fee** lists each fee with what it needs, what was found by itself and what is missing.

1. A fee that Needs evidence has a To do in the Fleet queue (titled "Field:" when the field staff capture it) saying exactly what to take: the guided cleanliness photos and description, a damage close-up, photos of where the car was left, a receipt.
2. Press **Attach evidence** on the line, choose what it is and add the photo or PDF (or a note). It is checked again at once; the To do closes by itself.
3. After a return the car is available again at once. It goes to cleaning only when the return report says it needs cleaning (Cleaning, Heavy, Pet or Smoking), until its detail job is done. The return checklist does not complete a return that is not clean without 3 guided photos and a description. The smoking or cleaning fee it drafts waits for your review of the return, then Finance.
4. **Add a return charge**: non-return, improper return, theft recovery, a flat tire or a roadside call-out (cost plus $50; not for a mechanical fault that is not the renter''s). Add each actual cost with its receipt.

## Tracker events and pound flags (release 48)

On the **Fleet map**, below the map and the alerts. It shows once an Admin has turned Tracker events on.

**Tracker events** lists each event with its evidence: when, the car and booking, the speed and the map point, the charge and the clause, and who was told. One event per car, kind and 30 minutes. The renter and the car''s owner are told by themselves; you do not need to message them about the event itself.

- A speeding record over 180, 220 or 300 km/h carries one charge, at the highest limit reached in the event. An Admin or Finance presses **Charge**; you do not.
- Harsh driving and a speed over the alert level are a heads-up only.
- A Tracker unplugged or tampered with, or a car outside Ontario: call the renter.

**A car that leaves Ontario or Canada**: you get an alert, an email and a text at once. Call the renter. For Canada there is an urgent To do: leaving Canada needs written approval, so with no approval and no answer, tell an Admin.

**Pound flags**: a car parked at a known pound.

1. You get an urgent To do and alert. Open **Pound flags**: the lot''s phone and hours are on the row.
2. Call the lot to confirm the car is there and what releases it. Call the renter. Keep every receipt.
3. Press **Record the path** and choose: the non-return charge with the costs, the theft recovery charge with the costs (add the police report number), **Recovered, nothing to charge**, or **Not a pound**. Write what happened in a sentence.

> Tip: Not sure which charge applies? Non-return is for a car not back after the final late notice. Theft recovery is for a car stolen, or recovered by the police or a repossession. Ask an Admin when it is neither.

**Pound lots** are listed below, read only. Tell an Admin when a lot''s phone or hours are wrong, or a pound is missing.

## One look: studio renders only (release 50)

Once a car has a studio view that passed, the site shows its studio views: each car is cut out and put on the same dealership background with the CarmaCars sign, one image exactly the same for every view of every car. The views are the sample photos'' angles in the same order (front three-quarter, side, rear three-quarter, front, rear, dashboard, seats, wheel); a view the car has no photo of is made by Gemini from its other photos. Its real outside photos follow, cut out the same way. Where the home page, a hero or a sample card showed a sample car, a real car takes its place only as a cutout, never its full photo. A car with none yet shows its photos as before. Its own photos stay on the car''s record. **Photo standard** > **Studio grid** shows every car''s views side by side with **Live**, **Gate refused** or **Flagged** and why.

## Sign first, then cars

An owner''s cars move only once the owner has signed their agreement and each car''s Schedule A entry. On the owner''s page, Agreements before cars lists what is missing and who it waits on; Send reminder emails the owner with the in-app notice and the push. A fleet supplier can add cars from a list of VINs too, with each car''s tier and plate.

A confirmed booking whose pickup was never recorded shows as "Pickup not recorded, car presumed out": record the handover (or the return, or a no-show) from the booking. Until then the car takes no new offer.

## Check-in visits (release 50)

A renter on a long rental (28 days or more, a long-term weekly rental, or a rideshare driver) is asked to bring the car in about once a month. It is a suggestion, never a requirement and never a fee.

1. Open **Checks** > **Check-in visits**. **Booked** comes first, then **Due**, **Overdue** (soft: a friendly call is fine) and **Done**. You get an email and a notice when a renter picks a time, and the morning of a visit.
2. Press **Do the visit**: take the five photos (front, rear, left side, right side, odometer), type the odometer, say whether there is new damage (where and what), the tire tread in mm, whether the fluids look right and any warning light, and notes.
3. Press **Save the visit**. The reading and the tread go into the car''s maintenance, which shows the next service due. Anything to look after (a service due, tread under 3 mm, fluids, a warning light) becomes a Fleet To do; damage is logged on the Damage tab with an Admin To do.
4. **Book a time for the renter** picks an office slot for them; **Skip this month** needs the reason; **Start a visit now** is for a renter who drops by.

On the booking page, **Check-in visits** shows the next one and turns them on for any rental, off for this one, or back to the rule.


## Log an expense from the receipt

**Maintenance** > **Expenses**, on a phone or a computer.

1. Press **Take a photo** (or **Upload photos**). Add more photos of the same receipt if it is long.
2. The amount before tax, the HST, the date, the shop, the category and the car are read from the photo. Check each one; anything not read clearly is said above the fields.
3. Who pays: the car''s owner (it goes on their next statement as a cost, with the receipt in their documents, and they get an email) or CarmaCars (a company expense on the car). Tick **I paid with my own money** to be paid back.
4. Press **Save**. The expense is listed under Logged from receipts, with its photos.

## Ownership documents in bulk

**More fleet** > **Listings** > **Ownership documents**

1. Press **Choose the files** and pick every permit photo or PDF at once.
2. Each file is read for its VIN and plate and filed on the car with that VIN. A file whose plate matches a car but whose VIN does not waits below with that car chosen: check it and press **File it on this car**. The owner sees it in their portal under Documents and gets an email.
3. A file that matched no car waits under Waiting for a car: open the file, choose the car and press **File it on this car**, or set it aside with the reason. Fleet has a To do while any file waits.

## Add old photos
**Add old photos** (a tab beside **Check-in visits**: Fleet under **Checks**, customer service under its **Check-in visits** link) puts photos of an earlier check-in or check-out on its booking: every booking picked up or returned in the last 60 days (`old_photos_days`), searchable by plate, car, renter or number. Choose **Check-in** or **Check-out** and pick many photos at once; they upload in the background and resume after a bad signal. **A pile of photos** groups a pile by the time each was taken (`old_photos_group_minutes`), reads the plate where it can, and suggests the check-in or check-out within `old_photos_match_hours` of it; one tap confirms a group. The photos show on the booking''s photo report as "added later by" the person, with the time they were taken. No email or text goes to the renter or the owner, and the booking does not change.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">You keep the cars moving: field jobs, daily checks, photo reviews after returns, and the listings with their duplicate check and plate covering. There is no commission for Fleet, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.</p><p class="gd-p">Your rail: Queue, Today, Field jobs, Field hours, Daily checks, Photo reviews, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Find a renter and Scorecard.</p><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-schedule-field-jobs" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Schedule field jobs</h2><p class="gd-p">Every confirmed booking gets its handover (or delivery) and return (or pickup) jobs by itself, at the booking&#39;s times and place, and put on a shift: the shift covering its time, or that day&#39;s (see Shifts and who gets a job). The people on the shift share its jobs, least busy first. You check and change them.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Jobs, next three days: each with its place, its shift, its field staff and whether they acknowledged it. &quot;Made from the booking&quot; marks the ones made by themselves; when the booking moves, they move too, unless you changed them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Change a job with <b class="gd-ui">To a shift</b> (another shift), <b class="gd-ui">Assign</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Reassign</b> (a field person on a shift that day when the day has shifts, or an Admin), <b class="gd-ui">Move</b> (time and place) or <b class="gd-ui">Cancel</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Handovers and returns without a job (when the automatic jobs are off, or one was cancelled) are listed first: press <b class="gd-ui">Schedule</b>, the place filled in from the booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An Admin turns the automatic jobs or the assignment off in Settings &gt; Program.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/fleet</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/565"><img src="/guides/img/va-fleet-02-field-jobs-desktop-8e721230.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="565"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:17.9%;top:51.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Shifts in your Google Calendar</h3><p class="gd-p">At the bottom of <b class="gd-ui">Field jobs</b> (and on your <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>), <b class="gd-ui">Add shifts, townhalls and interviews to Google Calendar</b> gives you a private link with every field shift, 14 days back to 60 days ahead: who claimed it or Open, the tasks and a link to it, and the weekly townhall. Press <b class="gd-ui">Make my calendar link</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Add to Google Calendar</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Add</b> in Google. Google refreshes it every few hours on its own. <b class="gd-ui">Regenerate link</b> stops the old link; <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> stops it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-shifts-and-who-gets-a-job" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Shifts and who gets a job</h2><p class="gd-p">Field staff take their shifts from the schedule published by itself: every hour, up to 14 days ahead, from the shift template in Program settings (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day), only forward from the latest shift already published. A handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own (90 minutes either side). A job is given by itself only to a field person who passed the academy and holds a shift that day, and work lands only on days with shifts.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On <b class="gd-ui">Field jobs</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Shifts, next seven days</b> shows each day and how many people are on a shift, and each shift its jobs (<b class="gd-ui">Jobs on it</b>). A shift with jobs and nobody on it is marked; within 24 hours of its start you get an alert and a To do, once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Need more? Press <b class="gd-ui">Publish shifts</b>: the first day&#39;s start and end, how many people, and for how many days the same hours repeat. A shift you cancel is not published again. Field staff take them on their phones.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a person</b> puts someone on a shift and <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes them off. A person who has not passed the academy cannot take shifts or be given a job.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A shift nobody claimed keeps its jobs: field staff see them when they look for shifts to claim, and the one who claims it gets them. A shift given up or swapped takes its jobs along; a cancelled shift sends them to another shift.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Work due on a day with no shifts moves to the day before when it is known in advance, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day. The job shows its planned day and keeps the booking&#39;s real time; the renter&#39;s times never change. A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning: cover it, or move the booking time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Unassign</b> takes a job off its person and its shift; tick <b class="gd-ui">Tell them</b> only if they should know. The Admins can be given a job too (no shift needed).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-missing-check-ins-and-check-outs" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Missing check-ins and check-outs</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Missing check-in and check-out</b> on Field jobs lists every past rental without its photos and readings (odometer, fuel, damage photos), closed bookings included.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Give to field staff</b> and choose the person: they add the photos and readings from their Today page.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-fleet-map" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fleet map</h2><p class="gd-p">At the top of <b class="gd-ui">Field jobs</b>: every car on the map with its renter, booking, due-back time and state, the alerts, and the trips by booking, the same as the Admin&#39;s. Every staff member sees the cars&#39; positions: customer service, Sales and Finance open the same map from <b class="gd-ui">Find a car</b> (<b class="gd-ui">Car map</b>), read only, and field staff under <b class="gd-ui">Map</b>. Every car page and booking page shows <b class="gd-ui">Where the car is</b>: moving or parked, when it last reported and <b class="gd-ui">Open on the map</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">No tracker yet</b>. Only Admins and fleet staff press <b class="gd-ui">Seen</b> on an alert. Each owner sees where their own cars are, never the renter or the booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press a car for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery and the trip under way.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">An alert (speeding, left Ontario or the zone, still driving after the return time, low or unplugged tracker, not reporting) also comes to your bell and as an urgent phone alert. Call the renter, then press <b class="gd-ui">Seen</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car still driving after its return time: call, send the late notice and offer a paid extension, as for any late return.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-field-hours" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Field hours</h2><p class="gd-p">Field staff clock in and out on their phones. You see who is clocked in and every shift of the two-week pay period, and you fix what they cannot.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Field hours</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Clocked in now</b> lists who is on, since when. <b class="gd-ui">Earlier period</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Later period</b> move between pay periods.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Someone forgot to clock out: press <b class="gd-ui">Clock out for them</b>, set the time they finished and write the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Someone forgot to clock in, or a time is wrong: <b class="gd-ui">Add hours</b> enters a shift, <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> fixes one and <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes one out. Each needs a reason; the change is kept in a log with what it was before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Once an Admin approves the pay run of a period, its shifts are locked: ask the Admin. You see hours only, not rates or pay.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Where they clocked in</h3><p class="gd-p">The hours list shows where each person clocked in and out: a map link and the distance from the lot. A clock in or out over 500 m away, or with the location refused, is shown in bold with the reason the person wrote. Their location is asked only at those two moments, never in between.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-daily-checks" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Daily checks</h2><p class="gd-p">Twice a day: the opening check by 9:00 and the closing check by 18:00.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Daily checks</b> and choose <b class="gd-ui">Opening check</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Closing check</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each line shows what was found. Tick OK, or Problem with a note.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the opening check</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Save the closing check</b>). You can save it again.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/checks</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/820"><img src="/guides/img/va-fleet-03-daily-checks-desktop-be06d6c0.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="820"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:6.5%;top:15.4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:44.7%;top:42%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:64.2%;top:94%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-check-a-car-out-or-in" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check a car out or in</h2><p class="gd-p">Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in from the booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a confirmed booking press <b class="gd-ui">Check in (pickup)</b>; on a booking on rent, <b class="gd-ui">Check out (return)</b>. Today lists the ones due, each with its button.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The checklist field staff use opens: readings (km and fuel or charge), the photo set with the plate and the gauges, damage close-ups and both signatures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Afterwards press <b class="gd-ui">Photo report</b>: times, Late by, kilometres, fuel, photos and the return charges. Fleet waives a charge with <b class="gd-ui">Waive</b> and a reason.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-photo-reviews-after-a-return" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Photo reviews after a return</h2><p class="gd-p">After each return, the field photo set waits under <b class="gd-ui">Photo reviews</b>. Compare it with the pickup set. Press <b class="gd-ui">Review done</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Ask for a re-shoot</b> if a photo is missing or unclear.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-similar-cars" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Similar cars</h2><p class="gd-p">A possible duplicate never keeps a car off the site: it shows on the car&#39;s checklist until you decide. Only Same car takes it off.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each flag shows the car, what it looks like (same VIN, plate, photo or specs) and the other car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Compare the permit, the plate and the photos.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Not a duplicate</b> with a note when they are different cars, or <b class="gd-ui">Same car</b> when they are.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/similar-cars</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/460"><img src="/guides/img/va-fleet-06-similar-cars-desktop-562b0382.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="460"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:23.6%;top:30.4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:94.8%;top:30.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-rates-and-kilometres" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rates and kilometres</h2><p class="gd-p">From a listing, press <b class="gd-ui">The car and its rates</b>, or open the car from Field jobs and its <b class="gd-ui">Rates &amp; fees</b> tab.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type the rates an Admin set. Only the daily rate is needed; the others follow from it when empty. The weekend rate is a price per day for each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Keep <b class="gd-ui">Use the defaults</b> for the kilometres, or choose <b class="gd-ui">Custom for this car</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Check What renters pay under the fields, then press <b class="gd-ui">Save the rates</b>. Rates, kilometres and deposit save together.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Price limits</b>, below: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts, read only. Offers, promo codes and lead-time pricing stay between them; an Admin or the owner changes them, and only an Admin allows one booking outside them.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-listings-and-covering-plates" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Listings and covering plates</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>. A draft waiting shows Needs review. Open it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The copy is written by itself (change a line only if you must: it is then kept). Check the photos: on each public photo, cover the plate or mark it not visible.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/listings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/340"><img src="/guides/img/va-fleet-05-listings-desktop-d2672e0a.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="340"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:54.5%;top:49.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol" start="3"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The listing&#39;s Steps to go live says what is next: 1 Photos, 2 Cover plates, 3 Review, 4 Live on the site, each with its button. The plates are checked by themselves: a plate found is blurred (Covered automatically), a photo with none is marked No plate visible, and a photo the check is not sure of stays Plate not checked. <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> on a photo takes an automatic decision back. To cover one yourself, press <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b>: the editor opens under the photo; <b class="gd-ui">Suggest the plate</b> asks for the box. A photo filed under the wrong shot: <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> under it on the Photos card, then take the right one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Drag over a plate to draw a box; drag a box to move it, its corner to resize it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Only a plate that is there is blurred, tight to the plate with a soft edge, so no character can be read (nothing is drawn on it; a car with no front plate gets no box there), then <b class="gd-ui">Save the covered photo</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">No plate in the shot? <b class="gd-ui">No plate visible on this photo</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/776"><img src="/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-phone-95d5afd2.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="776"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:52.6%;top:78.9%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50%;top:43.8%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:61.5%;top:62.1%" aria-hidden="true">5</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:43.1%;top:92.3%" aria-hidden="true">6</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>The plate check never holds a car back: a photo whose plate is not checked stays private, and goes public by itself once it is covered or marked. The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-missing-angles-and-short-videos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Missing angles and short videos</h2><p class="gd-p">On a listing, below First photo (Sales: in the Marketplace kit of the car).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A required angle with no photo? Fleet and Sales press <b class="gd-ui">Make</b> and the angle (for example <b class="gd-ui">Make Rear</b>): the image model makes the view from the car&#39;s photos, within its free daily use. Check it is the same car, then <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Reject</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Make a short video</b> for a 9:16 video of the car&#39;s approved photos with the price and the call to action. Keep the tab in front until it says Saved, then <b class="gd-ui">Download</b> it or schedule it on your Marketing page (Scheduled posts).</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>An AI view shows on the site after the real photos, labelled AI view. It is never the cover and never damage or condition evidence. A real photo always replaces it.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-publish-now" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish now</h2><p class="gd-p">Customer service and fleet publish a car themselves; nothing has to be finished first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the car from Listings or Field jobs. Its listing says why it is not on the site yet; press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>. With no rates yet it uses the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">What is still open (paperwork, details, photos, No VIN yet for a car added by its plate, a possible duplicate) shows as warnings after Publish now and on the car. None of them stops publishing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">New cars with their rates usually go on the site by themselves (Publish new cars automatically, on by default). A car taken off the site by staff waits for Publish now.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A car not on the fleet insurance policy yet can be requested, offered and paid for, but never handed over until the insurer confirms it. Requests and offers for such a car show a warning.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-calendar-sync-with-turo-and-other-platforms" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calendar sync with Turo and other platforms</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Calendar sync</b>: a car listed on Turo or Getaround must never be booked twice.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Turo has no calendar link: Turo&#39;s trip emails come in by themselves, find their car by themselves (Turo car number, plate, VIN, year, make, model, trim, colour, what earlier emails taught) and block it with the turnaround. Nothing to set up per car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">An email the reader cannot place waits as &quot;Which car is this?&quot;: press <b class="gd-ui">Which car is this?</b> and press the right car (best guesses first). It is remembered for that car&#39;s next emails. If the dates or trip number are missing: <b class="gd-ui">Add as a Turo trip</b> (choose the car, check the dates) or <b class="gd-ui">Dismiss</b>. A trip whose email did not come: <b class="gd-ui">Add a Turo trip</b> on the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each Turo trip shows the guest&#39;s name and phone when Turo&#39;s email includes them. Contact a Turo guest only about their trip, never with promotions.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Turo cannot read our calendar: under &quot;Block on Turo&quot;, block each CarmaCars booking on the car&#39;s Turo calendar, then press <b class="gd-ui">Done on Turo</b>. Dates that changed or a booking cancelled here show the dates to free on Turo.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Getaround, Google Calendar or another platform with a calendar (iCal) link: open <b class="gd-ui">Add a calendar link</b>, choose the platform, paste it and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the link</b>. Copy the car&#39;s CarmaCars link for that platform with <b class="gd-ui">Copy</b> and paste it into the platform&#39;s calendar import.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A double booking raises an urgent task for you and an email: move, swap or cancel one trip. A link that stops working raises a task after 3 failed reads: copy it from the platform again.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Add the photos and readings</h3><p class="gd-p">A pickup or return recorded with the details later gives Fleet the task <b class="gd-ui">Add the photos and readings for CC-...</b>. Open the booking and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the check-in (or check-out) photos and readings</b>: the usual checklist opens without the ready check or the renter&#39;s signature. Take the photos, the odometer, fuel, keys (and cleanliness at a return), sign and save. The task closes by itself; it cannot be closed by hand before.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-bookings-now" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Bookings now</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Rentals</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> opens on Now for fleet and customer service: the cars out with their renter and due-back countdown, coming back today and tomorrow (overdue first, in red), going out in the next 72 hours with what is ready, the money due in 7 days and the free cars. It refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. A booking listed as <b class="gd-ui">Out (pickup not recorded)</b> left without a check-in: press <b class="gd-ui">Mark picked up</b>, then add the photos, km and fuel from the task. A car overdue or due back today has <b class="gd-ui">Returned</b> (here, on Today and at the top of the booking): give the return time (now, or earlier; lateness follows it) and the km and fuel if known. The overdue messages stop and the task for the photos is yours. The search above it finds any booking.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">The renter says the car is back</h3><p class="gd-p">An urgent To do &quot;The renter says the car is back&quot; means the renter pressed <b class="gd-ui">I&#39;ve returned the car</b> on an overdue booking. Their overdue notices are paused. Open the booking, check the car (place, tracker, the renter&#39;s photos), then press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b> (correct the odometer, fuel or time first if needed; the trip is completed) or <b class="gd-ui">Deny</b> with the reason (the renter is told and the notices start again).</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> takes the VIN from the car: <b class="gd-ui">Scan the barcode</b> in the door frame or under the windshield, or <b class="gd-ui">Photo of the VIN</b>.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> on a listing takes any number of photos at once, in any order: each is sorted to its shot. A photo that fits no shot goes in with <b class="gd-ui">Extra outside photos</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Extra inside and detail photos</b>; drag the extras into their order in the review and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the order</b>. 10 photos and one outside photo complete the listing. Outside photos are framed big on the studio floor with a shadow under the tyres; a watermark or caption at a photo&#39;s edge is cut off by itself. <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b> opens with the plate box suggested: check it and save. A car small in the frame, or no model name behind it: press <b class="gd-ui">Frame the outside photos again</b> (then check the plates again). A bad cut-out (a mirror missing, background left): press <b class="gd-ui">Edit the cut-out</b>, erase or restore with the brush, move or size the car on the studio, then <b class="gd-ui">Save as a new version</b>. The version before is kept; if the car did not move, the plate check carries over. Every photo gets a light touch-up by itself; tick <b class="gd-ui">Use original colours</b> under a photo to make it again without it. Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom: a real photographed dealership room when one is stored (the car about 70% of the width, its wheels on the floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection; no logo on a real wall), else the dark drawn showroom (the logo on the wall, the model&#39;s name behind the car on the cover). A cut-out that is not clean enough is never placed in a room: the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual), noted on the photo. A car still on the black studio: press <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to this car</b>; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to every car</b> does every car. Under a photo, <b class="gd-ui">Redo</b> makes it again and <b class="gd-ui">Back to the original</b> puts back the version before. <b class="gd-ui">Marketing photos</b> on a listing makes copies in other scenes for Marketplace and social posts (choose a scene or <b class="gd-ui">Mix: a different scene on each photo</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Make the marketing set</b>); the website&#39;s photos stay as they are. <b class="gd-ui">First photo</b> on a listing chooses what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit: <b class="gd-ui">Plain car</b>, <b class="gd-ui">With a model</b> (the image model&#39;s car-show photo, a fully clothed adult model beside the car) or <b class="gd-ui">Flyer</b> (the price a day from the live rates, the call to action and the logo on the cover). Switch any time; until the chosen one is made the plain cover shows.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-one-screen-many-photos-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">One screen, many photos (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Import photos from a Google Drive link</b> on a listing adds the photos of a public Drive folder to the car, sorted and processed like Add photos. <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Import photos from Drive</b> reads a whole folder of folders (one per make, then per car), proposes the car for each folder, and imports once you confirm the table. The page follows the import and ends with what was imported, skipped and failed, and why. The same Drive file is never added twice. Customer service can import into a car whose listing is already started; Fleet and Admin can start one.</p><p class="gd-p">Check-in and check-out are one screen on the booking page: the time, km, fuel, many photos at once (tag angles if you like) and a note. The renter&#39;s own photos join the same report; each photo shows who took it. On a car&#39;s page, record <b class="gd-ui">Pickup from owner</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Return to owner</b> with photos: the owner sees them.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-repair-costs-on-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Repair costs on a car</h2><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Kickbacks and repairs</b> lists its repair costs and the kickbacks partners paid on it. <b class="gd-ui">Add a repair cost</b>: the date, the shop or another vendor, what was done, the amount and tax, who paid (CarmaCars, the owner or the insurer), the claim and a photo or PDF of the receipt.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-when-a-check-stops-the-pickup-or-the-return-release-33" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking page, <b class="gd-ui">What stops the pickup now</b> (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press <b class="gd-ui">Ask an Admin to override the pickup</b> (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking&#39;s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: <b class="gd-ui">Ask to record a past trip</b> with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-incident-cards-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Incident cards (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Incident cards</b>, prints the card for the visor or the glovebox: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, our support and roadside numbers, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. On a car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Incident card</b> prints that car; on the list, <b class="gd-ui">Print all cars</b> prints every car, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks. Laminate it and put one in each car. The insurance policy on the card is set by an Admin; until it is, the card tells the renter to ask for the slip. No price is ever printed on it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-government-forms-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Government forms (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner&#39;s car are on the owner&#39;s page and the car&#39;s page, under <b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b>. Open a form, press <b class="gd-ui">Change a value</b>, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under <b class="gd-ui">Versions</b> with their downloads. <b class="gd-ui">Back to the records</b> undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. <b class="gd-ui">Make again</b> keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick <b class="gd-ui">Discard the values changed by hand</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b>, opens the forms&#39; mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under <b class="gd-ui">Earlier mappings</b>. Only the boxes are filled: the form&#39;s own text and layout never change.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-odometer-and-fuel-at-every-check-in-and-check-out" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Odometer and fuel at every check-in and check-out</h2><p class="gd-p">Every check-in and check-out on one screen asks for two photos besides the others:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Photo of the dashboard</b>: the odometer and the fuel gauge, from the camera roll or the camera. The site reads it and asks, for example, &quot;Odometer 45,210 km, fuel 3/4: correct?&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Yes, correct</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">No, I will type it</b> and type the odometer and pick the fuel in eighths.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Selfie in front of the car</b>: taken now with the camera, never from the camera roll. A selfie without a fresh capture time is noted on the report for you to check; it never stops the check-in.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">At the return the site compares with the pickup: km driven, km over the included allowance and the fuel difference. The extra km (the booking&#39;s rate per km) are added to the booking by themselves. The fuel is prepared as a suggested line: the car&#39;s tank x the fuel missing x the local pump price of its grade x 1.25, plus the $20 refuelling fee (an electric car: battery kWh x the charge missing x $0.40, plus the fee). You and Finance confirm it on the deposit review; no card is charged by it. The photo report shows both dashboard photos side by side with the readings and these charges.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-change-the-car-of-a-confirmed-booking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change the car of a confirmed booking</h2><p class="gd-p">A car with a problem before pickup? On the booking, press <b class="gd-ui">Change the car</b>, choose a car free for the dates and say why. The price comes from the new car&#39;s rate sheet; more to pay is left open for the renter, less becomes a refund for approval. The jobs move to the new car and the renter gets one email.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-an-accident-reported-by-a-renter" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An accident reported by a renter</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter can report an accident from the accident card on their booking. It opens the incident with its first-response steps and your To do, and sends you an urgent alert (on duty) and to Admins: what happened, where, the photos and videos, the other party, the police report number, whether anyone is hurt and whether the car can be driven. Call the renter at once; a car that cannot be driven is already out of service with its calendar blocked.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-payments-and-calls-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Payments and calls (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Fleet takes payments on a booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab: text or email a pay link, charge the saved card when the renter agreed, hold the deposit, or record cash or an e-Transfer received (within your single limit; Finance gets a To do to check it). Refunds, captures and voids stay with Finance and the Admins.</p><p class="gd-p">Calls and texts about pickups, returns, deliveries and cars on rent come to Fleet first: the caller pop-up shows them, and <b class="gd-ui">More fleet</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Calls and texts</b> is your inbox. A car late back has <b class="gd-ui">Returning now</b> on its late panel: press it when the renter says they are on the way, and they get no more overdue reminders for that return time.</p><p class="gd-p">The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner&#39;s car are on the owner&#39;s page and the car&#39;s page, under <b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b>. Open a form, press <b class="gd-ui">Change a value</b>, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under <b class="gd-ui">Versions</b> with their downloads. <b class="gd-ui">Back to the records</b> undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. <b class="gd-ui">Make again</b> keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick <b class="gd-ui">Discard the values changed by hand</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Owners</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b>, opens the forms&#39; mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under <b class="gd-ui">Earlier mappings</b>. Only the boxes are filled: the form&#39;s own text and layout never change. The owner signs each form on screen: the page shows <b class="gd-ui">Owner&#39;s signature</b> beside the form (who, when, the version) and <b class="gd-ui">Download the print-ready form</b> has no signature on it. A value changed after signing shows <b class="gd-ui">Changed since signed</b> and the owner is asked to sign again.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-close-ended-trips" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Close ended trips</h2><p class="gd-p">A back-dated close sends the renter no email or text. Fleet gets a To do when a trip is still open 2 hours after its return time, and the morning digest lists how many are open.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Field jobs</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Close ended trips</b>: tick the trips that ended and were never closed, mark them returned on time or late (with the time), choose the deposit decision (deduct the balance owed, deduct the late fee, or release in full) and press <b class="gd-ui">Close</b>. An expired card hold is settled by expiry at once. An Admin presses Release for the rest. On a booking, an expired hold after the return has <b class="gd-ui">Mark settled (released by expiry)</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-the-primary-photo-release-43" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The primary photo (release 43)</h2><p class="gd-p">The first photo of a car is always its front exterior. When a car shows the flag <b class="gd-ui">Primary photo is not exterior</b> on the Vehicles list, its best outside photo is not on the site yet: add or approve one. <b class="gd-ui">Redo photos with Gemini</b> on the car page makes every photo of the car again from its original with Gemini (the background replaced by the showroom, inside photos cleaned up and sharp, a plate blurred only where the car has one, tight to the plate) and generates the angles the car has no photo of, marked <b class="gd-ui">AI generated</b>. A photo the check refuses three times stays off the site, flagged. Fleet also has the <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b> card on Listings: each car&#39;s photos at the standard, AI angles, flagged photos and last run, with <b class="gd-ui">Redo this car now</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Redo every car</b>. The whole fleet is brought to the standard by itself every 5 minutes, newest listed cars first.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-field-applicant-calls-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Field applicant calls (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Field applicants who pass the AI interview book a 10-minute interview date in the hour before the weekly townhall. <b class="gd-ui">Field applicant calls</b> on your home page lists the six slots and who took each one.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-value-and-fuel-on-the-car-page-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Value and fuel on the car page (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; the car &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Overview</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Value and fuel</b>:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Canadian Black Book value</b> (with the date checked) or an <b class="gd-ui">Estimated value (when no Black Book)</b>: renters on credit card coverage are checked against it. With neither, they go to staff review.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Tank (litres)</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Fuel grade</b> (regular, premium or diesel; empty uses the class), or <b class="gd-ui">Battery (kWh)</b> for an electric car. Empty uses the default in Program settings.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>. Customer service sees the card; only Fleet and an Admin change it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-shifts-delivery-and-fuel-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Shifts, delivery and fuel (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The shift board shows each field person&#39;s availability, the standing weekly shifts, who is under the minimum, and for each slot the people to ask. A shift nobody claimed 48 hours ahead alerts you.</li><li>You can approve new staff at the fourth onboarding step, or reject with a reason.</li><li>Delivery is priced by distance from 1940 Eglinton Ave E; the fuel line at the return is a suggestion from the tank and the pump price for you to check on the deposit review.</li><li>An Admin can delete a car that has only test bookings; a car with a real booking stays.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-calls-first-texts-after-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls first, texts after (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call before you text.</b> On a lead, a renter or a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> is the first button and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> the second.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On your To do and on <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b>, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-a-lead-you-handle-on-a-call-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A lead you handle on a call (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">When you answer or place a call with a lead, add a note on it, or create it from a call, the lead is yours for a limited time (15 minutes, as a Sales claim; an Admin can change it in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b>). Every call you handle adds the time again.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Sales see <b class="gd-ui">Being handled by</b> your first name and your function with the time, on the lead and in every list. They cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome meanwhile, and <b class="gd-ui">Next lead</b> skips it.</li><li>Another customer service or Fleet person can still work it; their call or note takes the hold over.</li><li>When it ends, the lead goes back to the salesperson who had a claim on it or who brought it, else to the open list. An Admin can <b class="gd-ui">Release hold</b> earlier.</li><li>A booking made from the lead is credited as always: customer service and Fleet get no sales commission for it.</li><li>Nobody who has not finished onboarding holds a lead.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-check-in-and-check-out-on-one-screen-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Start the check-in (pickup)</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Start the check-out (return)</b> on the booking, and <b class="gd-ui">Check in</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Check out</b> on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car&#39;s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Photos are one tap each: <b class="gd-ui">Take this photo</b> always shows the next angle.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example &quot;Next: Odometer&quot;) and takes you to it. When everything is in, press <b class="gd-ui">Hand over the keys</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Complete the return</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)</b> is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-a-late-return-is-a-choice-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A late return is a choice (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p">A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Late return</b> with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge as an extension</b>: every started day late at the booking&#39;s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge extra days</b>: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge the late return fee</b>: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge a custom amount</b>: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Waive it</b>: no charge, with the reason.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the late return charge</b>. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.</p><p class="gd-p">Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do &quot;Late return: choose the charge&quot;. Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do &quot;Late return: approve the charge&quot; and press <b class="gd-ui">Approve as asked</b>, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-every-view-generated-from-the-car-s-photos-release-47" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Every view generated from the car&#39;s photos (release 47)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every car now shows nine views generated by Gemini (in the order of the sample photos: front three-quarter first, then side, rear three-quarter, front, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats, trunk), made from the car&#39;s own photos, the sample view of the angle and the stock photo of the model, then cut out on the dealership background. A car with no listing photo of that side uses its check-in and check-out photos as references (never shown on the site). A view the check refuses three times is flagged (release 50: only views that passed are on the site). The real photos stay on the car&#39;s record. On <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Generated set</b> shows each car&#39;s views made out of nine; <b class="gd-ui">Redo this car now</b> makes them again.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-picked-up-deposit-pending-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Picked up, deposit pending (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">When the renter cannot place the deposit hold at the pickup (the card is declined, the bank wants a call) and the car must go, you can let it go with the deposit owed. On the job, under the deposit line, open <b class="gd-ui">Let the car go with the deposit owed</b>, say why, and go on with the check-in. On a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Record the pickup now</b> has the box <b class="gd-ui">Deposit not taken yet: let the car go owing it, because</b>, and the check-in panel has <b class="gd-ui">Deposit not taken: let the car go owing it</b>. The booking then shows <b class="gd-ui">Deposit pending $X</b> everywhere. Each morning the renter&#39;s saved card is tried once; if that fails, the renter gets the deposit link by text (or email). After 48 hours an Admin gets a To do. You do nothing more: once the deposit is taken the chip changes by itself.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-studio-renders-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Studio renders (release 48)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Every car&#39;s first photos are studio views made from its own photos, the front three-quarter first. Its real outside photos come after them, cut out on the same background.</li><li>Renders go live by themselves. You get &quot;Studio photos live&quot; in your next digest: check the colour, wheels and trim, and that the side profile faces left.</li><li>Something is off: open the car, <b class="gd-ui">Studio photos</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Make again</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Take off the site</b>.</li><li>To render every published car now: <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Render every published car</b>.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-evidence-for-every-fee-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Evidence for every fee (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every fee is charged only with its evidence. On a booking&#39;s Money tab, <b class="gd-ui">Evidence for every fee</b> lists each fee with what it needs, what was found by itself and what is missing.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A fee that Needs evidence has a To do in the Fleet queue (titled &quot;Field:&quot; when the field staff capture it) saying exactly what to take: the guided cleanliness photos and description, a damage close-up, photos of where the car was left, a receipt.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Attach evidence</b> on the line, choose what it is and add the photo or PDF (or a note). It is checked again at once; the To do closes by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">After a return the car is available again at once. It goes to cleaning only when the return report says it needs cleaning (Cleaning, Heavy, Pet or Smoking), until its detail job is done. The return checklist does not complete a return that is not clean without 3 guided photos and a description. The smoking or cleaning fee it drafts waits for your review of the return, then Finance.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a return charge</b>: non-return, improper return, theft recovery, a flat tire or a roadside call-out (cost plus $50; not for a mechanical fault that is not the renter&#39;s). Add each actual cost with its receipt.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-tracker-events-and-pound-flags-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tracker events and pound flags (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">On the <b class="gd-ui">Fleet map</b>, below the map and the alerts. It shows once an Admin has turned Tracker events on.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Tracker events</b> lists each event with its evidence: when, the car and booking, the speed and the map point, the charge and the clause, and who was told. One event per car, kind and 30 minutes. The renter and the car&#39;s owner are told by themselves; you do not need to message them about the event itself.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A speeding record over 180, 220 or 300 km/h carries one charge, at the highest limit reached in the event. An Admin or Finance presses <b class="gd-ui">Charge</b>; you do not.</li><li>Harsh driving and a speed over the alert level are a heads-up only.</li><li>A Tracker unplugged or tampered with, or a car outside Ontario: call the renter.</li></ul><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">A car that leaves Ontario or Canada</b>: you get an alert, an email and a text at once. Call the renter. For Canada there is an urgent To do: leaving Canada needs written approval, so with no approval and no answer, tell an Admin.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Pound flags</b>: a car parked at a known pound.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">You get an urgent To do and alert. Open <b class="gd-ui">Pound flags</b>: the lot&#39;s phone and hours are on the row.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Call the lot to confirm the car is there and what releases it. Call the renter. Keep every receipt.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record the path</b> and choose: the non-return charge with the costs, the theft recovery charge with the costs (add the police report number), <b class="gd-ui">Recovered, nothing to charge</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Not a pound</b>. Write what happened in a sentence.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Not sure which charge applies? Non-return is for a car not back after the final late notice. Theft recovery is for a car stolen, or recovered by the police or a repossession. Ask an Admin when it is neither.</div></aside><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Pound lots</b> are listed below, read only. Tell an Admin when a lot&#39;s phone or hours are wrong, or a pound is missing.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-one-look-studio-renders-only-release-50" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">One look: studio renders only (release 50)</h2><p class="gd-p">Once a car has a studio view that passed, the site shows its studio views: each car is cut out and put on the same dealership background with the CarmaCars sign, one image exactly the same for every view of every car. The views are the sample photos&#39; angles in the same order (front three-quarter, side, rear three-quarter, front, rear, dashboard, seats, wheel); a view the car has no photo of is made by Gemini from its other photos. Its real outside photos follow, cut out the same way. Where the home page, a hero or a sample card showed a sample car, a real car takes its place only as a cutout, never its full photo. A car with none yet shows its photos as before. Its own photos stay on the car&#39;s record. <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Studio grid</b> shows every car&#39;s views side by side with <b class="gd-ui">Live</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Gate refused</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Flagged</b> and why.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-sign-first-then-cars" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sign first, then cars</h2><p class="gd-p">An owner&#39;s cars move only once the owner has signed their agreement and each car&#39;s Schedule A entry. On the owner&#39;s page, Agreements before cars lists what is missing and who it waits on; Send reminder emails the owner with the in-app notice and the push. A fleet supplier can add cars from a list of VINs too, with each car&#39;s tier and plate.</p><p class="gd-p">A confirmed booking whose pickup was never recorded shows as &quot;Pickup not recorded, car presumed out&quot;: record the handover (or the return, or a no-show) from the booking. Until then the car takes no new offer.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-check-in-visits-release-50" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check-in visits (release 50)</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter on a long rental (28 days or more, a long-term weekly rental, or a rideshare driver) is asked to bring the car in about once a month. It is a suggestion, never a requirement and never a fee.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Checks</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Check-in visits</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Booked</b> comes first, then <b class="gd-ui">Due</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Overdue</b> (soft: a friendly call is fine) and <b class="gd-ui">Done</b>. You get an email and a notice when a renter picks a time, and the morning of a visit.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Do the visit</b>: take the five photos (front, rear, left side, right side, odometer), type the odometer, say whether there is new damage (where and what), the tire tread in mm, whether the fluids look right and any warning light, and notes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the visit</b>. The reading and the tread go into the car&#39;s maintenance, which shows the next service due. Anything to look after (a service due, tread under 3 mm, fluids, a warning light) becomes a Fleet To do; damage is logged on the Damage tab with an Admin To do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Book a time for the renter</b> picks an office slot for them; <b class="gd-ui">Skip this month</b> needs the reason; <b class="gd-ui">Start a visit now</b> is for a renter who drops by.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">On the booking page, <b class="gd-ui">Check-in visits</b> shows the next one and turns them on for any rental, off for this one, or back to the rule.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-log-an-expense-from-the-receipt" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Log an expense from the receipt</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Maintenance</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Expenses</b>, on a phone or a computer.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take a photo</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Upload photos</b>). Add more photos of the same receipt if it is long.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The amount before tax, the HST, the date, the shop, the category and the car are read from the photo. Check each one; anything not read clearly is said above the fields.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Who pays: the car&#39;s owner (it goes on their next statement as a cost, with the receipt in their documents, and they get an email) or CarmaCars (a company expense on the car). Tick <b class="gd-ui">I paid with my own money</b> to be paid back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>. The expense is listed under Logged from receipts, with its photos.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-ownership-documents-in-bulk" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Ownership documents in bulk</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">More fleet</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Ownership documents</b></p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Choose the files</b> and pick every permit photo or PDF at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each file is read for its VIN and plate and filed on the car with that VIN. A file whose plate matches a car but whose VIN does not waits below with that car chosen: check it and press <b class="gd-ui">File it on this car</b>. The owner sees it in their portal under Documents and gets an email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A file that matched no car waits under Waiting for a car: open the file, choose the car and press <b class="gd-ui">File it on this car</b>, or set it aside with the reason. Fleet has a To do while any file waits.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-add-old-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add old photos</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Add old photos</b> (a tab beside <b class="gd-ui">Check-in visits</b>: Fleet under <b class="gd-ui">Checks</b>, customer service under its <b class="gd-ui">Check-in visits</b> link) puts photos of an earlier check-in or check-out on its booking: every booking picked up or returned in the last 60 days (<span class="gd-url">old_photos_days</span>), searchable by plate, car, renter or number. Choose <b class="gd-ui">Check-in</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Check-out</b> and pick many photos at once; they upload in the background and resume after a bad signal. <b class="gd-ui">A pile of photos</b> groups a pile by the time each was taken (<span class="gd-url">old_photos_group_minutes</span>), reads the plate where it can, and suggests the check-in or check-out within <span class="gd-url">old_photos_match_hours</span> of it; one tap confirms a group. The photos show on the booking&#39;s photo report as &quot;added later by&quot; the person, with the time they were taken. No email or text goes to the renter or the owner, and the booking does not change.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'academy', 'chapter', 'commissions', 'Your training path is under **Me** > **Academy**. There is a path for each of your functions: customer service, fleet, finance, Sales in person or remote, field work.

## Watch the lessons

1. Open **Academy**. Each path lists its sections in order, with Passed, Open or Pass the one before.
2. Open a section. Each lesson is a short video made by your browser: scenes with captions, read aloud by your browser''s own voice.
3. Press **Play**. **Pause**, **Back** and **Next** move through the scenes; **Replay** starts again; Speed goes from 0.75x to 1.5x. **Voice on** turns the voice off and on.
4. No sound or no English voice on your device? The lesson plays with captions only, each scene timed for reading.
5. Each section ends with a lesson called **See it**: pictures of the real screens with numbered pins, good and bad example photos side by side, flow diagrams and Do and Do not pairs. Press **Next** to go through them.

> Tip: Use headphones in the office. The voice is your browser''s, so it can sound different on another device.

## Pass the quiz

1. Under the lessons, answer every question and press **Check my answers**. Every question also has one funny wrong answer among the options: picking it is simply wrong, and the line under it says so.
2. You need 90% (the pass mark in Program settings). Passed: the next section opens. Not yet: the questions you got wrong are marked (not the right answers). **Fix the ones marked wrong**: change only those, once, and press **Check my fixes**; that check counts. Still under the mark: wait 2 minutes, then **Try again later** starts the quiz again (10 tries a day).
3. A section that is on two of your paths (the policies, for example) counts on both once passed.

> Good to know: An Admin can open a section early for you, for example when you already did this work somewhere else. The academy gate is on: each section opens once you pass the one before it. If you were hired with one-step Hire, the rest of the portal waits until you pass your academy: the full academy for customer service, Fleet and Finance, the basics for Sales (the guide, your profile and the documents to sign stay open). Each path ends with a section on what changed recently.

## Your first steps: Welcome (release 34)

Your first sign-in opens **Welcome**, your onboarding checklist, in four steps:

1. Welcome.
2. Your profile and phone: add your home address and your mobile number in your profile.
3. The academy: pass the full academy (customer service, Fleet, Finance) or the basics of the Sales path (its first sections, marked Basics).
4. Your first tasks: press **Done** on each one as you finish it.

Until then, Welcome, the academy, the guide, your profile and pay details and the documents to sign are all that opens; any other page brings you to the academy. Then **Go to your portal** opens everything.

## Quiz rules (release 35)

A quiz passes at 90%. Questions come in a random order and open after the reading time. Under the mark, you fix the questions marked wrong once before it counts as a failed try. After a failed try, wait 2 minutes; you have 10 tries a day. New sections for your role are added to your path: if you had passed everything, you keep a week before they hold you, and nothing you passed is reset.

## The renter''s side and Ask the guide first (release 48)

Customer service has the path **The renter''s side** (release 50: customer service only): one section for each step a renter takes (the request, the offer, Complete your details and signing, paying and the deposit hold, coverage proof with the pink slip and OPCF 27, pickup, the trip, the return and the deposit back, and the errors renters call about). Each step shows what the renter sees and opens that page of the renter guide (**Renter guide**, at `/staff/guide/renter`). Your own path also has a section of worked examples from your chapter of this guide: what the renter says, where you click and what you say.

1. New staff take both from the start, before their portal opens.
2. Staff already working have 7 days: the academy page says the date. After it, the rest of the portal waits until the new sections are passed. Nothing you passed is reset.
3. **Ask the guide first**: the Assistant panel names the guide chapter of the page you are on, with a link. Read it before you ask a colleague, and say which chapter you read when you do.

## The basics, the rest, and pages you get stuck on (release 50)

1. What opens your portal: customer service, Fleet and Finance pass the full academy first. Sales passes the basics, the first sections marked **Basics** on the academy page (Sales in person 6, Sales remote 5), and the portal, work and leads open.
2. The rest opens your pay: Finish every other section of your paths before held pay is paid out (commission, bonuses and referral fees, and for customer service, Fleet and Finance your pay for hours too). Nothing is lost: the first pay run after you pass pays it in full. The academy page shows "Whole academy: 12 of 30 sections", and a held pay stub says why.
3. Stuck on a page? When the Stuck? prompt opens on a page, or the page keeps failing for you, that page''s academy section is given to you. Pages of that part of the portal bring you to the section until you pass it; the academy page lists it under **Pass these to continue**, and you get an alert with the link. The section opens even when it is not on your path.
4. The academy is shorter: questions that repeated an earlier section or that the lessons did not teach are gone. **The renter''s side** is now on the customer service path only.', 'Academy', 'Your training path: lessons narrated by your browser, a quiz per section, 80% to pass.',
  'Your training path is under **Me** > **Academy**. There is a path for each of your functions: customer service, fleet, finance, Sales in person or remote, field work.

## Watch the lessons

1. Open **Academy**. Each path lists its sections in order, with Passed, Open or Pass the one before.
2. Open a section. Each lesson is a short video made by your browser: scenes with captions, read aloud by your browser''s own voice.
3. Press **Play**. **Pause**, **Back** and **Next** move through the scenes; **Replay** starts again; Speed goes from 0.75x to 1.5x. **Voice on** turns the voice off and on.
4. No sound or no English voice on your device? The lesson plays with captions only, each scene timed for reading.
5. Each section ends with a lesson called **See it**: pictures of the real screens with numbered pins, good and bad example photos side by side, flow diagrams and Do and Do not pairs. Press **Next** to go through them.

> Tip: Use headphones in the office. The voice is your browser''s, so it can sound different on another device.

## Pass the quiz

1. Under the lessons, answer every question and press **Check my answers**. Every question also has one funny wrong answer among the options: picking it is simply wrong, and the line under it says so.
2. You need 90% (the pass mark in Program settings). Passed: the next section opens. Not yet: the questions you got wrong are marked (not the right answers). **Fix the ones marked wrong**: change only those, once, and press **Check my fixes**; that check counts. Still under the mark: wait 1 minute, then **Try again** starts the quiz again (10 tries a day).
3. A section that is on two of your paths (the policies, for example) counts on both once passed.

> Good to know: An Admin can open a section early for you, for example when you already did this work somewhere else. The academy gate is on: each section opens once you pass the one before it. If you were hired with one-step Hire, the rest of the portal waits until you pass your academy: the full academy for customer service, Fleet and Finance, the basics for Sales (the guide, your profile and the documents to sign stay open). Each path ends with a section on what changed recently.

## Your first steps: Welcome (release 34)

Your first sign-in opens **Welcome**, your onboarding checklist, in four steps:

1. Welcome.
2. Your profile and phone: add your home address and your mobile number in your profile.
3. The academy: pass the full academy (customer service, Fleet, Finance) or the basics of the Sales path (its first sections, marked Basics).
4. Your first tasks: press **Done** on each one as you finish it.

Until then, Welcome, the academy, the guide, your profile and pay details and the documents to sign are all that opens; any other page brings you to the academy. Then **Go to your portal** opens everything.

## Quiz rules (release 35)

A quiz passes at 90%. Questions come in a random order and open after the reading time. Under the mark, you fix the questions marked wrong once before it counts as a failed try. After a failed fix, wait 1 minute, then press **Try again**; you have 10 tries a day. New sections for your role are added to your path: if you had passed everything, you keep a week before they hold you, and nothing you passed is reset.

## The renter''s side and Ask the guide first (release 48)

Customer service has the path **The renter''s side** (release 50: customer service only): one section for each step a renter takes (the request, the offer, Complete your details and signing, paying and the deposit hold, coverage proof with the pink slip and OPCF 27, pickup, the trip, the return and the deposit back, and the errors renters call about). Each step shows what the renter sees and opens that page of the renter guide (**Renter guide**, at `/staff/guide/renter`). Your own path also has a section of worked examples from your chapter of this guide: what the renter says, where you click and what you say.

1. New staff take both from the start, before their portal opens.
2. Staff already working have 7 days: the academy page says the date. After it, the rest of the portal waits until the new sections are passed. Nothing you passed is reset.
3. **Ask the guide first**: the Assistant panel names the guide chapter of the page you are on, with a link. Read it before you ask a colleague, and say which chapter you read when you do.

## The basics, the rest, and pages you get stuck on (release 50)

1. What opens your portal: customer service, Fleet and Finance pass the full academy first. Sales passes the basics, the first sections marked **Basics** on the academy page (Sales in person 6, Sales remote 5), and the portal, work and leads open.
2. The rest opens your pay: Finish every other section of your paths before held pay is paid out (commission, bonuses and referral fees, and for customer service, Fleet and Finance your pay for hours too). Nothing is lost: the first pay run after you pass pays it in full. The academy page shows "Whole academy: 12 of 30 sections", and a held pay stub says why.
3. Stuck on a page? When the Stuck? prompt opens on a page, or the page keeps failing for you, that page''s academy section is given to you. Pages of that part of the portal bring you to the section until you pass it; the academy page lists it under **Pass these to continue**, and you get an alert with the link. The section opens even when it is not on your path.
4. The academy is shorter: questions that repeated an earlier section or that the lessons did not teach are gone. **The renter''s side** is now on the customer service path only.

## Answer yourself (release 51)

Every question says: **Answer yourself. Using AI tools, browser agents or computer-use software on this test is not allowed and breaks your agreement; CarmaCars may take legal action.** The quiz page blocks paste and copy and notices browser automation, clicks not made by a person, a pointer that jumps, leaving the page more than twice and answers picked faster than reading allows. Any of them voids the try (it counts as a failed try) and an Admin is told.',
