i><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Sales sees customer numbers hidden, like (647) •••-••00. Use <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> on the page: the number is found on our side. Search by phone still works.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-calls-in-your-browser-release-44" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls in your browser (release 44)</h2><p class="gd-p">You make and take calls in the staff portal, in your browser, on the CarmaCars number. Your own phone number is never used and never shown, wherever you work from.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Use a computer with a headset (or earphones with a microphone) in Chrome, Edge or Safari. The first time you call, the browser asks to use the microphone: press <b class="gd-ui">Allow</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> on a lead, a renter, a booking or any staff page. The call screen opens (a card at the bottom left on a computer, the whole screen on a phone) with the person&#39;s name, the number and <b class="gd-ui">Starting the call...</b>, then the call&#39;s timer once they answer. The customer sees the CarmaCars number. Sales: the number stays hidden, the call goes through all the same.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">To call someone without opening their page, press the round green phone button at the bottom left. <b class="gd-ui">Keypad</b>: type any number and press the green button. <b class="gd-ui">Contacts</b>: the people you called last, or type a name or number to find a lead (Sales: your own leads) or a renter, then tap the person.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">During the call: <b class="gd-ui">Mute</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Keypad</b> (for a phone menu that asks you to press a number), <b class="gd-ui">Speaker</b> (choose the microphone and, where the browser allows, the speaker), <b class="gd-ui">Hold</b> and the red <b class="gd-ui">End call</b> button. <b class="gd-ui">End call</b> is always on the screen, also while the call is still starting (it then says <b class="gd-ui">Cancel</b>). Switching apps on a phone keeps the call on; closing the page ends a call that is still starting.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Incoming calls: when someone calls the CarmaCars number, your browser rings while a staff page is open (customer service and Sales by default). Press <b class="gd-ui">Answer</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b>. The first person to answer takes the call and the others stop ringing. You see the caller&#39;s name when we know it (Sales: the number hidden).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Nobody online, or nobody answers: the caller hears a short message, and it is a missed call with its task, like every missed call. A call is never forwarded to your own phone.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Keep a staff page open during your shift with the computer&#39;s sound on, so you hear the ring.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">A call that fails (the microphone not allowed, the connection lost): the call screen says what to do. Press <b class="gd-ui">Close</b>, fix it and call again.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-calls-first-texts-after-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls first, texts after (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call before you text.</b> On a lead, a renter or a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> is the first button and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> the second.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On your To do and on <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b>, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-a-lead-you-handle-on-a-call-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A lead you handle on a call (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">When you answer or place a call with a lead, add a note on it, or create it from a call, the lead is yours for a limited time (15 minutes, as a Sales claim; an Admin can change it in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b>). Every call you handle adds the time again.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Sales see <b class="gd-ui">Being handled by</b> your first name and your function with the time, on the lead and in every list. They cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome meanwhile, and <b class="gd-ui">Next lead</b> skips it.</li><li>Another customer service or Fleet person can still work it; their call or note takes the hold over.</li><li>When it ends, the lead goes back to the salesperson who had a claim on it or who brought it, else to the open list. An Admin can <b class="gd-ui">Release hold</b> earlier.</li><li>A booking made from the lead is credited as always: customer service and Fleet get no sales commission for it.</li><li>Nobody who has not finished onboarding holds a lead.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-calling-from-the-site-your-mobile-release-40" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calling from the site: your mobile (release 40)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Call</b> on a lead, a renter, a request or a booking rings your own mobile first, then connects the person. They see the CarmaCars number, never yours. Sales see the number hidden and call this way only.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The first time, with no mobile on your profile, a small window asks <b class="gd-ui">Your mobile number</b>. Type your Canadian or US mobile (10 digits, for example (647) 555-0123) and press <b class="gd-ui">Save and call</b>. No code is texted: it is saved to your profile and the call starts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Your phone rings. Answer it: you hear &quot;CarmaCars call. Connecting you now.&quot; and the person&#39;s phone rings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A call that cannot start says why in the same window, with <b class="gd-ui">Try again</b>. Calling from the site not set up: ask customer service or an Admin to call, and tell an Admin.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">To add your number as a sign-in, use <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sign-in</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Add and verify my phone number</b>. No code after a minute? Press <b class="gd-ui">Resend the code</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Save it without a code</b>: calls still ring it, but you sign in with your email until it is verified.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-your-extension-release-51" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your extension (release 51)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your Admin may give you an extension on the CarmaCars phone menu. Callers press it and the call rings your browser phone, in the portal and in the app, while you are signed in. Your extension is on your <b class="gd-ui">Profile</b>. Keep a staff page open on your shift; a call you miss is in your alerts as <b class="gd-ui">Missed call on your line</b>.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'my-team', 'chapter', 'demo-portals', null, 'My team (managers)', 'What a manager sees of the staff assigned to them.',
  'An Admin can make you a manager and assign staff to you. You then have **My team** in the menu, and in the app under Profile.

## Your team

1. Open **My team**. Each member shows their hours in the last 7 days, academy progress, pay owed (held when their academy is not passed), field jobs open and done, and when they were last on.
2. Press a name for their KPIs by week, field jobs of the last 14 days and the next 7, their hours and their last 20 actions.

> Good to know: My team is read only. You see what an Admin sees of their work, never their pay details, address or customers'' numbers. You and the member are told when they join or leave your team.',
  '<p class="gd-p">An Admin can make you a manager and assign staff to you. You then have <b class="gd-ui">My team</b> in the menu, and in the app under Profile.</p><section class="gd-task" id="my-team-your-team" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your team</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">My team</b>. Each member shows their hours in the last 7 days, academy progress, pay owed (held when their academy is not passed), field jobs open and done, and when they were last on.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press a name for their KPIs by week, field jobs of the last 14 days and the next 7, their hours and their last 20 actions.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>My team is read only. You see what an Admin sees of their work, never their pay details, address or customers&#39; numbers. You and the member are told when they join or leave your team.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'a-return', 'chapter', 'a-handover', 'The return mirrors the handover. You record the car as it comes back and compare it with the pickup.

## Take the car back

The return is one screen, like the handover.

1. **Odometer, fuel, keys and cleanliness**: the fuel starts at the level of the pickup (or the Tracker''s reading), the keys at what was handed over, the cleanliness at Standard. Check each against the car and change what differs. Type the odometer if it is not filled in.
2. **Photos**: the same shots, in the same order, as at pickup. One tap each.
3. **Damage, compared with pickup**: for new damage, tap the diagram, fill in Where and What it is, press **Add the damage** and take a close-up photo.
4. **Cleanliness evidence** (only when the car is not clean): before any cleaning, take at least 3 of the guided photos (ash, butts, burns or residue; seats; headliner; ashtray and cupholders; floor and mats; anything else), then describe it in writing: the smell, where, how strong. A short video is optional. The return cannot be completed without them, and the smoking ($300) or cleaning fee is drafted for Fleet, then Finance, to review: it is never charged without this evidence.
5. Belongings: check the seats, the trunk, the glovebox and the door pockets. Something left? Open **Belongings left in the car, or a note**.
6. **Review and sign**: the renter signs, then you. The renter is not there, or will not sign? Open **The renter is not here, or will not sign** and tick which.
7. Press **Complete the return**. The check-out time is the moment you press it: the kilometres over the allowance and the fuel or charge used are charged from it. The deposit is not given back at the return: Finance settles it once tolls and tickets have had time to come in (about 7 days), and new damage you mark keeps it held.
8. The closing copy of both rental agreements follows by itself: time and date in, kilometres in, driven and charged, fuel in, the hours late, the new damage, the return charges and the totals, countersigned with your name, emailed to the renter.

## A late return

A car that comes back late is not charged by itself. The return screen shows **Late return** with how late the car is and what each choice costs:

1. **Decide later** (already chosen): the office chooses on the booking. Nothing is charged until then.
2. **Charge as an extension**: every started day late at the daily rate.
3. **Charge extra days**: you choose the days.
4. **Charge the late return fee**: the fee of the rental terms.
5. **Charge a custom amount**, with what it is for, or **Waive it**, with the reason.

Your choice is saved when you complete the return, and the renter gets a message that says what was chosen. A custom amount above your limit, or a waiver, waits for an Admin.

> Watch out: New damage needs a close-up photo and a clear note. Finance uses your photos and notes to bill the renter, so take your time.

> Tip: If the renter already pressed I''ve returned the car, the booking shows **The renter says the car is back** with their photos and readings. Check the car in as usual: that completes the trip and settles their report.

## On one screen (release 28)

The form with photos already taken is still on the booking: the actual return time, km, fuel, photos and a note. A late return is then chosen on the booking. A renter who returned the car themselves with km, fuel and photos has already completed the trip; add photos if anything is missing.', 'A return', 'Odometer, fuel, keys, cleanliness, photos, new damage, belongings and signatures.',
