Your choice is saved when you complete the return, and the renter gets a message that says what was chosen. A custom amount above your limit, or a waiver, waits for an Admin.

> Watch out: New damage needs a close-up photo and a clear note. Finance uses your photos and notes to bill the renter, so take your time.

> Tip: If the renter already pressed I''ve returned the car, the booking shows **The renter says the car is back** with their photos and readings. Check the car in as usual: that completes the trip and settles their report.

## On one screen (release 28)

The form with photos already taken is still on the booking: the actual return time, km, fuel, photos and a note. A late return is then chosen on the booking. A renter who returned the car themselves with km, fuel and photos has already completed the trip; add photos if anything is missing.',
  '<p class="gd-p">The return mirrors the handover. You record the car as it comes back and compare it with the pickup.</p><section class="gd-task" id="a-return-take-the-car-back" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Take the car back</h2><p class="gd-p">The return is one screen, like the handover.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Odometer, fuel, keys and cleanliness</b>: the fuel starts at the level of the pickup (or the Tracker&#39;s reading), the keys at what was handed over, the cleanliness at Standard. Check each against the car and change what differs. Type the odometer if it is not filled in.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Photos</b>: the same shots, in the same order, as at pickup. One tap each.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Damage, compared with pickup</b>: for new damage, tap the diagram, fill in Where and What it is, press <b class="gd-ui">Add the damage</b> and take a close-up photo.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">After the return the car is available again at once, unless you set the cleanliness to Cleaning, Heavy, Pet or Smoking: then it waits for its detail job. <b class="gd-ui">Cleanliness evidence</b> (only when the car is not clean): before any cleaning, take at least 3 of the guided photos (ash, butts, burns or residue; seats; headliner; ashtray and cupholders; floor and mats; anything else), then describe it in writing: the smell, where, how strong. A short video is optional. The return cannot be completed without them, and the smoking ($300) or cleaning fee is drafted for Fleet, then Finance, to review: it is never charged without this evidence.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Belongings: check the seats, the trunk, the glovebox and the door pockets. Something left? Open <b class="gd-ui">Belongings left in the car, or a note</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Review and sign</b>: the renter signs, then you. The renter is not there, or will not sign? Open <b class="gd-ui">The renter is not here, or will not sign</b> and tick which.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Complete the return</b>. The check-out time is the moment you press it: the kilometres over the allowance and the fuel or charge used are charged from it. The deposit is not given back at the return: Finance settles it once tolls and tickets have had time to come in (about 7 days), and new damage you mark keeps it held.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">The closing copy of both rental agreements follows by itself: time and date in, kilometres in, driven and charged, fuel in, the hours late, the new damage, the return charges and the totals, countersigned with your name, emailed to the renter.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-return-a-late-return" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A late return</h2><p class="gd-p">A car that comes back late is not charged by itself. The return screen shows <b class="gd-ui">Late return</b> with how late the car is and what each choice costs:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Decide later</b> (already chosen): the office chooses on the booking. Nothing is charged until then.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge as an extension</b>: every started day late at the daily rate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge extra days</b>: you choose the days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge the late return fee</b>: the fee of the rental terms.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge a custom amount</b>, with what it is for, or <b class="gd-ui">Waive it</b>, with the reason.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Your choice is saved when you complete the return, and the renter gets a message that says what was chosen. A custom amount above your limit, or a waiver, waits for an Admin.</p><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>New damage needs a close-up photo and a clear note. Finance uses your photos and notes to bill the renter, so take your time.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>If the renter already pressed I&#39;ve returned the car, the booking shows <b class="gd-ui">The renter says the car is back</b> with their photos and readings. Check the car in as usual: that completes the trip and settles their report.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="a-return-on-one-screen-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">On one screen (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">The form with photos already taken is still on the booking: the actual return time, km, fuel, photos and a note. A late return is then chosen on the booking. A renter who returned the car themselves with km, fuel and photos has already completed the trip; add photos if anything is missing.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'academy', 'chapter', 'my-hours-and-pay', 'Your training path is under **Me** > **Academy**: the handover, the return, cash and signing in the field, and the rules of the trip.

1. Open **Academy** and the first open section.
2. Press **Play** on each lesson: scenes with captions, read aloud by your phone''s own voice. **Pause**, **Back**, **Next**, **Replay** and Speed work as on a video. No voice on your phone? The captions play by themselves. Each section ends with a lesson called **See it**: pictures of the real screens with numbered pins, good and bad example photos, flow diagrams and Do and Do not pairs.
3. Answer the quiz and press **Check my answers**. Every question has one funny wrong answer among the options: picking it is simply wrong. 90% passes and opens the next section. Under that, the questions you got wrong are marked: **Fix the ones marked wrong** once and press **Check my fixes**; that check counts. Until you pass the full academy, the rest of the portal waits (the guide and your profile stay open).

> Tip: Nothing is downloaded: the lessons work on mobile data and use very little of it.

## Your first steps: Welcome (release 34)

Your first sign-in opens **Welcome**: welcome, then your profile and phone, then the academy, then your first tasks (press **Done** on each). Until you pass the full academy, only Welcome, the academy, the guide, your profile and pay details and the documents to sign open; any other page brings you to the academy.

## Quiz rules (release 35)

A quiz passes at 90%, opens after the reading time, lets you fix the questions marked wrong once, waits 2 minutes after a failed try and allows 10 tries a day. You get field jobs only once you have passed and hold a shift that day.

## The renter''s side and Ask the guide first (release 48)

Customer service''s training has the path **The renter''s side** (release 50: not the field path any more): what the renter sees at each step, from the request to the deposit back, with each page of the renter guide (**Renter guide**, at `/staff/guide/renter`). Your field path also has a section of worked examples from this guide: the ready check, the original licence, cash and add-ons.

1. New staff take both from the start. Staff already working have 7 days: the academy page says the date; after it, the rest of the portal waits until they are passed.
2. **Ask the guide first**: the Assistant panel names the guide chapter of the page you are on. Read it before you call the office.

## The basics and your pay (release 50)

1. The full academy opens your portal: pass every section of the field path, and your jobs and shifts open.
2. The rest opens your pay: Finish the other sections before your pay is paid out. **My pay** says when a stub is held, and why.
3. Stuck on a page? When the Stuck? prompt opens, or a page keeps failing for you, that page''s academy section is given to you: that part of the portal waits until you pass it, and you get an alert with the link.', 'Academy', 'Your training: watch the lessons on your phone, pass each quiz.',
  'Your training path is under **Me** > **Academy**: the handover, the return, cash and signing in the field, and the rules of the trip.

1. Open **Academy** and the first open section.
2. Press **Play** on each lesson: scenes with captions, read aloud by your phone''s own voice. **Pause**, **Back**, **Next**, **Replay** and Speed work as on a video. No voice on your phone? The captions play by themselves. Each section ends with a lesson called **See it**: pictures of the real screens with numbered pins, good and bad example photos, flow diagrams and Do and Do not pairs.
3. Answer the quiz and press **Check my answers**. Every question has one funny wrong answer among the options: picking it is simply wrong. 90% passes and opens the next section. Under that, the questions you got wrong are marked: **Fix the ones marked wrong** once and press **Check my fixes**; that check counts. Until you pass the full academy, the rest of the portal waits (the guide and your profile stay open).

> Tip: Nothing is downloaded: the lessons work on mobile data and use very little of it.

## Your first steps: Welcome (release 34)

Your first sign-in opens **Welcome**: welcome, then your profile and phone, then the academy, then your first tasks (press **Done** on each). Until you pass the full academy, only Welcome, the academy, the guide, your profile and pay details and the documents to sign open; any other page brings you to the academy.

## Quiz rules (release 35)

A quiz passes at 90%, opens after the reading time, lets you fix the questions marked wrong once, waits 1 minute after a failed fix and allows 10 tries a day. You get field jobs only once you have passed and hold a shift that day.

## The renter''s side and Ask the guide first (release 48)

Customer service''s training has the path **The renter''s side** (release 50: not the field path any more): what the renter sees at each step, from the request to the deposit back, with each page of the renter guide (**Renter guide**, at `/staff/guide/renter`). Your field path also has a section of worked examples from this guide: the ready check, the original licence, cash and add-ons.

1. New staff take both from the start. Staff already working have 7 days: the academy page says the date; after it, the rest of the portal waits until they are passed.
2. **Ask the guide first**: the Assistant panel names the guide chapter of the page you are on. Read it before you call the office.

## The basics and your pay (release 50)

1. The full academy opens your portal: pass every section of the field path, and your jobs and shifts open.
2. The rest opens your pay: Finish the other sections before your pay is paid out. **My pay** says when a stub is held, and why.
3. Stuck on a page? When the Stuck? prompt opens, or a page keeps failing for you, that page''s academy section is given to you: that part of the portal waits until you pass it, and you get an alert with the link.

## Answer yourself (release 51)

Every question says: **Answer yourself. Using AI tools, browser agents or computer-use software on this test is not allowed and breaks your agreement; CarmaCars may take legal action.** The quiz page blocks paste and copy and notices browser automation, clicks not made by a person, a pointer that jumps, leaving the page more than twice and answers picked faster than reading allows. Any of them voids the try (it counts as a failed try) and an Admin is told.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Your training path is under <b class="gd-ui">Me</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Academy</b>: the handover, the return, cash and signing in the field, and the rules of the trip.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Academy</b> and the first open section.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Play</b> on each lesson: scenes with captions, read aloud by your phone&#39;s own voice. <b class="gd-ui">Pause</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Back</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Next</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Replay</b> and Speed work as on a video. No voice on your phone? The captions play by themselves. Each section ends with a lesson called <b class="gd-ui">See it</b>: pictures of the real screens with numbered pins, good and bad example photos, flow diagrams and Do and Do not pairs.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Answer the quiz and press <b class="gd-ui">Check my answers</b>. Every question has one funny wrong answer among the options: picking it is simply wrong. 90% passes and opens the next section. Under that, the questions you got wrong are marked: <b class="gd-ui">Fix the ones marked wrong</b> once and press <b class="gd-ui">Check my fixes</b>; that check counts. Until you pass the full academy, the rest of the portal waits (the guide and your profile stay open).</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Nothing is downloaded: the lessons work on mobile data and use very little of it.</div></aside><section class="gd-task" id="academy-your-first-steps-welcome-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your first steps: Welcome (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your first sign-in opens <b class="gd-ui">Welcome</b>: welcome, then your profile and phone, then the academy, then your first tasks (press <b class="gd-ui">Done</b> on each). Until you pass the full academy, only Welcome, the academy, the guide, your profile and pay details and the documents to sign open; any other page brings you to the academy.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-quiz-rules-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Quiz rules (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">A quiz passes at 90%, opens after the reading time, lets you fix the questions marked wrong once, waits 1 minute after a failed fix and allows 10 tries a day. You get field jobs only once you have passed and hold a shift that day.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-the-renter-s-side-and-ask-the-guide-first-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The renter&#39;s side and Ask the guide first (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">Customer service&#39;s training has the path <b class="gd-ui">The renter&#39;s side</b> (release 50: not the field path any more): what the renter sees at each step, from the request to the deposit back, with each page of the renter guide (<b class="gd-ui">Renter guide</b>, at <span class="gd-url">/staff/guide/renter</span>). Your field path also has a section of worked examples from this guide: the ready check, the original licence, cash and add-ons.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">New staff take both from the start. Staff already working have 7 days: the academy page says the date; after it, the rest of the portal waits until they are passed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Ask the guide first</b>: the Assistant panel names the guide chapter of the page you are on. Read it before you call the office.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-the-basics-and-your-pay-release-50" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The basics and your pay (release 50)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The full academy opens your portal: pass every section of the field path, and your jobs and shifts open.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The rest opens your pay: Finish the other sections before your pay is paid out. <b class="gd-ui">My pay</b> says when a stub is held, and why.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Stuck on a page? When the Stuck? prompt opens, or a page keeps failing for you, that page&#39;s academy section is given to you: that part of the portal waits until you pass it, and you get an alert with the link.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-answer-yourself-release-51" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Answer yourself (release 51)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every question says: <b class="gd-ui">Answer yourself. Using AI tools, browser agents or computer-use software on this test is not allowed and breaks your agreement; CarmaCars may take legal action.</b> The quiz page blocks paste and copy and notices browser automation, clicks not made by a person, a pointer that jumps, leaving the page more than twice and answers picked faster than reading allows. Any of them voids the try (it counts as a failed try) and an Admin is told.</p></section>');
